IAL\tPROFESSIONAL_TRANSLATOR\nsrc/translations/mondo-jp-preprocessed.babelon.tsv:23062:http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/mondo.owl\thttp://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/mondo/releases/2026-03-03/mondo.owl\ten\tja\tMONDO:0957993\trdfs:label\tprogressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial dna deletions, autosomal recessive 6\tミトコンドリアDNA欠失を伴う進行性外眼筋麻痺, 常染色体潜性6\thttps://dbcls.rois.ac.jp/index-en.html\tEXACT\tOFFICIAL\tPROFESSIONAL_TRANSLATOR\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.obo:448:name: progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.obo:452:synonym: \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mtDNA deletions\" EXACT [OMIMPS:157640]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.obo:455:is_a: MONDO:0005181 ! progressive external ophthalmoplegia\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.obo:497:def: \"Auriculo-condylar syndrome (ACS) presents with bilateral external ear malformations ('question mark' ears), mandibular condyle hypoplasia, microstomia, micrognathia, microglossia and facial asymmetry. Additional manifestations include hypotonia, ptosis, cleft palate, puffy cheeks, developmental delay, impaired hearing and respiratory distress.\" [Orphanet:137888]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.obo:19745:def: \"A type of defective gonadal development in patients with a wide spectrum of chromosomal mosaic variants. Their karyotypes are of partial sex chromosome monosomy resulting from an absence or an abnormal second sex chromosome (X or Y). Karyotypes include 45,X/46,xx; 45,X/46,xx/47,xxx; 46,xxp-; 45,X/46,xy; 45,X/47,xyy; 46,xypi; etc. The spectrum of phenotypes may range from phenotypic female to phenotypic male including variations in gonads and internal and external genitalia, depending on the ratio in each gonad of 45,X primordial germ cells to those with normal 46,xx or 46,xy constitution.\" [MESH:D006060]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.obo:32813:def: \"A rare condition characterized by the unequivocal presence of both testicular and ovarian tissues in an individual. It is usually manifested with ambiguous external genitalia.\" [NCIT:C85207]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.obo:32884:name: external ear disorder\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.obo:32885:def: \"A disease involving the external ear.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6601-2165]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.obo:32887:synonym: \"disease of external ear\" EXACT [MONDO:patterns/location_top]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.obo:32888:synonym: \"disease or disorder of external ear\" EXACT []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.obo:32889:synonym: \"disorder of external ear\" EXACT [MONDO:patterns/location_top]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.obo:32890:synonym: \"external ear disease\" EXACT [DOID:379, MONDO:patterns/location]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.obo:32891:synonym: \"external ear disease or disorder\" EXACT [MONDO:design_pattern, MONDO:patterns/location]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.obo:32892:synonym: \"external ear disorder\" EXACT [NCIT:C26972]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.obo:32910:property_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/external_ear_disease\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.obo:35941:name: external ear basal cell carcinoma\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.obo:35942:def: \"A basal cell carcinoma that arises from the skin of the external ear.\" [NCIT:C6082]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.obo:35945:synonym: \"basal cell carcinoma of external Ear\" EXACT [NCIT:C6082]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.obo:35946:synonym: \"basal cell carcinoma of the external Ear\" EXACT [DOID:4287, NCIT:C6082]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.obo:35947:synonym: \"basal cell carcinoma of the external ear\" EXACT [DOID:4287, NCIT:C6082]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.obo:35948:synonym: \"basal cell external ear carcinoma\" EXACT [MONDO:patterns/location]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.obo:35949:synonym: \"external Ear basal cell carcinoma\" EXACT [DOID:4287, 