ks/mondo_mappings_exact_source_with_matches.tsv:6218:MONDO:0021200\tobsolete rare disease\tskos:exactMatch\tNCIT:C4873\tRare Disorder\tsemapv:UnspecifiedMatching\t0.95\tMONDO:MONDO\t\t\t\t\t\t\nsrc/scripts/notebooks/mondo_mappings_exact_source_with_matches.tsv:6239:MONDO:0021235\texternal ear neoplasm\tskos:exactMatch\tNCIT:C4652\tExternal Ear Neoplasm\tsemapv:UnspecifiedMatching\t0.95\tMONDO:MONDO\t\t\t\t\t\t\nsrc/scripts/notebooks/mondo_mappings_exact_source_with_matches.tsv:6340:MONDO:0021402\tpolyp of external auditory canal\tskos:exactMatch\tNCIT:C4366\tExternal Ear Polyp\tsemapv:UnspecifiedMatching\t0.95\tMONDO:MONDO\t\t\t\t\t\t\nsrc/scripts/notebooks/MondoSubsetOverlaps.ipynb:63:    \"# Get all rare disease CURIES\\n\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:3716:      \"lbl\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:3722:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mtDNA deletions\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:3805:          \"val\" : \"Auriculo-condylar syndrome (ACS) presents with bilateral external ear malformations ('question mark' ears), mandibular condyle hypoplasia, microstomia, micrognathia, microglossia and facial asymmetry. Additional manifestations include hypotonia, ptosis, cleft palate, puffy cheeks, developmental delay, impaired hearing and respiratory distress.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:49375:          \"val\" : \"A type of defective gonadal development in patients with a wide spectrum of chromosomal mosaic variants. Their karyotypes are of partial sex chromosome monosomy resulting from an absence or an abnormal second sex chromosome (X or Y). Karyotypes include 45,X/46,xx; 45,X/46,xx/47,xxx; 46,xxp-; 45,X/46,xy; 45,X/47,xyy; 46,xypi; etc. The spectrum of phenotypes may range from phenotypic female to phenotypic male including variations in gonads and internal and external genitalia, depending on the ratio in each gonad of 45,X primordial germ cells to those with normal 46,xx or 46,xy constitution.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:82463:          \"val\" : \"A rare condition characterized by the unequivocal presence of both testicular and ovarian tissues in an individual. It is usually manifested with ambiguous external genitalia.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:82617:      \"lbl\" : \"external ear disorder\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:82621:          \"val\" : \"A disease involving the external ear.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:82627:          \"val\" : \"disease of external ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:82631:          \"val\" : \"disease or disorder of external ear\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:82634:          \"val\" : \"disorder of external ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:82638:          \"val\" : \"external ear disease\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:82642:          \"val\" : \"external ear disease or disorder\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:82646:          \"val\" : \"external ear disorder\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:82692:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/external_ear_disease\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:90376:      \"lbl\" : \"external ear basal cell carcinoma\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:90380:          \"val\" : \"A basal cell carcinoma that arises from the skin of the external ear.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:90386:          \"val\" : \"basal cell carcinoma of external Ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:90390:          \"val\" : \"basal cell carcinoma of the external Ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:90394:          \"val\" : \"basal cell carcinoma of the external ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:90398:          \"val\" : \"basal cell external ear carcinoma\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:90402:          \"val\" : \"external Ear basal cell carcinoma\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:90406:          \"val\" : \"external ear skin basal cell carcinoma\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:90410:          \"val\" : \"skin basal cell carcinoma of external ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:90426:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/external_ear_basal_cell_carcinoma\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:90443:      \"lbl\" : \"external ear carcinoma\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:90447:          \"val\" : \"A carcinoma that arises from epithelial cells of the external ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:90452:          \"val\" : \"carcinoma of external Ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:90456:          \"val\" : \"carcinoma of external ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:90460:          \"val\" : \"carcinoma of the external Ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:90464:          \"val\" : \"carcinoma of the external ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:90468:          \"val\" : \"external Ear carcinoma\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:90472:          \"val\" : \"external ear carcinoma\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:90486:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/external_ear_carcinoma\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:104844:          \"val\" : \"A malignant neoplasm that affects the ear. Representative examples include ceruminous adenocarcinoma and squamous cell carcinoma of the external ear and adenocarcinoma of the middle ear.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:113435:      \"lbl\" : \"external ear squamous cell carcinoma\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:113439:          \"val\" : \"A squamous cell carcinoma that arises from the skin of the external ear.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:113445:          \"val\" : \"epidermoid carcinoma of external Ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:113449:          \"val\" : \"epidermoid carcinoma of the external Ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:113453:          \"val\" : \"epidermoid carcinoma of the external ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:113457:          \"val\" : \"external Ear epidermoid carcinoma\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:113461:          \"val\" : \"external Ear squamous cell carcinoma\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:113465:          \"val\" : \"external ear squamous cell carcinoma\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:113469:          \"val\" : \"squamous cell carcinoma of external Ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:113473:          \"val\" : \"squamous cell carcinoma of the external Ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:113489:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/external_ear_squamous_cell_carcinoma\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:116314:      \"lbl\" : \"external ear cancer\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:116318:          \"val\" : \"A malignant neoplasm involving the external ear.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:116323:          \"val\" : \"cancer of external ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:116327:          \"val\" : \"external ear cancer\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:116331:          \"val\" : \"malignant external Ear neoplasm\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:116335:          \"val\" : \"malignant external Ear tumor\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:116340:          \"val\" : \"malignant external Ear tumour\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:116343:          \"val\" : \"malignant external ear neoplasm\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:116347:          \"val\" : \"malignant neoplasm of external Ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:116351:          \"val\" : \"malignant neoplasm of external ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:116355:          \"val\" : \"malignant neoplasm of the external Ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:116359:          \"val\" : \"malignant neoplasm of the external ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:116363:          \"val\" : \"malignant tumor of external Ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:116367:          \"val\" : \"malignant tumor of the external Ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:116372:          \"val\" : \"malignant tumour of external Ear\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:116376:          \"val\" : \"malignant tumour of the external Ear\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:130601:          \"val\" : \"An infiltrating adenocarcinoma derived from ceruminous glands in the external auditory canal.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:146100:          \"val\" : \"Diseases of the ninth cranial (glossopharyngeal) nerve or its nuclei in the medulla. The nerve may be injured by diseases affecting the lower brain stem, floor of the posterior fossa, jugular foramen, or the nerve's extracranial course. Clinical manifestations include loss of sensation from the pharynx, decreased salivation, and syncope. Glossopharyngeal neuralgia refers to a condition that features recurrent unilateral sharp pain in the tongue, angle of the jaw, external auditory meatus and throat that may be associated with syncope. Episodes may be triggered by cough, sneeze, swallowing, or pressure on the tragus of the ear. (Adams et al., Principles of Neurology, 6th ed, p1390)\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:185224:      \"lbl\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:185234:          \"val\" : \"chronic progressive external ophthalmoplegia [ambiguous]\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:185237:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:185241:          \"val\" : \"chronic progressive external ophthalmoplegia\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:185272:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/chronic_progressive_external_ophthalmoplegia\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:203562:          \"val\" : \"A sexually transmitted papillary growth caused by the human papillomavirus. It usually arises in the skin and mucous membranes of the perianal region and external genitalia.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:252546:          \"val\" : \"Overproduction of parathyroid hormone in response to influence external to the parathyroid glands.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:252624:          \"val\" : \"A condition with a clinical picture similar to that of Parkinson disease, but which is caused by external factors, including medication.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:262361:          \"val\" : \"Distal arthrogryposis type 5 is an inherited developmental defect syndrome characterized by multiple congenital contractures of limbs, without primary neurologic and/or muscle disease that affects limb function, and ocular anomalies (ptosis, external ophtalmoplegia and/or strabismus). Intelligence is normal.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:263172:      \"lbl\" : \"atresia of external auditory canal and conductive deafness\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:263178:          \"val\" : \"atresia of external auditory canal and conductive deafness\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:263192:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/atresia_of_external_auditory_canal_and_conductive_deafness\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:263832:          \"val\" : \"Spinocerebellar ataxia type 3 (SCA3), also known as Machado-Joseph disease, is the most common subtype of type 1 autosomal dominant cerebellar ataxia (ADCA type 1), a neurodegenerative disorder, and is characterized by ataxia, external progressive ophthalmoplegia, and other neurological manifestations.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:273172:          \"val\" : \"Autosomal dominant popliteal pterygium syndrome (AD-PPS) is a rare genetic malformative disorder characterized by cleft lip, with or without cleft palate, contractures of the lower extremities, abnormal external genitalia, syndactyly of fingers and/or toes, and a pyramidal skin fold over the hallux nail.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:278432:          \"val\" : \"Gorham-Stout disease (GSD) is a rare disease of massive osteolysis associated with proliferation and dilation of lymphatic vessels. GSD may affect any bone in the body and can be monostotic or polyostotic. Symptoms at presentation are dependent upon the location(s) of the disease; the most common symptom is localized pain. The disease may be discovered after a pathological fracture.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:278927:          \"val\" : \"Deafness-ear malformation-facial palsy syndrome is characterized by profound conductive deafness due to stapedial abnormalities associated with variable malformations of the external ears and facial paralysis. It has been described in three sibs and their mother. Inheritance is autosomal dominant.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:287315:      \"lbl\" : \"external auditory canal atresia-vertical talus-hypertelorism syndrome\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:287332:          \"val\" : \"external auditory canal, bilateral atresia of, with congenital vertical talus\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:287335:          \"val\" : \"inherited congenital bilateral atresia of the external auditory canal, congenital bilateral vertical talus and increased interocular distance\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:287351:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/external_auditory_canal_atresia_vertical_talus_hypertelorism_syndrome\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:287354:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/external_auditory_canal_bilateral_atresia_of_with_congenital_vertical_talus\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:293353:          \"val\" : \"Oculoauriculovertebral spectrum (OAVS) with radial defects is a rare branchial arches and limb primordia development disorder characterized by variable degrees of uni- or bilateral craniofacial malformation and radial defects that result in extremely variable phenotypic manifestations. Characteristic features include low postnatal weight, short stature, vertebral defects, hearing loss, and facial dysmorphism (incl. facial asymmetry, external, middle, and inner ear malformations, orofacial clefts, and mandibular hypoplasia). These features are invariably associated with radial defects, such as preaxial polydactyly, thumb and/or radius hypoplasia/agenesis, or triphalangeal thumb. Cardiac, pulmonary, renal, and central nervous system involvement has also been reported.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:299024:          \"val\" : \"radial ray defects, hearing impairment, external ophthalmoplegia, and thrombocytopenia\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:299040:          \"val\" : \"radial Ray defects, hearing impairment, external ophthalmoplegia, and thrombocytopenia\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:299097:          \"val\" : \"Johnson neuroectodermal syndrome is characterized by alopecia, anosmia or hyposmia, conductive deafness with malformed ears and microtia and/or atresia of the external auditory canal, and hypogonadotropic hypogonadism.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:305786:          \"val\" : \"Nager syndrome, also called Nager acrofacial dysostosis (NAFD) is a congenital malformation syndrome characterized by mandibulofacial dystosis (malar hypoplasia, micrognathia, external ear malformations) and variable preaxial limb defects.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:309045:      \"lbl\" : \"autosomal dominant progressive external ophthalmoplegia\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:309049:          \"val\" : \"Autosomal dominant form of progressive external ophthalmoplegia.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:309059:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant type 1\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:309063:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia, autosomal dominant\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:309072:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant 1\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:309088:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/progressive_external_ophthalmoplegia_with_mitochondrial_dna_deletions_autosomal_dominant_1\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:309933:          \"val\" : \"A condition that affects the skin, hair, mucosa (areas ofthe body that are lined with mucus), gums (gingiva), eyes, nose and lungs. Symptoms typically begin in infancy and may include development of cataracts (clouding of the eye lens); blindness; hair loss (alopecia); abnormal changes to the perineum (the area between the anus and external genitalia); and small, skin-colored bumps (keratosis pilaris). Terminal lung disease has also been reported. The cause of HMD is thought to be an abnormality in desmosomes and gap junctions, which are structures involved in cell-to-cell contact. HMD typically follows autosomal dominant inheritance, but has occurred sporadically (in an individual who has no family history of the condition). Treatment typically focuses on individual symptoms of the condition.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:329273:          \"val\" : \"Radio-renal syndrome is a rare developmental defect during embryogenesis characterized by variable upper limb reduction defects and renal anomalies. Patients typically present absence/hypoplasia of digits, radii and/or ulnae, short stature and mild external ear malformation, as well as kidney agenesis or ectopia. There have been no further descriptions in the literature since 1983.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:330626:          \"val\" : \"Autosomal dominant Robinow syndrome (DRS) is the more common type of Robinow syndrome (RS) characterized by mild to moderate limb shortening and abnormalities of the head, face and external genitalia.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:346681:          \"val\" : \"microcephaly, IUGR, hypertelorism, ptosis, iris coloboma, hooked nose, external ear dysplasia, psychomotor retardation\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:347333:          \"val\" : \"Ablepharon macrostomia syndrome is an extremely rare multiple congenital malformation syndrome characterized by the association of ablepharon, macrostomia, abnormal external ears, syndactyly of the hands and feet, skin findings (such as dry and coarse skin or redundant folds of skin), absent or sparse hair, genital malformations and developmental delay (in 2/3 of cases). Other reported manifestations include malar hypoplasia, absent or hypoplastic nipples, umbilical abnormalities and growth retardation. It is a mainly sporadic disorder, although a few familial cases having been reported, and it displays significant clinical overlap with Fraser syndrome.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:348845:          \"val\" : \"Acrocraniofacial dysostosis is a very rare form of acrofacial dyosotosis, reported in two sisters to date, characterized by short stature, acrocephaly, ocular hypertelorism, ptosis of eyelids, ocular proptosis, downslanting palpebral fissures, high nasal bridge, anteverted nostrils, short philtrum, cleft palate, micrognathia, abnormal external ears, preauricular pits, mixed hearing loss, bulbous digits, metatarsus varus, pectus excavatum and various radiological abnormalities. Features of this syndrome were reported to overlap with otopalatodigital syndrome types 1 and 2. There have been no further descriptions in the literature since 1988.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:349950:          \"val\" : \"A type of arthrogryposis characterized by congenital cleft palate, microcephaly, craniostenosis and arthrogryposis (limitation of extension of elbows, flexed adducted thumbs, camptodactyly and clubfeet). Additional features include facial dysmorphism (\\\"myopathic\\\" stiff face, antimongoloid slanting, external ophthalmoplegia, telecanthus, low-set large malrotated ears, open mouth, mierogenia and high arched palate). Velopharyngeal insufficiency with difficulties in swallowing, increased secretion of the nose and throat, prominent occiput, generalized muscular hypotonia with mild cyanosis and no spontaneous movements, seizures, torticollis, areflexia, intellectual disability, hypertrichosis of the lower extremities, and scleredema (in the first days of life) are also observed. The disease often leads to early death. Transmission is autosomal recessive. No new cases of adducted thumbs-arthrogryposis, Christian type have been described since 1983.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:363911:          \"val\" : \"Cereballar ataxia - ectodermal dysplasia is a very rare disease, characterized by hypodontia and sparse hair in combination with cerebellar ataxia and normal intelligence. Imaging demonstrates a cerebellar atrophy.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:367468:          \"val\" : \"Verloove Vanhorick-Brubakk syndrome is a multiple congenital anomalies/dysmorphic syndrome characterized by multiple skeletal malformations (short femora and humeri, bilateral absence of metatarsal and metacarpal bone in hands and feet, bilateral partial syndactyly of fingers and toes or oligopolysyndactyly, deformed lumbosacral spine), congenital heart disease (truncus arteriosus), lung and urogenital malformations (bilateral bilobar lungs, horseshoe kidney, cryptorchidism), and facial malformations (bilateral cleft lip and palate, micrognathia, small, low-set ears without external meatus). It is lethal in the neonatal period. There have been no further descriptions in the literature since 1981.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:373239:      \"lbl\" : \"conductive deafness-malformed external ear syndrome\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:373249:          \"val\" : \"conductive hearing loss-malformed external ear syndrome\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:373257:          \"val\" : \"conductive deafness - malformed external ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:373261:          \"val\" : \"conductive deafness with malformed external ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:373269:          \"val\" : \"deafness, conductive, with malformed external EAR\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:373290:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/deafness_conductive_with_malformed_external_ear\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:373314:          \"val\" : \"Conductive deafness-ptosis-skeletal anomalies syndrome is a rare, genetic ectodermal dysplasia syndrome characterized by conductive hearing loss due to atresia of the external auditory canal and the middle ear complicated by chronic infection, ptosis and skeletal anomalies (internal rotation of hips, dislocation of the radial heads and fifth finger clinodactyly). In addition, a thin, pinched nose, delayed hair growth and dysplastic teeth are associated. There have been no further descriptions in the literature since 1978.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:417013:      \"lbl\" : \"congenital multicore myopathy with external ophthalmoplegia\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:417029:          \"val\" : \"minicore myopathy with external ophthalmoplegia\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:417035:          \"val\" : \"multicore myopathy with external ophthalmoplegia\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:417039:          \"val\" : \"multiminicore disease with external ophthalmoplegia\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:417042:          \"val\" : \"multiminicore myopathy multicore myopathy with external ophthalmoplegia\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:417064:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/congenital_multicore_myopathy_with_external_ophthalmoplegia\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:422243:      \"lbl\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal recessive 1\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:422247:          \"val\" : \"Any autosomal recessive progressive external ophthalmoplegia in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the POLG gene.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:422253:          \"val\" : \"POLG autosomal recessive progressive external ophthalmoplegia\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:422257:          \"val\" : \"autosomal recessive progressive external ophthalmoplegia caused by mutation in POLG\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:422261:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal recessive 1\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:422265:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal recessive type 1\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:422278:          \"val\" : \"autosomal recessive progressive external ophthalmoplegia\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:422282:          \"val\" : \"cerebellar ataxia infantile with progressive external ophthalmoplegia\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:422286:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with cerebellar ataxia infantile\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:422290:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia, autosomal recessive 1\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:422305:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/progressive_external_ophthalmoplegia_with_mitochondrial_dna_deletions_autosomal_recessive_1\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:422308:          \"val\" : \"https://rarediseases.info.nih.gov/diseases/1191/progressive-external-ophthalmoplegia-autosomal-recessive-1\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:423302:          \"val\" : \"A rare, genetic intellectual disability syndrome characterized by macrocephaly, hypotonia, dysmorphic facial features (wide forehead, ptosis, downslanting palpebral fissures, enlarged and calcified external ears, large jaw), sparse body hair, tall stature, and intellectual disability. Hearing loss, insulin-resistant diabetes, and progressive distal muscle wasting (leading to joint contractures) have also been reported in adulthood. Rare manifestations include behavioral abnormalities (aggression and restlessness), hypothyroidism, cerebral calcification, ataxia, and peripheral neuropathy.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:434859:          \"val\" : \"Ulbright-Hodes syndrome is characterized by renal dysplasia, growth retardation, phocomelia or mesomelia, radiohumeral fusion, rib abnormalities, anomalies of the external genitalia and a potter-like facies. The syndrome has been described in three infants (one pair of sibs and an unrelated case), all of whom died shortly after birth from respiratory distress resulting from pulmonary hypoplasia and oligohydramnios caused by renal dysplasia. The mode of transmission appears to be autosomal recessive.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:436957:          \"val\" : \"Autosomal recessive Robinow syndrome (RRS) is the less common type of Robinow syndrome (RS) characterized by short-limb dwarfism, costovertebral segmentation defects and abnormalities of the head, face and external genitalia.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:441591:          \"val\" : \"Spondylocostal dysostosis-anal and genitourinary malformations syndrome is characterized by the association of spondylocostal dysostosis with anal and genitourinary malformations (anal atresia and agenesis of external and internal genitalia). To date, only four cases have been described in the literature. Autosomal recessive inheritance has been suggested.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:448850:          \"val\" : \"visceral myopathy-familial external ophthalmoplegia syndrome\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:448854:          \"val\" : \"familial visceral myopathy with external ophthalmoplegia\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:448858:          \"val\" : \"intestinal pseudoobstruction with external ophthalmoplegia\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:448864:          \"val\" : \"visceral myopathy - familial external ophthalmoplegia\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:448868:          \"val\" : \"visceral myopathy, familial, with external ophthalmoplegia\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:448890:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/visceral_myopathy_familial_with_external_ophthalmoplegia\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:486696:          \"val\" : \"A rare neurodevelopmental disorder in the ciliopathy group that is lethal in males and characterized by variable anomalies including external malformations (craniofacial and digital), and possible involvement of the central nervous system (CNS) and of viscera (kidneys, pancreas and ovaries) in females.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:488865:          \"val\" : \"progressive basal ganglion dysfunction, mental and growth retardation, external ophthalmoplegia, postnatal microcephaly and deafness\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:491115:          \"val\" : \"46,XY complete gonadal dysgenesis (46,XY CGD) is a disorder of sex development (DSD) associated with anomalies in gonadal development that result in the presence of female external and internal genitalia despite the 46,XY karyotype.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:492136:          \"val\" : \"Kearns-Sayre syndrome (KSS) is a mitochondrial disease characterized by progressive external ophthalmoplegia (PEO), pigmentary retinitis and an onset before the age of 20 years. Common additional features include deafness, cerebellar ataxia and heart block.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:492173:          \"val\" : \"chronic progressive external ophthalmoplegia with myopathy\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:492189:          \"val\" : \"ophthalmoplegia, progressive external, with ragged red fibers\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:492194:          \"val\" : \"ophthalmoplegia, progressive external, with ragged red fibres\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:492197:          \"val\" : \"ophthalmoplegia, progressive external, with ragged-Red fibers\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:492201:          \"val\" : \"ophthalmoplegia, progressive external, with ragged-Red fibres\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:492703:          \"val\" : \"Lethal infantile mitochondrial myopathy is a rare mitochondrial oxidative phosphorylation disorder characterized by progressive generalized hypotonia, progressive external ophthalmoplegia and severe lactic acidosis, which results in early fatality (days to months after birth). Patients may present with lethargy and areflexia and may associate additional features, such as cardiomyopathy, renal dysfunction, liver involvement and seizures.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:493972:          \"val\" : \"Chondrodysplasia - disorder of sex development is an extremely rare disorder of sex development, reported in only two siblings (one terminated in pregnancy) to date, characterized by the clinical features of 46,XY complete gonadal dysgenesis (normal external female genitalia, lack of pubertal development, primary amenorrhea, and hypergonadotrophic hypogonadism) in association with severe dwarfism with generalized chondrodysplasia (bell-shaped thorax, micromelia, brachydactyly). Other reported features in the live sibling included eye anomalies (hypoplastic irides, myopia, coloboma of optic disks), dysmorphic features (deep-set eyes, upslanting palpebral fissures, puffy eyelids, large ears and mouth, mild prognathism), muscular hypoplasia, mild intellectual deficiency and severe microcephaly with cerebellar vermis hypoplasia. An autosomal recessive inheritance has been suggested.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:498478:          \"val\" : \"Waters-West syndrome is characterized by the association of lethal non-spherocytic, non-immune hemolytic anemia with abnormalities of the external genitalia (micropenis and hypospadias), flat occiput, dimpled earlobes, deep plantar creases, and increased space between the first and second toes. It has been described only once in two brothers who died a few hours after birth. The second-born infant had massive ascites and hepatosplenomegaly. The mother had two spontaneous abortions (at 6 and 12 weeks gestation) but gave birth to a normal girl, suggesting an autosomal or X-linked recessive mode of inheritance. Although the parents were not known to be consanguineous, they shared a French-Canadian and American Indian ethnic origin.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:499351:          \"val\" : \"Loose anagen syndrome is a rare benign hair disorder affecting predominantly blond females in childhood and characterized by the presence of hair that can be easily and painlessly pulled out. Most of the hair is in the anagen phase and lacks an external epithelial sheath. Hair grows back quickly and the condition improves spontaneously with aging. Loose anagen hair can be associated with other anomalies, such as coloboma.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:500175:          \"val\" : \"A congenital malformation of the external ear, seen more frequently in males, that occurs sporadically or is inherited, that is characterized by unilateral (79-93% of cases, 60% of which involve the right ear) or bilateral small and abnormally shaped auricles and that is often associated with atresia or stenosis of the ear canal, attention deficit disorders and delayed language development. The variation in auricle size ranges from grade I, where the auricle is simply smaller than normal, to grade IV, also known as anotia, where there is a complete absence of the external ear and of the auditory canal.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:509683:          \"val\" : \"A rare, congenital malformation syndrome characterized by the association of anterior ocular chamber cleavage disorder with developmental delay, short stature and congenital hypothyroidism. Additional manifestations include cerebellar hypoplasia, tracheal stenosis, narrow external auditory meatus, and hip dislocation. There have been no further description in the literature since 1995.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:523688:          \"val\" : \"Limb-mammary syndrome (LMS) is a rare disease belonging to the group of ectodermal dysplasias.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:550472:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia and scoliosis\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:550484:          \"val\" : \"ophthalmoplegia, progressive external, and scoliosis\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:558062:          \"val\" : \"anophthalmia clinical with micrognathia malformed ears digital anomalies and abnormal external genitalia\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:558066:          \"val\" : \"anophthalmia, clinical, with micrognathia, malformed ears, digital anomalies, and abnormal external genitalia\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:574161:      \"lbl\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant 2\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:574165:          \"val\" : \"Any progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the SLC25A4 gene.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:574171:          \"val\" : \"SLC25A4 progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:574175:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions caused by mutation in SLC25A4\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:574179:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant 2\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:574183:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant type 2\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:574192:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia, autosomal dominant 2\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:574209:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/progressive_external_ophthalmoplegia_with_mitochondrial_dna_deletions_autosomal_dominant_2\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:574380:      \"lbl\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant 3\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:574384:          \"val\" : \"Any progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the TWNK gene.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:574390:          \"val\" : \"TWNK progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:574394:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions caused by mutation in TWNK\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:574398:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant 3\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:574402:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant type 3\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:574411:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia, autosomal dominant 3\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:574428:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/progressive_external_ophthalmoplegia_with_mitochondrial_dna_deletions_autosomal_dominant_3\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:578212:          \"val\" : \"external ophthalmoplegia with synergistic divergence\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:578215:          \"val\" : \"external ophthalmoplegia, synergistic divergence, jaw winking, and oculocutaneous hypopigmentation\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:583601:      \"lbl\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant 4\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:583605:          \"val\" : \"Any progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the POLG2 gene.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:583611:          \"val\" : \"POLG2 progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:583615:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions caused by mutation in POLG2\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:583619:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant 4\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:583623:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant type 4\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:583632:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia, autosomal dominant 4\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:583649:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/progressive_external_ophthalmoplegia_with_mitochondrial_dna_deletions_autosomal_dominant_4\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:605449:          \"val\" : \"Oculoauricular syndrome, Schorderet type is a rare, genetic developmental defect during embryogenesis characterized by various ophthalmic anomalies (including congenital microphthalmia, microcornea, cataract, anterior segment dysgenesis, ocular coloboma and early onset rod-cone dystrophy), and abnormal external ears (low-set pinna with crumpled helix, narrow intertragic incisure, abnormal bridge connecting the crus of the helix and the anthelix, narrow external acoustic meatus, and lobule aplasia).\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:605467:          \"val\" : \"microphthalmia, microcornea, anterior segment dysgenesis, cataract, ocular coloboma, retinal pigment epithelium abnormalities, Rod-cone dystrophy, and anomalies of the external Ear\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:622169:      \"lbl\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant 5\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:622173:          \"val\" : \"Any progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the RRM2B gene.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:622179:          \"val\" : \"RRM2B progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:622183:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions caused by mutation in RRM2B\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:622187:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant 5\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:622191:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant type 5\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:622200:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia, autosomal dominant 5\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:622217:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/progressive_external_ophthalmoplegia_with_mitochondrial_dna_deletions_autosomal_dominant_5\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:639676:          \"val\" : \"A rare, genetic, developmental defect during embryogenesis disorder characterized by severe, early-onset, salt-wasting adrenal insufficiency and ambiguous/female external genitalia (irrespective of chromosomal sex) due to mutations in the <i>CYP11A1</i> gene. Milder cases may present delayed onset of adrenal gland dysfunction and genitalia phenotype may range from normal male to female in individuals with 46,XY karyotype. Imaging studies reveal hypoplastic/absent adrenal glands and biochemical findings include low serum cortisol, mineralocorticoids, androgens, and sodium, with elevated potassium levels.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:677105:          \"val\" : \"Progressive external ophthalmoplegia-myopathy-emaciation syndrome is a rare mitochondrial oxidative phosphorylation disorder due to nuclear DNA anomalies characterized by progressive external ophthalmoplegia without diplopia, cerebellar atrophy, proximal skeletal muscle weakness with generalized muscle wasting, profound emaciation, respiratory failure, spinal deformity and facial muscle weakness (manifesting with ptosis, dysphonia, dysphagia and nasal speech). Intellectual disability, gastrointestinal symptoms (e.g. nausea, abdominal fullness, and loss of appetite), dilated cardiomyopathy and renal colic have also been reported.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:677144:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia-myopathy-emaciation syndrome\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:678407:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant type 6\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:678416:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant 6\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:678420:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia, autosomal dominant 6\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:678437:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/progressive_external_ophthalmoplegia_with_mitochondrial_dna_deletions_autosomal_dominant_6_2\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:688750:          \"val\" : \"Syndromic microphthalmia-12 is a rare disease characterized by bilateral small eyeballs (microphthalmia), lungs that are too small (pulmonary hypoplasia), and a defect or hole in the diaphragm that allows the abdominal contents to move into the chest cavity (diaphragmatic hernia). Other symptoms may include: Severe global developmental delay with progressive motor impairment due to spasticity and/or uncontrolled repetitive muscular contractions (dystonia), with or without abnormal quick movements that resemble dancing (chorea), Defects of the cerebellum (Chiari type I malformation) Accumulation of cerebrospinal fluid inside the brain (hydrocephaly), Severe feeding difficulties, Mild facial dysmorphism with broad nasal root and tip, and a very small chin (micrognathia), Severe language delay, Wheelchair-bound. Syndromic microphthalmia-12 is caused by mutations in the RARB gene. There is no specific treatment for this syndrome.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:715748:      \"lbl\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal recessive 2\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:715752:          \"val\" : \"Any progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the RNASEH1 gene.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:715758:          \"val\" : \"RNASEH1 progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:715762:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions caused by mutation in RNASEH1\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:715766:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal recessive 2\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:715770:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal recessive type 2\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:715779:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia, autosomal recessive 2\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:715794:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/progressive_external_ophthalmoplegia_with_mitochondrial_dna_deletions_autosomal_recessive_2\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:719704:          \"val\" : \"Autosomal dominant optic atrophy plus syndrome (ADOA plus) is a variant of autosomal dominant optic atrophy (ADOA) associating the typical optic atrophy with other extra-ocular manifestations such as sensorineural deafness, myopathy, chronic progressive external ophthalmoplegia, ataxia and peripheral neuropathy. More rarely, other manifestations have been associated with this condition, such as spastic paraplegia, multiple-sclerosis like illness.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:729902:      \"lbl\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal recessive 3\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:729906:          \"val\" : \"Any autosomal recessive progressive external ophthalmoplegia in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the TK2 gene.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:729917:          \"val\" : \"TK2 autosomal recessive progressive external ophthalmoplegia\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:729921:          \"val\" : \"autosomal recessive progressive external ophthalmoplegia caused by mutation in TK2\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:729925:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal recessive 3\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:729929:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal recessive 3; PEOB3\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:729932:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal recessive type 3\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:729936:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia, autosomal recessive 3\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:729951:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/progressive_external_ophthalmoplegia_with_mitochondrial_dna_deletions_autosomal_recessive_3\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:729968:      \"lbl\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal recessive 4\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:729972:          \"val\" : \"An extremely rare multiple mitochondrial DNA deletion syndrome with markedly decreased deoxyguanosine kinase (DGUOK) activity in skeletal muscle characterized by a highly variable phenotype. Clinical manifestations include progressive external ophthalmoplegia, mitochondrial myopathy, recurrent rhabdomyolysis, lower motor neuron disease, mild cognitive impairment, sensory axonal neuropathy, optic atrophy, ataxia, hypogonadism and/or parkinsonism.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:729991:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal recessive 4\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:729995:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal recessive type 4\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:729999:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia, autosomal recessive 4\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:730018:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/progressive_external_ophthalmoplegia_with_mitochondrial_dna_deletions_autosomal_recessive_4\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:744003:          \"val\" : \"Arachnodactyly-intellectual disability-dysmorphism syndrome is characterized by moderate intellectual deficit, brachycephaly, typical facies (thin lips and microstomia), ectomorphic habitus with extremely long, thin fingers and toes, and hypoplastic external genitalia. It has been described in three patients.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:744096:          \"val\" : \"Arrhinia is an extremely rare, major congenital malformation consisting of an absence of the nose ranging from hyporrhinia (absence of external nasal structures) to total arrhinia (absence of external nose, nasal airways, olfactory bulbs, or olfactory nerve) often causing respiratory distress and requiring surgical correction. Arrhinia can be bilateral or unilateral (hemiarrhinia). Associated anomalies include ocular features (hypertelorism, microphthalmia, eyelid coloboma), facial clefts, midline defects and microtia.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:747029:          \"val\" : \"Maternally inherited cardiomyopathy and hearing loss is a mitochondrial disease described in two unrelated families to date that has a heterogeneous clinical presentation characterized by the association of progressive sensorineural hearing loss with hypertrophic cardiomyopathy and, in the majority of cases, encephalomyopathy symptoms such as ataxia, slurred speech, progressive external opthalmoparesis (PEO), muscle weakness, myalgia, and exercise intolerance.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:751409:          \"val\" : \"Proboscis lateralis (PL) is a rare congenital facial abnormality characterized by failed development of the external nose on one side that is replaced by a tubular structure composed of skin and soft tissue usually attached at the inner canthus of the eye and therefore often associated with maldevelopment of the nasal cavity or paranasal sinuses of the affected side. PL is also associated with other craniofacial abnormalities such as orbital anomalies, cleft lip/palate, frontal encephalocele and holoprosencephaly.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:759532:          \"val\" : \"Isolated congenital auditory ossicle malformation is a rare, congential, middle ear anomaly characterized by, usually unilateral and sporadic, variations in the number, size and/or configuration of the ossicles, with no tympanic membrane and external ear abnormalities and no history of trauma or infection. Patients frequently present late, after schooling has started, with non- progressive, conductive hearing loss often associated with speech delay and poor school performance.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:759538:          \"val\" : \"congenital auditory ossicle malformation without external ear abnormality\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:770510:          \"val\" : \"Complete septate uterus is a rare, non-syndromic uterovaginal malformation characterized by a uterus that has a longitudinal septum which elongates from the uterine fundus to the internal or external cervical os. Most often women are asymptomatic, however dysmenorrhoea, unilateral obstruction, and endometriosis could be observed. Unlike urinary tract abnormalities, which are very rarely associated, poor reproductive outcome is frequent.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:773063:          \"val\" : \"Axial mesodermal dysplasia spectrum is a rare developmental defect during embryogenesis syndrome characterized by congenital manifestations of both oculo-auriculo-vertebral spectrum and caudal regression sequence. Phenotype is highly variable but patients typically present facial dysmorphism (incl. asymmetry, hypertelorism), auricular abnormalities (e.g. preauricular tags, microtia, absence of middle ear ossicles), skeletal malformations (hemivertebrae, hip dislocation, sacral agenesis/dysplasia, talipes equinovarus, flexion deformity of lower limbs), cardiac defects (dextrocardia, septal defects), renal and genitourinary anomalies (such as renal agensis/dysplasia, abnormal external genitalia, cryptorchidia), as well as anal anomalies such as anal atresia and rectovesical fistula.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:781529:          \"val\" : \"OPCA with macular Degeneration and external ophthalmoplegia\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:783059:          \"val\" : \"Pulmonary fibrosis - hepatic hyperplasia - bone marrow hypoplasia, also named Btrimorphic syndromeB (i.e. three (inherited) morbidities, pulmonary, hepatic and cytopenia), is a rare disease reported in 4 cases to date, manifesting with idiopathic pulmonary fibrosis, hepatic nodular regenerative hyperplasia leading to portal hypertension and thrombocytopenia due to bone marrow hypoplasia. The condition was associated with 100% mortality.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:786962:          \"val\" : \"A rare, genetically highly heterogeneous otorhinolaryngologic disease, resulting from inner and/or middle ear or hearing nerve anomalies, typically characterized by bilateral, severe to profound hearing loss (mean sensorineural hearing impairment of 60 dB or more for 500-, 1,000-, and 2,000-Hz frequency tones in the better ear) which occurs before the onset of speech development and is not associated with visible external ear abnormalities or any other medical problems. It is usually nonprogressive and impedes oral language acquisition.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:787007:          \"val\" : \"Postlingual non-syndromic genetic deafness is a rare, genetically highly heterogeneous otorhinolaryngologic disease, resulting from inner and/or middle ear or hearing nerve anomalies, typically characterized by progressive, bilateral, moderate to profound hearing loss (mean sensorineural hearing impairment equal to 40 dB or more for 500-, 1,000-, and 2,000-Hz frequency tones in the better ear) which occurs after the onset of speech development and is not associated with visible external ear abnormalities or any other medical problems. Language development is not initially significantly delayed.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:787049:          \"val\" : \"A central nervous system malformation syndrome characterized by holoprosencephaly with microcephaly, abnormal eye morphology (hypotelorism, cyclopia, exophthalmos), nasal anomalies (single nostril or absent nose), and cleft lip/palate, combined with signs of caudal regression (sacral agenesis, sirenomelia with absent external genitalia).\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:793663:          \"val\" : \"Isotretinoin embryopathy is an association of malformations caused by the teratogenic effect of isotretinoin, an oral synthetic vitamin A derivative, which is used to treat severe recalcitrant cystic acne. Exposure to isotretinoin during the first trimester of pregnancy has been associated with an increased risk of spontaneous abortions and severe birth defects including serious craniofacial (microcephaly, asymmetric crying facies, microphthalmia, developmental abnormalities of the external ear, ocular hypertelorism), cardio vascular (conotruncal heart defects, aortic arch abnormalities), and central nervous system (hydrocephalus, microcephaly, lissencephaly, Dandy-Walker malformation, cognitive deficit) anomalies and thymic aplasia. Isoretinoin is contraindicated during pregnancy.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:809085:          \"val\" : \"Mitochondrial DNA depletion syndrome, encephalomyopathic form is a group of mitochondrial DNA maintenance syndrome diseases characterized by predominantly neuromuscular manifestations with typically infantile onset of hypotonia, lactic acidosis, psychomotor delay, progressive hyperkinetic-dystonic movement disorders, external ophtalmoplegia, sensosineural hearing loss, generalized seizures and variable renal tubular dysfunction. It may be associated with a broad range of other clinical features.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:809345:          \"val\" : \"A rare, mitochondrial DNA maintenance syndrome characterized by cerebellar ataxia, sensory peripheral neuropathy, myoclonus, epilepsy, progressive cognitive impairment, late-onset ptosis and external ophthalmoplegia. Liver failure may also occur, most often in association with the use of antiepileptic drug sodium valproate.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:809399:      \"lbl\" : \"autosomal recessive progressive external ophthalmoplegia\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:809403:          \"val\" : \"Autosomal recessive form of progressive external ophthalmoplegia.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:809413:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia, autosomal recessive\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:809429:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/autosomal_recessive_progressive_external_ophthalmoplegia\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:823856:          \"val\" : \"Machado-Joseph disease type 2 is a subtype of Machado-Joseph disease (SCA3/MJD) with intermediate severity characterized by an intermediate age of onset, cerebellar ataxia and external progressive ophthalmoplegia, with variable pyramidal and extrapyramidal signs.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:829063:          \"val\" : \"Infantile glycerol kinase deficiency (GKD) is a severe form of GKD characterized clinically by poor feeding, failure to thrive, salt-wasting dehydration, vomiting, Addisonian pigmentation, hypotonia, and disorders of consciousness. Some patients have complex GKD associated with adrenal hypoplasia congenita and/or Duchenne muscular dystrophy (DMD) with manifestations including intellectual deficit, dysmorphic facial features, abnormal external genitalia, strabismus, seizures, and progressive lethargy.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:830939:          \"val\" : \"Inherited isolated adrenal insufficiency due to partial CYP11A1 deficiency is a rare, genetic, chronic, primary adrenal insufficiency disorder, due to partial loss-of-function CYP11A1 mutations, characterized by early-onset adrenal insufficiency without associated abnormal external male genitalia. Patients present with signs of adrenal crisis, including electrolite abnormalities, severe weakness, recurrent vomiting and seizures. Ultrasound reveals absent (or very small) adrenal glands.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:833644:          \"val\" : \"A rare disease caused by compression of the celiac axis by an abnormally shaped arcuate ligament (the part of the diaphragm in which both pillars join in the midline around the aorta). Patients have recurrent abdominal pain, anorexia and weight loss. The pain is epigastric, and diarrhea or constipation may be present as well. Onset of pain will usually, although not always, be after food intake, and may be associated with nausea and emesis. Other symptoms may include lassitude, exercise intolerance and vomiting. Occasionally, a patient may show an abdominal murmur upon auscultation.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:840082:          \"val\" : \"A syndrome characterized by the association of gastrointestinal dysmotility, peripheral neuropathy, chronic progressive external ophthalmoplegia and leukoencephalopathy.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:840192:          \"val\" : \"Conditions affecting individuals with 46,XX karyotype characterized by atypical development of one or more of the following: the gonads, the internal reproductive structures, the external reproductive/genital structures.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:849088:          \"val\" : \"A rare multiple congenital anomalies syndrome characterized by mild to severe intellectual disability, a distinctive facial gestalt (blepharophimosis, maxillary hypoplasia, telecanthus, microtia and atresia of the external auditory meatus) as well as skeletal and articular abnormalities (e.g. camptodactyly of the fingers, cutaneous syndactyly, talipes equinovarus, flexion contractures of the proximal interphalangeal joints, hip or elbow subluxation, joint laxity). Affected individuals also present neonatal hypotonia, variable respiratory manifestations, chronic feeding difficulties and gray matter heterotopia.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:850280:          \"val\" : \"The salt wasting form of classic congenital adrenal hyperplasia due to 21-hydroxylase deficiency (classical 21 OHD CAH) is characterized by virilization of the external genitalia in females, hypocortisolism, precocious pseudopuberty and renal salt loss due to aldosterone deficiency.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:850315:          \"val\" : \"The simple virilizing form of classical congenital adrenal hyperplasia due to 21-hydroxylase deficiency (classical 21 OHD CAH) is characterized by genital ambiguity and virilization of the external genitalia in females, hypocortisolism and precocious pseudopuberty without salt-wasting.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:857105:      \"lbl\" : \"adult-onset chronic progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial myopathy\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:857109:          \"val\" : \"Adult-onset chronic progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial myopathy is a rare mitochondrial disease characterized by adult onset of progressive external ophthalmoplegia, exercise intolerance, muscle weakness, manifestations of spinocerebellar ataxia (e.g. impaired gait, dysarthria) and mild motor peripheral neuropathy. Respiratory insufficiency has been reported in some cases.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:867228:      \"lbl\" : \"childhood-onset autosomal recessive myopathy with external ophthalmoplegia\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:867232:          \"val\" : \"A rare, genetic, non-dystrophic myopathy disease characterized by childhood-onset severe external ophthalmoplegia, typically without ptosis, associated with mild, very slowly progressive muscular weakness and atrophy, involving the facial, neck flexor and limb (upper > lower, proximal > distal) muscles. Muscle biopsy shows type 1 fiber uniformity, absent, or abnormally small, type 2A fibers, increased variability of fiber size, internalized nuclei and/or fatty infiltration.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:867250:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/childhood_onset_autosomal_recessive_myopathy_with_external_ophthalmoplegia\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:902565:      \"lbl\" : \"maternally-inherited progressive external ophthalmoplegia\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:902575:          \"val\" : \"maternally-inherited chronic progressive external ophthalmoplegia\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:902588:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/mitochondrial_dna_related_progressive_external_ophthalmoplegia\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:904291:        \"comments\" : [ \"Note that the ordo class is specifically for rare diseases, but we broaden to be inclusive of HH1\" ],\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:909535:          \"val\" : \"Androgen insensitivity syndrome (AIS) is a disorder of sex development (DSD) characterized by the presence of female external genitalia, ambiguous genitalia or variable defects in virilization in a 46,XY individual with absent or partial responsiveness to age-appropriate levels of androgens. It comprises two clinical subgroups: complete AIS (CAIS) and partial AIS (PAIS).\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:909668:          \"val\" : \"A condition in males that affects sexual development. It is characterized by underdevelopment of the Leydig cells, which are cells in the testes that secrete male sex hormones (androgens) and are important for male sexual development. Individuals with LCH have a typical male genetic make-up (46, XY), but due to lowered levels of androgens, may have a range of genital (reproductive organ) differences. Individuals with LCH may have a small penis (micropenis),the opening of the urethra may be located on the underside of the penis (hypospadias), or the scrotum may be divided into two halves (bifid scrotum). Given these differences in development, the external genitalia may not appear clearly male or female (ambiguous genitalia). Some individuals with LCH can have female external genitalia and small testes that have not descended and are located in the pelvis, abdomen, or groin. This may be referred to as type 1, whereas less severe cases might be called type 2. LCH is inherited in an autosomal recessive manner and is caused by mutations in the LHCGR gene.Although there is no specific treatment or cure for LCH, there may be ways to manage the symptoms. A team of doctors or specialists is often needed to figure out the treatment options for each person.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:911242:          \"val\" : \"The association of auricular abnormalities and cleft lip with or without cleft palate has been described in two siblings. One sibling had postauricular pits, profound myopia, nystagmus and retinal pigment abnormalities. The second sibling was a fetus (gestational age: 23 weeks) with severe cleft lip, cleft palate and external ear abnormalities.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:912364:          \"val\" : \"A rare genetic neuromuscular disease characterized by early onset of proximal or generalized muscle weakness, external ophthalmoplegia with or without ptosis, and joint contractures. Hypotonia, neonatal respiratory distress necessitating ventilation, and severe dysphagia have also been reported. The disease is of variable severity and non- or slowly progressive. Patients typically remain ambulatory. Muscle biopsy may show predominance of type 1 fibers, marked variability in fiber size, increased internal nuclei, and proliferation of perimysial and endomysial connective tissue.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:913160:          \"val\" : \"Bickerstaff's brainstem encephalitis (BBE) is a rare post-infectious neurological disease characterized by the association of external ophthalmoplegia, ataxia, lower limb arreflexia, extensor plantar response and disturbance of consciousness (drowsiness, stupor or coma).\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:922258:      \"lbl\" : \"macrostomia-preauricular tags-external ophthalmoplegia syndrome\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:922262:          \"val\" : \"Macrostomia-preauricular tags-external ophthalmoplegia syndrome combines macrostomia or abnormal mouth contour, preauricular tags, uni- or bilateral ptosis and external ophthalmoplegia. It was described in nine members of a Brazilian family. It is a new phenotype belonging to the so-called oculoauriculovertebral spectrum, resulting from a branchial arch anomaly. Transmission is autosomal dominant.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:922277:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/macrostomia_preauricular_tags_external_ophthalmoplegia_syndrome\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:922313:          \"val\" : \"perineal hemangioma-external genitalia malformations-lipomyelomeningocele-vesicorenal abnormalities-imperforate anus syndrome\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:941245:          \"val\" : \"A congenital malformation of the external ear and the most extreme form of microtia characterized by the complete absence of the external ear and auditory canal, conductive hearing loss, attention deficit disorders and delayed language development.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:950600:          \"val\" : \"Robinow syndrome (RS) is a rare genetic syndrome characterized by limb shortening and abnormalities of the head, face and external genitalia.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:976412:      \"lbl\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal recessive 5\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:976423:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal recessive 5\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:976427:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia, autosomal recessive 5\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:976443:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/progressive_external_ophthalmoplegia_with_mitochondrial_dna_deletions_autosomal_recessive_5\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:977914:          \"val\" : \"Hemochromatosis type 1 (classic) is the most common form of hereditary hemochromatosis (HH), a group of diseases characterized by excessive tissue iron deposition. Due to its incidence (1/200-1/1000), it is not considered as a rare disease, unlike the other subforms of the disease\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:979060:          \"val\" : \"Complete androgen insensitivity syndrome (CAIS) is a form of androgen insensitivity syndrome (AIS), a disorder of sex development (DSD), characterized by the presence of female external genitalia in a 46,XY individual with normal testis development but undescended testes and unresponsiveness to age-appropriate levels of androgens.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:986104:          \"val\" : \"Damage inflicted on the body as the direct or indirect result of an external force, with or without disruption of structural continuity.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:988839:      \"lbl\" : \"external ear neoplasm\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:988843:          \"val\" : \"A neoplasm (disease) that involves the external ear.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:988848:          \"val\" : \"external Ear tumor\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:988853:          \"val\" : \"external Ear tumour\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:988856:          \"val\" : \"external ear neoplasm (disease)\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:988860:          \"val\" : \"external ear tumor\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:988865:          \"val\" : \"external ear tumour\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:988868:          \"val\" : \"neoplasm of external Ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:988872:          \"val\" : \"neoplasm of external ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:988876:          \"val\" : \"neoplasm of the external Ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:988880:          \"val\" : \"tumor of external Ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:988884:          \"val\" : \"tumor of external ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:988888:          \"val\" : \"tumor of the external Ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:988893:          \"val\" : \"tumour of external Ear\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:988897:          \"val\" : \"tumour of external ear\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:988901:          \"val\" : \"tumour of the external Ear\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:1003260:          \"val\" : \"A viral or bacterial infection that affects the external, middle, or inner ear. It may follow an upper respiratory infection. Signs and symptoms include pain, ear discharge, ear fullness, hearing loss, vertigo, nausea, and vomiting.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:1021220:      \"lbl\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant 1\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:1021224:          \"val\" : \"Any autosomal dominant progressive external ophthalmoplegia in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the POLG gene.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:1021235:          \"val\" : \"POLG autosomal dominant progressive external ophthalmoplegia\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:1021239:          \"val\" : \"autosomal dominant progressive external ophthalmoplegia caused by mutation in POLG\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:1021243:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant 1\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:1021247:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia, autosomal dominant 1\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:1070618:          \"val\" : \"Choanal atresia-athelia-hypothyroidism-delayed puberty-short stature syndrome is an autosomal dominant disorder characterized by choanal atresia, athelia or hypoplastic nipples, branchial sinus abnormalities, neck pits, lacrimal duct anomalies, hearing loss, external ear malformations, and thyroid abnormalities.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:1083138:          \"val\" : \"Penetrating and non-penetrating injuries to the spinal cord resulting from traumatic external forces (e.g., WOUNDS, GUNSHOT; WHIPLASH INJURIES; etc.).\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:1088859:      \"lbl\" : \"X-linked external auditory canal atresia-dilated internal auditory canal-facial dysmorphism syndrome\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:1109408:          \"val\" : \"46,XX testicular disorder of sex development (46,XX testicular DSD) is characterized by male external genitalia, ranging from normal to ambiguous with associated testosterone deficiency.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:1122636:          \"val\" : \"An anterior midline defect with variable expression involving the infraumbilical abdominal wall including the pelvis, urinary tract, and external genitalia.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:1128016:          \"val\" : \"A rare disease due to a severely impaired central autonomic control of breathing and dysfunction of the autonomous nervous system. The incidence is estimated to be at 1 of 200 000 livebirths. A heterozygous mutation of PHOX-2B gene is found in 90% of the patients. Association with a Hirschsprung's disease is observed in 16% of the cases. Despite a high mortality rate and a lifelong dependence to mechanical ventilation, the long-term outcome of CCHS should be ultimately improved by multidisciplinary and coordinated follow-up of the patients.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:1138604:          \"val\" : \"A myopathy that is characterized by muscle breakdown (rhabdomyolysis), heat and exertion-related muscle pain (myalgia) and cramping symptoms, severe muscle pain, sudden elevation and subsequent fall of serum creatine phosphokinase levels and products of muscle breakdown in the urine (myoglobinuria). Associated with RYR1 variations. Rhabdomyolysis is associated with a range of external triggers, including strenuous exercise beyond the limit of fatigue, heat stress, illicit drug or alcohol abuse, use of supplements or certain medications, recent viral illness or muscle trauma.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:1149574:      \"lbl\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial dna deletions, autosomal recessive 6\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-rare.json:1149589:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/progressive_external_ophthalmoplegia_with_mitochondrial_dna_deletions_autosomal_recessive_6\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:6:subsetdef: doid_rare \"DOID rare disease subset\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:7:subsetdef: gard_rare \"GARD rare disease subset\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:11:subsetdef: inferred_rare \"inferred rare disease subset\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:48:synonymtypedef: EXCLUDE \"Synonym to be removed from public release but maintained in edit version as record of external usage\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:1013:name: progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:1017:synonym: \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mtDNA deletions\" EXACT [OMIMPS:157640]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:1020:is_a: MONDO:0005181 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432\"} ! progressive external ophthalmoplegia\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:1151:def: \"Auriculo-condylar syndrome (ACS) presents with bilateral external ear malformations ('question mark' ears), mandibular condyle hypoplasia, microstomia, micrognathia, microglossia and facial asymmetry. Additional manifestations include hypotonia, ptosis, cleft palate, puffy cheeks, developmental delay, impaired hearing and respiratory distress.\" [Orphanet:137888]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:3368:def: \"Fungus infection of the external ear, usually by aspergillus species\" [MESH:D059249]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:3369:synonym: \"external ear fungal infectious disease\" EXACT [MONDO:patterns/location]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:16556:name: external ear lipoma\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:16557:def: \"A benign adipose tissue neoplasm of the external ear.\" [NCIT:C4618]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:16558:synonym: \"external Ear lipoma\" EXACT [DOID:10203, NCIT:C4618]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:16559:synonym: \"external ear lipoma\" EXACT [DOID:10203, MONDO:patterns/location, NCIT:C4618]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:16560:synonym: \"lipoma of external Ear\" EXACT [NCIT:C4618]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:16561:synonym: \"lipoma of external ear\" EXACT [NCIT:C4618]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:16562:synonym: \"lipoma of the external auditory meatus\" EXACT []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:16563:synonym: \"lipoma of the external Ear\" EXACT [DOID:10203, NCIT:C4618]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:16564:synonym: \"lipoma of the external ear\" EXACT [DOID:10203, NCIT:C4618]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:16572:is_a: MONDO:0021235 {source=\"MONDO:Redundant\", source=\"NCIT:C4618/inferred\"} ! external ear neoplasm\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:16576:property_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/external_ear_lipoma\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:16951:def: \"A contagious viral infection caused by the mumps virus. Symptoms include swollen and tender parotid glands, fever, muscle aches and fatigue. Due to vaccination programs, mumps has become a rare disease.\" [NCIT:C29888]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:18356:def: \"An otitis externa which involves infection of the external ear that has spread to involve the skull bone containing part of the ear canal, the middle ear, and the inner ear. It is caused by the bacteria Pseudomonas. This is common in people with weakened immune systems and in older people with diabetes.\" [DOID:10516, http://www.merck.com/mmhe/sec19/ch219/ch219c.html, http://www.nlm.nih.gov/medlineplus/ency/article/000672.htm]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:33285:def: \"Resorption of calcified dental tissue, involving demineralization due to reversal of the cation exchange and lacunar resorption by osteoclasts. There are two types: external (as a result of tooth pathology) and internal (apparently initiated by a peculiar inflammatory hyperplasia of the pulp). (From Jablonski, Dictionary of Dentistry, 1992, p676)\" [MESH:D014091]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:37934:def: \"A male infertility disorder caused by conditions external to the testis, such as hormonal imbalances, reproductive tract obstructions, or systemic illness.\" [PMID:33269513]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:39939:def: \"A type of defective gonadal development in patients with a wide spectrum of chromosomal mosaic variants. Their karyotypes are of partial sex chromosome monosomy resulting from an absence or an abnormal second sex chromosome (X or Y). Karyotypes include 45,X/46,xx; 45,X/46,xx/47,xxx; 46,xxp-; 45,X/46,xy; 45,X/47,xyy; 46,xypi; etc. The spectrum of phenotypes may range from phenotypic female to phenotypic male including variations in gonads and internal and external genitalia, depending on the ratio in each gonad of 45,X primordial germ cells to those with normal 46,xx or 46,xy constitution.\" [MESH:D006060]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:40332:name: external pathological resorption\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:40339:property_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/external_pathological_resorption\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:43116:def: \"A category of psychiatric disorders which are characterized by physical or psychological symptoms that are intentionally produced in order to assume the sick role; there is no external incentive for the behavior, such as economic gain or avoiding legal responsibility, and the person is unaware of any self-motivating factors.\" [NCIT:C92198]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:46052:def: \"Papilloma's are benign epithelial neoplasms that produce visible warty projections from epithelial surfaces. Papilloma's of the urethra typically occur just within or on the external meatus. - 2003\" [NCIT:C5061]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:48418:def: \"An illusion of movement, either of the external world revolving around the individual or of the individual revolving in space. Vertigo may be associated with disorders of the inner ear (ear, inner); vestibular nerve; brainstem; or cerebral cortex. Lesions in the temporal lobe and parietal lobe may be associated with focal seizures that may feature vertigo as an ictal manifestation. (From Adams et al., Principles of Neurology, 6th ed, pp300-1)\" [MESH:D014717]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:51934:relationship: excluded_subClassOf MONDO:0020167 {source=\"Orphanet:861\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432\"} ! obsolete malposition of external canthus\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:59871:def: \"A rare condition characterized by the unequivocal presence of both testicular and ovarian tissues in an individual. It is usually manifested with ambiguous external genitalia.\" [NCIT:C85207]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:60010:name: external ear disorder\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:60011:def: \"A disease involving the external ear.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6601-2165]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:60013:synonym: \"disease of external ear\" EXACT [MONDO:patterns/location_top]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:60014:synonym: \"disease or disorder of external ear\" EXACT []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:60015:synonym: \"disorder of external ear\" EXACT [MONDO:patterns/location_top]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:60016:synonym: \"external ear disease\" EXACT [DOID:379, MONDO:patterns/location]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:60017:synonym: \"external ear disease or disorder\" EXACT [MONDO:design_pattern, MONDO:patterns/location]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:60018:synonym: \"external ear disorder\" EXACT [NCIT:C26972]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:60039:property_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/external_ear_disease\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:60677:def: \"A benign epithelial neoplasm arising from the apocrine sweat glands. Representative examples include tubular apocrine adenoma and external auditory canal ceruminous adenoma.\" [NCIT:P378]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:64088:name: external ear basal cell carcinoma\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:64089:def: \"A basal cell carcinoma that arises from the skin of the external ear.\" [NCIT:C6082]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:64092:synonym: \"basal cell carcinoma of external Ear\" EXACT [NCIT:C6082]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:64093:synonym: \"basal cell carcinoma of the external Ear\" EXACT [DOID:4287, NCIT:C6082]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:64094:synonym: \"basal cell carcinoma of the external ear\" EXACT [DOID:4287, NCIT:C6082]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:64095:synonym: \"basal cell external ear carcinoma\" EXACT [MONDO:patterns/location]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:64096:synonym: \"external Ear basal cell carcinoma\" EXACT [DOID:4287, NCIT:C6082]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:64097:synonym: \"external ear skin basal cell carcinoma\" EXACT [MONDO:patterns/location]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:64098:synonym: \"skin basal cell carcinoma of external ear\" EXACT [MONDO:design_pattern]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:64104:is_a: MONDO:0002944 {source=\"DOID:4287\", source=\"MONDO:Redundant\", source=\"NCIT:C6082\"} ! external ear carcinoma\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:64108:property_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/external_ear_basal_cell_carcinoma\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:64116:name: external ear carcinoma\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:64117:def: \"A carcinoma that arises from epithelial cells of the external ear\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6601-2165]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:64118:synonym: \"carcinoma of external Ear\" EXACT [NCIT:C6081]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:64119:synonym: \"carcinoma of external ear\" EXACT [MONDO:patterns/carcinoma, NCIT:C6081]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:64120:synonym: \"carcinoma of the external Ear\" EXACT [DOID:4288, NCIT:C6081]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:64121:synonym: \"carcinoma of the external ear\" EXACT [DOID:4288, NCIT:C6081]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:64122:synonym: \"external Ear carcinoma\" EXACT [DOID:4288, NCIT:C6081]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:64123:synonym: \"external ear carcinoma\" EXACT [DOID:4288, MONDO:patterns/location, NCIT:C6081]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:64129:is_a: MONDO:0003574 {source=\"DOID:4288\", source=\"MONDO:Redundant\", source=\"NCIT:C6081\"} ! external ear cancer\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:64132:property_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/external_ear_carcinoma\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:71935:def: \"A malignant neoplasm that affects the ear. Representative examples include ceruminous adenocarcinoma and squamous cell carcinoma of the external ear and adenocarcinoma of the middle ear.\" [NCIT:P378]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:77160:name: external ear squamous cell carcinoma\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:77161:def: \"A squamous cell carcinoma that arises from the skin of the external ear.\" [NCIT:C6083]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:77164:synonym: \"epidermoid carcinoma of external Ear\" EXACT [NCIT:C6083]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:77165:synonym: \"epidermoid carcinoma of the external Ear\" EXACT [DOID:5538, NCIT:C6083]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:77166:synonym: \"epidermoid carcinoma of the external ear\" EXACT [DOID:5538, NCIT:C6083]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:77167:synonym: \"external Ear epidermoid carcinoma\" EXACT [NCIT:C6083]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:77168:synonym: \"external Ear squamous cell carcinoma\" EXACT [DOID:5538, NCIT:C6083]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:77169:synonym: \"external ear squamous cell carcinoma\" EXACT [DOID:5538, MONDO:patterns/location, NCIT:C6083]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:77170:synonym: \"squamous cell carcinoma of external Ear\" EXACT [NCIT:C6083]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:77171:synonym: \"squamous cell carcinoma of the external Ear\" EXACT [NCIT:C6083]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:77177:is_a: MONDO:0002944 {source=\"DOID:5538\", source=\"MONDO:Redundant\", source=\"NCIT:C6083\"} ! external ear carcinoma\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:77181:property_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/external_ear_squamous_cell_carcinoma\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:78849:name: external ear cancer\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:78850:def: \"A malignant neoplasm involving the external ear.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6601-2165]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:78851:synonym: \"cancer of external ear\" EXACT [MONDO:patterns/cancer]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:78852:synonym: \"external ear cancer\" EXACT [DOID:5665, MONDO:patterns/location]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:78853:synonym: \"malignant external Ear neoplasm\" EXACT [NCIT:C4653]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:78854:synonym: \"malignant external ear neoplasm\" EXACT [MONDO:patterns/cancer, NCIT:C4653]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:78855:synonym: \"malignant external Ear tumor\" EXACT [NCIT:C4653]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:78856:synonym: \"malignant external Ear tumour\" EXACT OMO:0003005 []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:78857:synonym: \"malignant neoplasm of external Ear\" EXACT [NCIT:C4653]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:78858:synonym: \"malignant neoplasm of external ear\" EXACT [MONDO:patterns/cancer, NCIT:C4653]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:78859:synonym: \"malignant neoplasm of the external Ear\" EXACT [DOID:5665, NCIT:C4653]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:78860:synonym: \"malignant neoplasm of the external ear\" EXACT [DOID:5665, NCIT:C4653]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:78861:synonym: \"malignant tumor of external Ear\" EXACT [DOID:5665, NCIT:C4653]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:78862:synonym: \"malignant tumor of the external Ear\" EXACT [NCIT:C4653]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:78863:synonym: \"malignant tumour of external Ear\" EXACT OMO:0003005 []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:78864:synonym: \"malignant tumour of the external Ear\" EXACT OMO:0003005 []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:78872:is_a: MONDO:0021235 {source=\"MONDO:Redundant\", source=\"NCIT:C4653\"} ! external ear neoplasm\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:86468:def: \"An infiltrating adenocarcinoma derived from ceruminous glands in the external auditory canal.\" [NCIT:P378]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:86480:is_a: MONDO:0002944 {source=\"NCIT:C4176\"} ! external ear carcinoma\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:95560:def: \"A benign epithelial neoplasm derived from ceruminous glands in the external auditory canal. It presents as a gray mass covered by skin. It is characterized by a proliferation of glands composed of cells with abundant eosinophilic and granular cytoplasm.\" [NCIT:C6088]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:95564:synonym: \"ceruminous adenoma of external auditory canal\" EXACT [NCIT:C6088]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:95565:synonym: \"ceruminous adenoma of the external auditory canal\" EXACT [NCIT:C6088]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:95566:synonym: \"external auditory canal ceruminous adenoma\" EXACT [NCIT:C6088]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:95651:def: \"Diseases of the ninth cranial (glossopharyngeal) nerve or its nuclei in the medulla. The nerve may be injured by diseases affecting the lower brain stem, floor of the posterior fossa, jugular foramen, or the nerve's extracranial course. Clinical manifestations include loss of sensation from the pharynx, decreased salivation, and syncope. Glossopharyngeal neuralgia refers to a condition that features recurrent unilateral sharp pain in the tongue, angle of the jaw, external auditory meatus and throat that may be associated with syncope. Episodes may be triggered by cough, sneeze, swallowing, or pressure on the tragus of the ear. (Adams et al., Principles of Neurology, 6th ed, p1390)\" [MESH:D020435]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:104456:def: \"Death of tissue due to external pressure.\" [NCIT:P378]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:108520:synonym: \"external Ear infection\" EXACT [NCIT:C3299]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:108540:is_a: MONDO:0002776 {source=\"DOID:9463\", source=\"ICD10CM:H60\", source=\"MONDO:Redundant\", source=\"NCIT:C3299/inferred\"} ! external ear disorder\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:110211:synonym: \"external thrombosed hemorrhoids\" EXACT []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:110212:synonym: \"Thrombosed external haemorrhoids\" EXACT OMO:0003005 []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:119418:name: progressive external ophthalmoplegia\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:119426:synonym: \"chronic progressive external ophthalmoplegia\" RELATED []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:119427:synonym: \"chronic progressive external ophthalmoplegia [ambiguous]\" EXACT []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:119428:synonym: \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia\" EXACT [DOID:12558, ICD10CM:H49.4, icd11.foundation:1698427219, ICD9CM:378.72, Orphanet:520820]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:119446:property_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/chronic_progressive_external_ophthalmoplegia\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:131319:def: \"A sexually transmitted papillary growth caused by the human papillomavirus. It usually arises in the skin and mucous membranes of the perianal region and external genitalia.\" [NCIT:P378]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:135386:def: \"An acute, localized swelling of the eyelid that may be external or internal and usually is a pyogenic (typically staphylococcal) infection or abscess.\" [https://www.merckmanuals.com/professional/eye-disorders/eyelid-and-lacrimal-disorders/chalazion-and-hordeolum-stye]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:154116:name: cholesteatoma of external ear\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:154117:def: \"A cholesteatoma (disease) that involves the external ear.\" [MONDO:patterns/location]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:154119:synonym: \"cholesteatoma (disease) of external ear\" EXACT []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:154120:synonym: \"external ear cholesteatoma (disease)\" EXACT [MONDO:patterns/location]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:154128:is_a: MONDO:0002776 {source=\"DOID:9462\", source=\"ICD10CM:H60.4/inferred\", source=\"MONDO:Redundant\"} ! external ear disorder\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:154132:property_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/cholesteatoma_of_external_ear\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:159409:def: \"A rare cutaneous tumor of eccrine sweat gland origin. It is most commonly found on the extremities and is usually benign. There is no indication that heredity or external agents cause these tumors.\" [MESH:D018250]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:164684:def: \"Narrowing or occlusion of the renal artery or arteries. It is due usually to atherosclerosis; fibromuscular dysplasia; thrombosis; embolism, or external pressure. The reduced renal perfusion can lead to renovascular hypertension (hypertension, renovascular).\" [MESH:D012078]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:165187:def: \"Overproduction of parathyroid hormone in response to influence external to the parathyroid glands.\" [NCIT:P378]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:165245:def: \"A condition with a clinical picture similar to that of Parkinson disease, but which is caused by external factors, including medication.\" [NCIT:P378]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:166695:def: \"An acute neurological disorder characterized by the triad of ophthalmoplegia, ataxia, and disturbances of mental activity or consciousness. Eye movement abnormalities include nystagmus, external rectus palsies, and reduced conjugate gaze. thiamine deficiency and chronic alcoholism are associated conditions. Pathologic features include periventricular petechial hemorrhages and neuropil breakdown in the diencephalon and brainstem. Chronic thiamine deficiency may lead to korsakoff syndrome. (Adams et al., Principles of Neurology, 6th ed, pp1139-42; Davis & Robertson, Textbook of Neuropathology, 2nd ed, pp452-3)\" [MESH:D014899]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:171038:def: \"Distal arthrogryposis type 5 is an inherited developmental defect syndrome characterized by multiple congenital contractures of limbs, without primary neurologic and/or muscle disease that affects limb function, and ocular anomalies (ptosis, external ophtalmoplegia and/or strabismus). Intelligence is normal.\" [Orphanet:1154]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:171430:name: atresia of external auditory canal and conductive deafness\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:171434:synonym: \"atresia of external auditory canal and conductive deafness\" EXACT [OMIM:108760]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:171440:property_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/atresia_of_external_auditory_canal_and_conductive_deafness\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:171768:def: \"Spinocerebellar ataxia type 3 (SCA3), also known as Machado-Joseph disease, is the most common subtype of type 1 autosomal dominant cerebellar ataxia (ADCA type 1), a neurodegenerative disorder, and is characterized by ataxia, external progressive ophthalmoplegia, and other neurological manifestations.\" [Orphanet:98757]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:176476:def: \"Autosomal dominant popliteal pterygium syndrome (AD-PPS) is a rare genetic malformative disorder characterized by cleft lip, with or without cleft palate, contractures of the lower extremities, abnormal external genitalia, syndactyly of fingers and/or toes, and a pyramidal skin fold over the hallux nail.\" [Orphanet:1300]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:179090:def: \"Gorham-Stout disease (GSD) is a rare disease of massive osteolysis associated with proliferation and dilation of lymphatic vessels. GSD may affect any bone in the body and can be monostotic or polyostotic. Symptoms at presentation are dependent upon the location(s) of the disease; the most common symptom is localized pain. The disease may be discovered after a pathological fracture.\" [Orphanet:73]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:179328:def: \"Deafness-ear malformation-facial palsy syndrome is characterized by profound conductive deafness due to stapedial abnormalities associated with variable malformations of the external ears and facial paralysis. It has been described in three sibs and their mother. Inheritance is autosomal dominant.\" [Orphanet:3232]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:181517:synonym: \"exostoses of external auditory canal\" RELATED []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:181562:def: \"A congenital disorder characterized by malformations of the external ear, which is caused by the first and second branchial arch dysplasia or the first branchial groove insufficiency in the embryonic stage.\" [PMID:37196371]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:184153:name: external auditory canal atresia-vertical talus-hypertelorism syndrome\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:184160:synonym: \"external auditory canal, bilateral atresia of, with congenital vertical talus\" RELATED []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:184161:synonym: \"inherited congenital bilateral atresia of the external auditory canal, congenital bilateral vertical talus and increased interocular distance\" RELATED [GARD:0004638]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:184173:property_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/external_auditory_canal_atresia_vertical_talus_hypertelorism_syndrome\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:184174:property_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/external_auditory_canal_bilateral_atresia_of_with_congenital_vertical_talus\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:187743:def: \"Oculoauriculovertebral spectrum (OAVS) with radial defects is a rare branchial arches and limb primordia development disorder characterized by variable degrees of uni- or bilateral craniofacial malformation and radial defects that result in extremely variable phenotypic manifestations. Characteristic features include low postnatal weight, short stature, vertebral defects, hearing loss, and facial dysmorphism (incl. facial asymmetry, external, middle, and inner ear malformations, orofacial clefts, and mandibular hypoplasia). These features are invariably associated with radial defects, such as preaxial polydactyly, thumb and/or radius hypoplasia/agenesis, or triphalangeal thumb. Cardiac, pulmonary, renal, and central nervous system involvement has also been reported.\" [Orphanet:2549]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:191301:synonym: \"radial Ray defects, hearing impairment, external ophthalmoplegia, and thrombocytopenia\" RELATED []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:191302:synonym: \"radial ray defects, hearing impairment, external ophthalmoplegia, and thrombocytopenia\" EXACT [DOID:0111381, OMIM:147750, Orphanet:2307]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:191329:def: \"Johnson neuroectodermal syndrome is characterized by alopecia, anosmia or hyposmia, conductive deafness with malformed ears and microtia and/or atresia of the external auditory canal, and hypogonadotropic hypogonadism.\" [Orphanet:2316]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:194789:def: \"Nager syndrome, also called Nager acrofacial dysostosis (NAFD) is a congenital malformation syndrome characterized by mandibulofacial dystosis (malar hypoplasia, micrognathia, external ear malformations) and variable preaxial limb defects.\" [Orphanet:245]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:194974:relationship: excluded_subClassOf MONDO:0017311 {source=\"Orphanet:284963/inferred\", source=\"Orphanet:558\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432\"} ! obsolete rare disease with thoracic aortic aneurysm and aortic dissection\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:196635:name: autosomal dominant progressive external ophthalmoplegia\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:196636:def: \"Autosomal dominant form of progressive external ophthalmoplegia.\" [MONDO:patterns/autosomal_dominant]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:196645:synonym: \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant 1\" RELATED [MONDO:Lexical]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:196646:synonym: \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant type 1\" EXACT [MONDO:RULE_1]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:196647:synonym: \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia, autosomal dominant\" EXACT [MONDO:patterns/autosomal_dominant]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:196653:is_a: MONDO:0000090 {source=\"DC-OMIM:157640\", source=\"OMIM:157640\"} ! progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:196655:intersection_of: MONDO:0005181 ! progressive external ophthalmoplegia\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:196657:property_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/progressive_external_ophthalmoplegia_with_mitochondrial_dna_deletions_autosomal_dominant_1\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:197101:def: \"A condition that affects the skin, hair, mucosa (areas ofthe body that are lined with mucus), gums (gingiva), eyes, nose and lungs. Symptoms typically begin in infancy and may include development of cataracts (clouding of the eye lens); blindness; hair loss (alopecia); abnormal changes to the perineum (the area between the anus and external genitalia); and small, skin-colored bumps (keratosis pilaris). Terminal lung disease has also been reported. The cause of HMD is thought to be an abnormality in desmosomes and gap junctions, which are structures involved in cell-to-cell contact. HMD typically follows autosomal dominant inheritance, but has occurred sporadically (in an individual who has no family history of the condition). Treatment typically focuses on individual symptoms of the condition.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432, https://rarediseases.info.nih.gov/diseases/5427/hereditary-mucoepithelial-dysplasia]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:200459:synonym: \"external ophthalmoplegia, nonprogressive, congenital hereditary\" RELATED []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:207586:def: \"Radio-renal syndrome is a rare developmental defect during embryogenesis characterized by variable upper limb reduction defects and renal anomalies. Patients typically present absence/hypoplasia of digits, radii and/or ulnae, short stature and mild external ear malformation, as well as kidney agenesis or ectopia. There have been no further descriptions in the literature since 1983.\" [Orphanet:3015]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:208390:def: \"Autosomal dominant Robinow syndrome (DRS) is the more common type of Robinow syndrome (RS) characterized by mild to moderate limb shortening and abnormalities of the head, face and external genitalia.\" [Orphanet:3107]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:217290:synonym: \"microcephaly, IUGR, hypertelorism, ptosis, iris coloboma, hooked nose, external ear dysplasia, psychomotor retardation\" RELATED [GARD:0007896]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:217605:def: \"Ablepharon macrostomia syndrome is an extremely rare multiple congenital malformation syndrome characterized by the association of ablepharon, macrostomia, abnormal external ears, syndactyly of the hands and feet, skin findings (such as dry and coarse skin or redundant folds of skin), absent or sparse hair, genital malformations and developmental delay (in 2/3 of cases). Other reported manifestations include malar hypoplasia, absent or hypoplastic nipples, umbilical abnormalities and growth retardation. It is a mainly sporadic disorder, although a few familial cases having been reported, and it displays significant clinical overlap with Fraser syndrome.\" [Orphanet:920]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:218303:def: \"Acrocraniofacial dysostosis is a very rare form of acrofacial dyosotosis, reported in two sisters to date, characterized by short stature, acrocephaly, ocular hypertelorism, ptosis of eyelids, ocular proptosis, downslanting palpebral fissures, high nasal bridge, anteverted nostrils, short philtrum, cleft palate, micrognathia, abnormal external ears, preauricular pits, mixed hearing loss, bulbous digits, metatarsus varus, pectus excavatum and various radiological abnormalities. Features of this syndrome were reported to overlap with otopalatodigital syndrome types 1 and 2. There have been no further descriptions in the literature since 1988.\" [Orphanet:949]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:218809:def: \"A type of arthrogryposis characterized by congenital cleft palate, microcephaly, craniostenosis and arthrogryposis (limitation of extension of elbows, flexed adducted thumbs, camptodactyly and clubfeet). Additional features include facial dysmorphism (\\\"myopathic\\\" stiff face, antimongoloid slanting, external ophthalmoplegia, telecanthus, low-set large malrotated ears, open mouth, mierogenia and high arched palate). Velopharyngeal insufficiency with difficulties in swallowing, increased secretion of the nose and throat, prominent occiput, generalized muscular hypotonia with mild cyanosis and no spontaneous movements, seizures, torticollis, areflexia, intellectual disability, hypertrichosis of the lower extremities, and scleredema (in the first days of life) are also observed. The disease often leads to early death. Transmission is autosomal recessive. No new cases of adducted thumbs-arthrogryposis, Christian type have been described since 1983.\" [Orphanet:2952]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:225822:def: \"Cereballar ataxia - ectodermal dysplasia is a very rare disease, characterized by hypodontia and sparse hair in combination with cerebellar ataxia and normal intelligence. Imaging demonstrates a cerebellar atrophy.\" [Orphanet:1174]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:227625:def: \"Verloove Vanhorick-Brubakk syndrome is a multiple congenital anomalies/dysmorphic syndrome characterized by multiple skeletal malformations (short femora and humeri, bilateral absence of metatarsal and metacarpal bone in hands and feet, bilateral partial syndactyly of fingers and toes or oligopolysyndactyly, deformed lumbosacral spine), congenital heart disease (truncus arteriosus), lung and urogenital malformations (bilateral bilobar lungs, horseshoe kidney, cryptorchidism), and facial malformations (bilateral cleft lip and palate, micrognathia, small, low-set ears without external meatus). It is lethal in the neonatal period. There have been no further descriptions in the literature since 1981.\" [Orphanet:3429]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:230609:name: conductive deafness-malformed external ear syndrome\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:230616:synonym: \"conductive deafness - malformed external ear\" RELATED [GARD:0001460]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:230617:synonym: \"conductive deafness with malformed external ear\" RELATED [GARD:0001460]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:230619:synonym: \"conductive hearing loss-malformed external ear syndrome\" EXACT [Orphanet:3216]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:230620:synonym: \"deafness, conductive, with malformed external EAR\" RELATED []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:230631:property_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/deafness_conductive_with_malformed_external_ear\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:230641:def: \"Conductive deafness-ptosis-skeletal anomalies syndrome is a rare, genetic ectodermal dysplasia syndrome characterized by conductive hearing loss due to atresia of the external auditory canal and the middle ear complicated by chronic infection, ptosis and skeletal anomalies (internal rotation of hips, dislocation of the radial heads and fifth finger clinodactyly). In addition, a thin, pinched nose, delayed hair growth and dysplastic teeth are associated. There have been no further descriptions in the literature since 1978.\" [Orphanet:3236]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:252282:name: congenital multicore myopathy with external ophthalmoplegia\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:252291:synonym: \"minicore myopathy with external ophthalmoplegia\" RELATED []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:252294:synonym: \"multicore myopathy with external ophthalmoplegia\" RELATED [GARD:0010316]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:252295:synonym: \"multiminicore disease with external ophthalmoplegia\" RELATED []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:252296:synonym: \"multiminicore myopathy multicore myopathy with external ophthalmoplegia\" RELATED []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:252306:property_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/congenital_multicore_myopathy_with_external_ophthalmoplegia\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:254806:name: progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal recessive 1\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:254807:def: \"Any autosomal recessive progressive external ophthalmoplegia in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the POLG gene.\" [MONDO:patterns/disease_series_by_gene]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:254811:synonym: \"autosomal recessive progressive external ophthalmoplegia\" RELATED [GARD:0001191]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:254812:synonym: \"autosomal recessive progressive external ophthalmoplegia caused by mutation in POLG\" EXACT [MONDO:design_pattern]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:254813:synonym: \"cerebellar ataxia infantile with progressive external ophthalmoplegia\" RELATED [GARD:0001191]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:254815:synonym: \"POLG autosomal recessive progressive external ophthalmoplegia\" EXACT [MONDO:design_pattern, MONDO:patterns/disease_series_by_gene]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:254816:synonym: \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with cerebellar ataxia infantile\" RELATED [GARD:0001191]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:254817:synonym: \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal recessive 1\" EXACT [MONDO:Lexical, OMIM:258450]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:254818:synonym: \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal recessive type 1\" EXACT [MONDO:RULE_1]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:254819:synonym: \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia, autosomal recessive 1\" RELATED []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:254825:is_a: MONDO:0000090 {source=\"DC-OMIM:258450\", source=\"OMIM:258450\"} ! progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:254826:is_a: MONDO:0016810 {source=\"MONDO:Redundant\", source=\"Orphanet:254886/btnt\"} ! autosomal recessive progressive external ophthalmoplegia\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:254827:intersection_of: MONDO:0016810 ! autosomal recessive progressive external ophthalmoplegia\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:254831:property_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/progressive_external_ophthalmoplegia_with_mitochondrial_dna_deletions_autosomal_recessive_1\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:254832:property_value: seeAlso \"https://rarediseases.info.nih.gov/diseases/1191/progressive-external-ophthalmoplegia-autosomal-recessive-1\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"GARD:0001191\"}\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:255334:def: \"A rare, genetic intellectual disability syndrome characterized by macrocephaly, hypotonia, dysmorphic facial features (wide forehead, ptosis, downslanting palpebral fissures, enlarged and calcified external ears, large jaw), sparse body hair, tall stature, and intellectual disability. Hearing loss, insulin-resistant diabetes, and progressive distal muscle wasting (leading to joint contractures) have also been reported in adulthood. Rare manifestations include behavioral abnormalities (aggression and restlessness), hypothyroidism, cerebral calcification, ataxia, and peripheral neuropathy.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432, Orphanet:3042]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:261101:def: \"Ulbright-Hodes syndrome is characterized by renal dysplasia, growth retardation, phocomelia or mesomelia, radiohumeral fusion, rib abnormalities, anomalies of the external genitalia and a potter-like facies. The syndrome has been described in three infants (one pair of sibs and an unrelated case), all of whom died shortly after birth from respiratory distress resulting from pulmonary hypoplasia and oligohydramnios caused by renal dysplasia. The mode of transmission appears to be autosomal recessive.\" [Orphanet:3404]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:262170:def: \"Autosomal recessive Robinow syndrome (RRS) is the less common type of Robinow syndrome (RS) characterized by short-limb dwarfism, costovertebral segmentation defects and abnormalities of the head, face and external genitalia.\" [Orphanet:1507]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:264508:def: \"Spondylocostal dysostosis-anal and genitourinary malformations syndrome is characterized by the association of spondylocostal dysostosis with anal and genitourinary malformations (anal atresia and agenesis of external and internal genitalia). To date, only four cases have been described in the literature. Autosomal recessive inheritance has been suggested.\" [Orphanet:94095]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:268218:synonym: \"familial visceral myopathy with external ophthalmoplegia\" RELATED [GARD:0005496]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:268219:synonym: \"intestinal pseudoobstruction with external ophthalmoplegia\" RELATED []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:268221:synonym: \"visceral myopathy - familial external ophthalmoplegia\" RELATED [GARD:0005496]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:268222:synonym: \"visceral myopathy, familial, with external ophthalmoplegia\" RELATED []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:268223:synonym: \"visceral myopathy-familial external ophthalmoplegia syndrome\" EXACT [Orphanet:1876]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:268233:property_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/visceral_myopathy_familial_with_external_ophthalmoplegia\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:285912:name: ophthalmoplegia, external, and myopia\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:285915:synonym: \"ophthalmoplegia, external, and myopia\" EXACT [MONDO:Lexical, OMIM:311000]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:285921:property_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/ophthalmoplegia_external_and_myopia\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:286033:def: \"A rare neurodevelopmental disorder in the ciliopathy group that is lethal in males and characterized by variable anomalies including external malformations (craniofacial and digital), and possible involvement of the central nervous system (CNS) and of viscera (kidneys, pancreas and ovaries) in females.\" [Orphanet:2750]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:287034:synonym: \"progressive basal ganglion dysfunction, mental and growth retardation, external ophthalmoplegia, postnatal microcephaly and deafness\" RELATED [GARD:0009288]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:288141:def: \"46,XY complete gonadal dysgenesis (46,XY CGD) is a disorder of sex development (DSD) associated with anomalies in gonadal development that result in the presence of female external and internal genitalia despite the 46,XY karyotype.\" [Orphanet:242]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:288711:def: \"Kearns-Sayre syndrome (KSS) is a mitochondrial disease characterized by progressive external ophthalmoplegia (PEO), pigmentary retinitis and an onset before the age of 20 years. Common additional features include deafness, cerebellar ataxia and heart block.\" [Orphanet:480]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:288720:synonym: \"chronic progressive external ophthalmoplegia with myopathy\" RELATED []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:288733:synonym: \"ophthalmoplegia, progressive external, with ragged red fibers\" RELATED [GARD:0006817]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:288734:synonym: \"ophthalmoplegia, progressive external, with ragged red fibres\" RELATED OMO:0003005 []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:288735:synonym: \"ophthalmoplegia, progressive external, with ragged-Red fibers\" RELATED []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:288736:synonym: \"ophthalmoplegia, progressive external, with ragged-Red fibres\" RELATED OMO:0003005 []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:288754:is_a: MONDO:0005181 {source=\"DOID:12934\", source=\"MESH:D007625\", source=\"icd11.foundation:399100745\"} ! progressive external ophthalmoplegia\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:288958:def: \"Lethal infantile mitochondrial myopathy is a rare mitochondrial oxidative phosphorylation disorder characterized by progressive generalized hypotonia, progressive external ophthalmoplegia and severe lactic acidosis, which results in early fatality (days to months after birth). Patients may present with lethargy and areflexia and may associate additional features, such as cardiomyopathy, renal dysfunction, liver involvement and seizures.\" [Orphanet:254857]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:289654:def: \"Chondrodysplasia - disorder of sex development is an extremely rare disorder of sex development, reported in only two siblings (one terminated in pregnancy) to date, characterized by the clinical features of 46,XY complete gonadal dysgenesis (normal external female genitalia, lack of pubertal development, primary amenorrhea, and hypergonadotrophic hypogonadism) in association with severe dwarfism with generalized chondrodysplasia (bell-shaped thorax, micromelia, brachydactyly). Other reported features in the live sibling included eye anomalies (hypoplastic irides, myopia, coloboma of optic disks), dysmorphic features (deep-set eyes, upslanting palpebral fissures, puffy eyelids, large ears and mouth, mild prognathism), muscular hypoplasia, mild intellectual deficiency and severe microcephaly with cerebellar vermis hypoplasia. An autosomal recessive inheritance has been suggested.\" [Orphanet:1422]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:292036:def: \"Waters-West syndrome is characterized by the association of lethal non-spherocytic, non-immune hemolytic anemia with abnormalities of the external genitalia (micropenis and hypospadias), flat occiput, dimpled earlobes, deep plantar creases, and increased space between the first and second toes. It has been described only once in two brothers who died a few hours after birth. The second-born infant had massive ascites and hepatosplenomegaly. The mother had two spontaneous abortions (at 6 and 12 weeks gestation) but gave birth to a normal girl, suggesting an autosomal or X-linked recessive mode of inheritance. Although the parents were not known to be consanguineous, they shared a French-Canadian and American Indian ethnic origin.\" [Orphanet:1046]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:292514:def: \"Loose anagen syndrome is a rare benign hair disorder affecting predominantly blond females in childhood and characterized by the presence of hair that can be easily and painlessly pulled out. Most of the hair is in the anagen phase and lacks an external epithelial sheath. Hair grows back quickly and the condition improves spontaneously with aging. Loose anagen hair can be associated with other anomalies, such as coloboma.\" [Orphanet:168]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:292907:def: \"A congenital malformation of the external ear, seen more frequently in males, that occurs sporadically or is inherited, that is characterized by unilateral (79-93% of cases, 60% of which involve the right ear) or bilateral small and abnormally shaped auricles and that is often associated with atresia or stenosis of the ear canal, attention deficit disorders and delayed language development. The variation in auricle size ranges from grade I, where the auricle is simply smaller than normal, to grade IV, also known as anotia, where there is a complete absence of the external ear and of the auditory canal.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432, Orphanet:83463]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:297740:def: \"A rare, congenital malformation syndrome characterized by the association of anterior ocular chamber cleavage disorder with developmental delay, short stature and congenital hypothyroidism. Additional manifestations include cerebellar hypoplasia, tracheal stenosis, narrow external auditory meatus, and hip dislocation. There have been no further description in the literature since 1995.\" [Orphanet:2321]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:305274:def: \"Limb-mammary syndrome (LMS) is a rare disease belonging to the group of ectodermal dysplasias.\" [Orphanet:69085]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:318817:def: \"Inflammation of the nasal mucous membranes caused by an IgE-mediated response to external allergens. The inflammation may also involve the mucous membranes of the sinuses, eyes, middle ear, and pharynx. Symptoms include sneezing, nasal congestion, rhinorrhea, and itching. It may lead to fatigue, drowsiness, and malaise thus causing impairment of the quality of life.\" [NCIT:C79532]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:319509:synonym: \"ophthalmoplegia, progressive external, and scoliosis\" RELATED []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:319510:synonym: \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia and scoliosis\" EXACT [Orphanet:2744]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:323541:synonym: \"anophthalmia clinical with micrognathia malformed ears digital anomalies and abnormal external genitalia\" RELATED [GARD:0003645]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:323542:synonym: \"anophthalmia, clinical, with micrognathia, malformed ears, digital anomalies, and abnormal external genitalia\" RELATED []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:329331:name: lateral semicircular canal malformation, familial, with external and middle ear abnormalities\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:329332:synonym: \"lateral semicircular canal malformation, familial, with external and middle ear abnormalities\" EXACT [OMIM:608814]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:329338:property_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/lateral_semicircular_canal_malformation_familial_with_external_and_middle_ear_abnormalities\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:329339:property_value: seeAlso \"https://rarediseases.info.nih.gov/diseases/10067/lateral-semicircular-canal-malformation-familial-with-external-and-middle-ear-abnormalities\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"GARD:0010067\"}\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:332370:name: progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant 2\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:332371:def: \"Any progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the SLC25A4 gene.\" [MONDO:patterns/disease_series_by_gene]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:332376:synonym: \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions caused by mutation in SLC25A4\" EXACT [MONDO:design_pattern]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:332377:synonym: \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant 2\" EXACT [MONDO:Lexical, OMIM:609283]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:332378:synonym: \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant type 2\" EXACT [MONDO:RULE_1]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:332379:synonym: \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia, autosomal dominant 2\" RELATED []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:332380:synonym: \"SLC25A4 progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions\" EXACT [MONDO:design_pattern, MONDO:patterns/disease_series_by_gene]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:332387:is_a: MONDO:0008003 {source=\"Orphanet:254892/btnt\"} ! autosomal dominant progressive external ophthalmoplegia\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:332388:intersection_of: MONDO:0000090 ! progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:332391:property_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/progressive_external_ophthalmoplegia_with_mitochondrial_dna_deletions_autosomal_dominant_2\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:332466:name: progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant 3\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:332467:def: \"Any progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the TWNK gene.\" [MONDO:patterns/disease_series_by_gene]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:332472:synonym: \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions caused by mutation in TWNK\" EXACT [MONDO:design_pattern]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:332473:synonym: \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant 3\" EXACT [MONDO:Lexical, OMIM:609286]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:332474:synonym: \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant type 3\" EXACT [MONDO:RULE_1]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:332475:synonym: \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia, autosomal dominant 3\" RELATED []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:332476:synonym: \"TWNK progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions\" EXACT [MONDO:design_pattern, MONDO:patterns/disease_series_by_gene]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:332483:is_a: MONDO:0008003 {source=\"Orphanet:254892/btnt\"} ! autosomal dominant progressive external ophthalmoplegia\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:332484:intersection_of: MONDO:0000090 ! progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:332487:property_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/progressive_external_ophthalmoplegia_with_mitochondrial_dna_deletions_autosomal_dominant_3\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:334436:synonym: \"external ophthalmoplegia with synergistic divergence\" RELATED []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:334437:synonym: \"external ophthalmoplegia, synergistic divergence, jaw winking, and oculocutaneous hypopigmentation\" RELATED []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:337404:name: progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant 4\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:337405:def: \"Any progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the POLG2 gene.\" [MONDO:patterns/disease_series_by_gene]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:337409:synonym: \"POLG2 progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions\" EXACT [MONDO:design_pattern, MONDO:patterns/disease_series_by_gene]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:337410:synonym: \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions caused by mutation in POLG2\" EXACT [MONDO:design_pattern]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:337411:synonym: \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant 4\" EXACT [MONDO:Lexical, OMIM:610131]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:337412:synonym: \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant type 4\" EXACT [MONDO:RULE_1]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:337413:synonym: \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia, autosomal dominant 4\" RELATED []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:337420:is_a: MONDO:0008003 {source=\"Orphanet:254892/btnt\"} ! autosomal dominant progressive external ophthalmoplegia\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:337421:intersection_of: MONDO:0000090 ! progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:337424:property_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/progressive_external_ophthalmoplegia_with_mitochondrial_dna_deletions_autosomal_dominant_4\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:348918:def: \"Oculoauricular syndrome, Schorderet type is a rare, genetic developmental defect during embryogenesis characterized by various ophthalmic anomalies (including congenital microphthalmia, microcornea, cataract, anterior segment dysgenesis, ocular coloboma and early onset rod-cone dystrophy), and abnormal external ears (low-set pinna with crumpled helix, narrow intertragic incisure, abnormal bridge connecting the crus of the helix and the anthelix, narrow external acoustic meatus, and lobule aplasia).\" [Orphanet:157962]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:348928:synonym: \"microphthalmia, microcornea, anterior segment dysgenesis, cataract, ocular coloboma, retinal pigment epithelium abnormalities, Rod-cone dystrophy, and anomalies of the external Ear\" RELATED []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:358290:name: progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant 5\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:358291:def: \"Any progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the RRM2B gene.\" [MONDO:patterns/disease_series_by_gene]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:358296:synonym: \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions caused by mutation in RRM2B\" EXACT [MONDO:design_pattern]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:358297:synonym: \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant 5\" EXACT [MONDO:Lexical, OMIM:613077]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:358298:synonym: \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant type 5\" EXACT [MONDO:RULE_1]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:358299:synonym: \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia, autosomal dominant 5\" RELATED []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:358300:synonym: \"RRM2B progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions\" EXACT [MONDO:design_pattern, MONDO:patterns/disease_series_by_gene]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:358307:is_a: MONDO:0008003 {source=\"Orphanet:254892/btnt\"} ! autosomal dominant progressive external ophthalmoplegia\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:358308:intersection_of: MONDO:0000090 ! progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:358311:property_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/progressive_external_ophthalmoplegia_with_mitochondrial_dna_deletions_autosomal_dominant_5\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:366996:def: \"A rare, genetic, developmental defect during embryogenesis disorder characterized by severe, early-onset, salt-wasting adrenal insufficiency and ambiguous/female external genitalia (irrespective of chromosomal sex) due to mutations in the <i>CYP11A1</i> gene. Milder cases may present delayed onset of adrenal gland dysfunction and genitalia phenotype may range from normal male to female in individuals with 46,XY karyotype. Imaging studies reveal hypoplastic/absent adrenal glands and biochemical findings include low serum cortisol, mineralocorticoids, androgens, and sodium, with elevated potassium levels.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432, Orphanet:168558]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:385672:def: \"Progressive external ophthalmoplegia-myopathy-emaciation syndrome is a rare mitochondrial oxidative phosphorylation disorder due to nuclear DNA anomalies characterized by progressive external ophthalmoplegia without diplopia, cerebellar atrophy, proximal skeletal muscle weakness with generalized muscle wasting, profound emaciation, respiratory failure, spinal deformity and facial muscle weakness (manifesting with ptosis, dysphonia, dysphagia and nasal speech). Intellectual disability, gastrointestinal symptoms (e.g. nausea, abdominal fullness, and loss of appetite), dilated cardiomyopathy and renal colic have also been reported.\" [Orphanet:352447]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:385688:synonym: \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia-myopathy-emaciation syndrome\" RELATED []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:386311:synonym: \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant 6\" RELATED [MONDO:Lexical]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:386312:synonym: \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant type 6\" EXACT [MONDO:RULE_1]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:386313:synonym: \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia, autosomal dominant 6\" RELATED []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:386320:is_a: MONDO:0000090 {source=\"DC-OMIM:615156\", source=\"OMIM:615156\"} ! progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:386323:property_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/progressive_external_ophthalmoplegia_with_mitochondrial_dna_deletions_autosomal_dominant_6_2\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:391259:def: \"Syndromic microphthalmia-12 is a rare disease characterized by bilateral small eyeballs (microphthalmia), lungs that are too small (pulmonary hypoplasia), and a defect or hole in the diaphragm that allows the abdominal contents to move into the chest cavity (diaphragmatic hernia). Other symptoms may include: Severe global developmental delay with progressive motor impairment due to spasticity and/or uncontrolled repetitive muscular contractions (dystonia), with or without abnormal quick movements that resemble dancing (chorea), Defects of the cerebellum (Chiari type I malformation) Accumulation of cerebrospinal fluid inside the brain (hydrocephaly), Severe feeding difficulties, Mild facial dysmorphism with broad nasal root and tip, and a very small chin (micrognathia), Severe language delay, Wheelchair-bound. Syndromic microphthalmia-12 is caused by mutations in the RARB gene. There is no specific treatment for this syndrome.\" [https://rarediseases.info.nih.gov/diseases/13235/syndromic-microphthalmia-12]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:404156:name: progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal recessive 2\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:404157:def: \"Any progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the RNASEH1 gene.\" [MONDO:patterns/disease_series_by_gene]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:404163:synonym: \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions caused by mutation in RNASEH1\" EXACT [MONDO:design_pattern]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:404164:synonym: \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal recessive 2\" EXACT [MONDO:Lexical, OMIM:616479]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:404165:synonym: \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal recessive type 2\" EXACT [MONDO:RULE_1]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:404166:synonym: \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia, autosomal recessive 2\" RELATED []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:404167:synonym: \"RNASEH1 progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions\" EXACT [MONDO:design_pattern, MONDO:patterns/disease_series_by_gene]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:404173:is_a: MONDO:0000090 {source=\"DC-OMIM:616479\", source=\"MONDO:Redundant\", source=\"OMIM:616479\"} ! progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:404174:is_a: MONDO:0018002 {source=\"Orphanet:329336/btnt\"} ! adult-onset chronic progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial myopathy\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:404175:intersection_of: MONDO:0000090 ! progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:404178:property_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/progressive_external_ophthalmoplegia_with_mitochondrial_dna_deletions_autosomal_recessive_2\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:406058:def: \"Autosomal dominant optic atrophy plus syndrome (ADOA plus) is a variant of autosomal dominant optic atrophy (ADOA) associating the typical optic atrophy with other extra-ocular manifestations such as sensorineural deafness, myopathy, chronic progressive external ophthalmoplegia, ataxia and peripheral neuropathy. More rarely, other manifestations have been associated with this condition, such as spastic paraplegia, multiple-sclerosis like illness.\" [Orphanet:1215]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:411207:name: progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal recessive 3\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:411208:def: \"Any autosomal recessive progressive external ophthalmoplegia in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the TK2 gene.\" [MONDO:patterns/disease_series_by_gene]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:411211:synonym: \"autosomal recessive progressive external ophthalmoplegia caused by mutation in TK2\" EXACT [MONDO:design_pattern]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:411213:synonym: \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal recessive 3\" EXACT [OMIM:617069]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:411214:synonym: \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal recessive 3; PEOB3\" EXACT []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:411215:synonym: \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal recessive type 3\" EXACT [MONDO:RULE_1]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:411216:synonym: \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia, autosomal recessive 3\" RELATED []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:411217:synonym: \"TK2 autosomal recessive progressive external ophthalmoplegia\" EXACT [MONDO:design_pattern, MONDO:patterns/disease_series_by_gene]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:411223:is_a: MONDO:0000090 {source=\"DC-OMIM:617069\", source=\"OMIM:617069\"} ! progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:411224:is_a: MONDO:0016810 {source=\"MONDO:Redundant\", source=\"Orphanet:254886/btnt\"} ! autosomal recessive progressive external ophthalmoplegia\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:411225:intersection_of: MONDO:0016810 ! autosomal recessive progressive external ophthalmoplegia\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:411228:property_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/progressive_external_ophthalmoplegia_with_mitochondrial_dna_deletions_autosomal_recessive_3\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:411236:name: progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal recessive 4\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:411237:def: \"An extremely rare multiple mitochondrial DNA deletion syndrome with markedly decreased deoxyguanosine kinase (DGUOK) activity in skeletal muscle characterized by a highly variable phenotype. Clinical manifestations include progressive external ophthalmoplegia, mitochondrial myopathy, recurrent rhabdomyolysis, lower motor neuron disease, mild cognitive impairment, sensory axonal neuropathy, optic atrophy, ataxia, hypogonadism and/or parkinsonism.\" [Orphanet:329314]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:411248:synonym: \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal recessive 4\" EXACT [OMIM:617070]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:411249:synonym: \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal recessive type 4\" EXACT [MONDO:RULE_1]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:411250:synonym: \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia, autosomal recessive 4\" RELATED []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:411258:is_a: MONDO:0000090 {source=\"DC-OMIM:617070\", source=\"OMIM:617070\"} ! progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:411261:property_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/progressive_external_ophthalmoplegia_with_mitochondrial_dna_deletions_autosomal_recessive_4\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:418177:name: obsolete rare disease involving intestinal motility\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:419323:def: \"Arachnodactyly-intellectual disability-dysmorphism syndrome is characterized by moderate intellectual deficit, brachycephaly, typical facies (thin lips and microstomia), ectomorphic habitus with extremely long, thin fingers and toes, and hypoplastic external genitalia. It has been described in three patients.\" [Orphanet:1130]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:419370:def: \"Arrhinia is an extremely rare, major congenital malformation consisting of an absence of the nose ranging from hyporrhinia (absence of external nasal structures) to total arrhinia (absence of external nose, nasal airways, olfactory bulbs, or olfactory nerve) often causing respiratory distress and requiring surgical correction. Arrhinia can be bilateral or unilateral (hemiarrhinia). Associated anomalies include ocular features (hypertelorism, microphthalmia, eyelid coloboma), facial clefts, midline defects and microtia.\" [Orphanet:1134]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:420813:def: \"Maternally inherited cardiomyopathy and hearing loss is a mitochondrial disease described in two unrelated families to date that has a heterogeneous clinical presentation characterized by the association of progressive sensorineural hearing loss with hypertrophic cardiomyopathy and, in the majority of cases, encephalomyopathy symptoms such as ataxia, slurred speech, progressive external opthalmoparesis (PEO), muscle weakness, myalgia, and exercise intolerance.\" [Orphanet:1349]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:421696:name: obsolete rare disease with Pierre Robin syndrome\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:423263:name: obsolete external auditory canal aplasia/hypoplasia\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:423265:synonym: \"external auditory canal stenosis/atresia\" EXACT []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:423268:property_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/external_auditory_canal_aplasia_hypoplasia\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:423388:def: \"Proboscis lateralis (PL) is a rare congenital facial abnormality characterized by failed development of the external nose on one side that is replaced by a tubular structure composed of skin and soft tissue usually attached at the inner canthus of the eye and therefore often associated with maldevelopment of the nasal cavity or paranasal sinuses of the affected side. PL is also associated with other craniofacial abnormalities such as orbital anomalies, cleft lip/palate, frontal encephalocele and holoprosencephaly.\" [Orphanet:141099]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:426351:name: obsolete pinnae and external auditory canal anomaly\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:426355:property_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/pinnae_and_external_auditory_canal_anomaly\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:427977:def: \"Isolated congenital auditory ossicle malformation is a rare, congential, middle ear anomaly characterized by, usually unilateral and sporadic, variations in the number, size and/or configuration of the ossicles, with no tympanic membrane and external ear abnormalities and no history of trauma or infection. Patients frequently present late, after schooling has started, with non- progressive, conductive hearing loss often associated with speech delay and poor school performance.\" [Orphanet:162526]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:427984:synonym: \"congenital auditory ossicle malformation without external ear abnormality\" EXACT [Orphanet:162526]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:430234:name: obsolete rare disease with dentinogenesis imperfecta\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:434488:def: \"Complete septate uterus is a rare, non-syndromic uterovaginal malformation characterized by a uterus that has a longitudinal septum which elongates from the uterine fundus to the internal or external cervical os. Most often women are asymptomatic, however dysmenorrhoea, unilateral obstruction, and endometriosis could be observed. Unlike urinary tract abnormalities, which are very rarely associated, poor reproductive outcome is frequent.\" [Orphanet:180126]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:435210:name: obsolete rare disease with autism\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:436559:relationship: excluded_subClassOf MONDO:0017952 {source=\"Orphanet:183\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432\"} ! obsolete non-familial rare disease with dilated cardiomyopathy\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:436580:def: \"Axial mesodermal dysplasia spectrum is a rare developmental defect during embryogenesis syndrome characterized by congenital manifestations of both oculo-auriculo-vertebral spectrum and caudal regression sequence. Phenotype is highly variable but patients typically present facial dysmorphism (incl. asymmetry, hypertelorism), auricular abnormalities (e.g. preauricular tags, microtia, absence of middle ear ossicles), skeletal malformations (hemivertebrae, hip dislocation, sacral agenesis/dysplasia, talipes equinovarus, flexion deformity of lower limbs), cardiac defects (dextrocardia, septal defects), renal and genitourinary anomalies (such as renal agensis/dysplasia, abnormal external genitalia, cryptorchidia), as well as anal anomalies such as anal atresia and rectovesical fistula.\" [Orphanet:1834]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:436612:def: \"OBSOLETE. Polymalformative genetic syndrome with increased risk of developing cancer (PGSIRC) comprises a wide range of syndromes characterized by congenital malformations with a high risk of developing tumors including up to 50 different rare diseases.\" [Orphanet:183422]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:441734:synonym: \"OPCA with macular Degeneration and external ophthalmoplegia\" RELATED []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:442756:def: \"Pulmonary fibrosis - hepatic hyperplasia - bone marrow hypoplasia, also named Btrimorphic syndromeB (i.e. three (inherited) morbidities, pulmonary, hepatic and cytopenia), is a rare disease reported in 4 cases to date, manifesting with idiopathic pulmonary fibrosis, hepatic nodular regenerative hyperplasia leading to portal hypertension and thrombocytopenia due to bone marrow hypoplasia. The condition was associated with 100% mortality.\" [Orphanet:210136]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:444892:def: \"A rare, genetically highly heterogeneous otorhinolaryngologic disease, resulting from inner and/or middle ear or hearing nerve anomalies, typically characterized by bilateral, severe to profound hearing loss (mean sensorineural hearing impairment of 60 dB or more for 500-, 1,000-, and 2,000-Hz frequency tones in the better ear) which occurs before the onset of speech development and is not associated with visible external ear abnormalities or any other medical problems. It is usually nonprogressive and impedes oral language acquisition.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432, Orphanet:216445]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:444913:def: \"Postlingual non-syndromic genetic deafness is a rare, genetically highly heterogeneous otorhinolaryngologic disease, resulting from inner and/or middle ear or hearing nerve anomalies, typically characterized by progressive, bilateral, moderate to profound hearing loss (mean sensorineural hearing impairment equal to 40 dB or more for 500-, 1,000-, and 2,000-Hz frequency tones in the better ear) which occurs after the onset of speech development and is not associated with visible external ear abnormalities or any other medical problems. Language development is not initially significantly delayed.\" [Orphanet:216452]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:444932:def: \"A central nervous system malformation syndrome characterized by holoprosencephaly with microcephaly, abnormal eye morphology (hypotelorism, cyclopia, exophthalmos), nasal anomalies (single nostril or absent nose), and cleft lip/palate, combined with signs of caudal regression (sacral agenesis, sirenomelia with absent external genitalia).\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432, Orphanet:2165]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:446292:def: \"OBSOLETE. Rare hereditary hemochromatosis comprises the rare forms of hereditary hemochromatosis (HH), a group of diseases characterized by excessive tissue iron deposition. These rare forms are hemochromatosis type 2 (juvenile), type 3 (TFR2-related), and type 4 (ferroportin disease). Hemochromatosis type 1 (also called classic hemochromatosis) is not a rare disease.\" [Orphanet:220489]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:448808:def: \"Isotretinoin embryopathy is an association of malformations caused by the teratogenic effect of isotretinoin, an oral synthetic vitamin A derivative, which is used to treat severe recalcitrant cystic acne. Exposure to isotretinoin during the first trimester of pregnancy has been associated with an increased risk of spontaneous abortions and severe birth defects including serious craniofacial (microcephaly, asymmetric crying facies, microphthalmia, developmental abnormalities of the external ear, ocular hypertelorism), cardio vascular (conotruncal heart defects, aortic arch abnormalities), and central nervous system (hydrocephalus, microcephaly, lissencephaly, Dandy-Walker malformation, cognitive deficit) anomalies and thymic aplasia. Isoretinoin is contraindicated during pregnancy.\" [Orphanet:2305]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:451697:def: \"OBSOLETE. Mitochondrial oxidative phosphorylation disorder due to nuclear DNA anomalies is a group of clinically heterogeneous diseases, commonly defined by lack of cellular energy due to defects of oxidative phosphorylation (OXPHOS), resulting from pathogenic mutations in the nuclear DNA. Mitochondrial oxidative phosphorylation disorder due to nuclear DNA anomalies includes diseases classified according to defects in: genes encoding structural components of OXPHOS complexes (such as Leigh syndrome, coenzyme Q10 deficiency); genes encoding assembly factors of OXPHOS complexes (such as GRACILE syndrome); genes altering the stability of mitochondrial DNA (such as autosomal dominant progressive external ophthalmoplegia, mitochondrial DNA depletion syndrome); mitochondrial protein synthesis.\" [Orphanet:2443]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:457301:def: \"Mitochondrial DNA depletion syndrome, encephalomyopathic form is a group of mitochondrial DNA maintenance syndrome diseases characterized by predominantly neuromuscular manifestations with typically infantile onset of hypotonia, lactic acidosis, psychomotor delay, progressive hyperkinetic-dystonic movement disorders, external ophtalmoplegia, sensosineural hearing loss, generalized seizures and variable renal tubular dysfunction. It may be associated with a broad range of other clinical features.\" [Orphanet:254803]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:457529:def: \"A rare, mitochondrial DNA maintenance syndrome characterized by cerebellar ataxia, sensory peripheral neuropathy, myoclonus, epilepsy, progressive cognitive impairment, late-onset ptosis and external ophthalmoplegia. Liver failure may also occur, most often in association with the use of antiepileptic drug sodium valproate.\" [Orphanet:254881]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:457555:name: autosomal recessive progressive external ophthalmoplegia\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:457556:def: \"Autosomal recessive form of progressive external ophthalmoplegia.\" [MONDO:patterns/autosomal_recessive]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:457564:synonym: \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia, autosomal recessive\" EXACT [MONDO:patterns/autosomal_recessive]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:457570:is_a: MONDO:0005181 {source=\"Orphanet:254886\"} ! progressive external ophthalmoplegia\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:457572:intersection_of: MONDO:0005181 ! progressive external ophthalmoplegia\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:457574:property_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/autosomal_recessive_progressive_external_ophthalmoplegia\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:465805:def: \"Machado-Joseph disease type 2 is a subtype of Machado-Joseph disease (SCA3/MJD) with intermediate severity characterized by an intermediate age of onset, cerebellar ataxia and external progressive ophthalmoplegia, with variable pyramidal and extrapyramidal signs.\" [Orphanet:276241]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:468680:def: \"Infantile glycerol kinase deficiency (GKD) is a severe form of GKD characterized clinically by poor feeding, failure to thrive, salt-wasting dehydration, vomiting, Addisonian pigmentation, hypotonia, and disorders of consciousness. Some patients have complex GKD associated with adrenal hypoplasia congenita and/or Duchenne muscular dystrophy (DMD) with manifestations including intellectual deficit, dysmorphic facial features, abnormal external genitalia, strabismus, seizures, and progressive lethargy.\" [Orphanet:284408]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:469058:name: obsolete rare disease with thoracic aortic aneurysm and aortic dissection\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:469739:def: \"Inherited isolated adrenal insufficiency due to partial CYP11A1 deficiency is a rare, genetic, chronic, primary adrenal insufficiency disorder, due to partial loss-of-function CYP11A1 mutations, characterized by early-onset adrenal insufficiency without associated abnormal external male genitalia. Patients present with signs of adrenal crisis, including electrolite abnormalities, severe weakness, recurrent vomiting and seizures. Ultrasound reveals absent (or very small) adrenal glands.\" [Orphanet:289548]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:471134:def: \"A rare disease caused by compression of the celiac axis by an abnormally shaped arcuate ligament (the part of the diaphragm in which both pillars join in the midline around the aorta). Patients have recurrent abdominal pain, anorexia and weight loss. The pain is epigastric, and diarrhea or constipation may be present as well. Onset of pain will usually, although not always, be after food intake, and may be associated with nausea and emesis. Other symptoms may include lassitude, exercise intolerance and vomiting. Occasionally, a patient may show an abdominal murmur upon auscultation.\" [Orphanet:293208]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:474928:def: \"A syndrome characterized by the association of gastrointestinal dysmotility, peripheral neuropathy, chronic progressive external ophthalmoplegia and leukoencephalopathy.\" [Orphanet:298]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:474975:def: \"Conditions affecting individuals with 46,XX karyotype characterized by atypical development of one or more of the following: the gonads, the internal reproductive structures, the external reproductive/genital structures.\" [NCIT:C127169]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:476764:name: obsolete rare disease with myoclonus as a major feature\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:480327:def: \"A rare multiple congenital anomalies syndrome characterized by mild to severe intellectual disability, a distinctive facial gestalt (blepharophimosis, maxillary hypoplasia, telecanthus, microtia and atresia of the external auditory meatus) as well as skeletal and articular abnormalities (e.g. camptodactyly of the fingers, cutaneous syndactyly, talipes equinovarus, flexion contractures of the proximal interphalangeal joints, hip or elbow subluxation, joint laxity). Affected individuals also present neonatal hypotonia, variable respiratory manifestations, chronic feeding difficulties and gray matter heterotopia.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432, Orphanet:314679]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:480510:synonym: \"rare disease with Cushing syndrome as a major feature\" EXACT []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:480965:def: \"The salt wasting form of classic congenital adrenal hyperplasia due to 21-hydroxylase deficiency (classical 21 OHD CAH) is characterized by virilization of the external genitalia in females, hypocortisolism, precocious pseudopuberty and renal salt loss due to aldosterone deficiency.\" [Orphanet:315306]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:480984:def: \"The simple virilizing form of classical congenital adrenal hyperplasia due to 21-hydroxylase deficiency (classical 21 OHD CAH) is characterized by genital ambiguity and virilization of the external genitalia in females, hypocortisolism and precocious pseudopuberty without salt-wasting.\" [Orphanet:315311]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:483893:name: obsolete non-familial rare disease with dilated cardiomyopathy\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:484939:name: adult-onset chronic progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial myopathy\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:484940:def: \"Adult-onset chronic progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial myopathy is a rare mitochondrial disease characterized by adult onset of progressive external ophthalmoplegia, exercise intolerance, muscle weakness, manifestations of spinocerebellar ataxia (e.g. impaired gait, dysarthria) and mild motor peripheral neuropathy. Respiratory insufficiency has been reported in some cases.\" [Orphanet:329336]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:490382:name: childhood-onset autosomal recessive myopathy with external ophthalmoplegia\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:490383:def: \"A rare, genetic, non-dystrophic myopathy disease characterized by childhood-onset severe external ophthalmoplegia, typically without ptosis, associated with mild, very slowly progressive muscular weakness and atrophy, involving the facial, neck flexor and limb (upper > lower, proximal > distal) muscles. Muscle biopsy shows type 1 fiber uniformity, absent, or abnormally small, type 2A fibers, increased variability of fiber size, internalized nuclei and/or fatty infiltration.\" [Orphanet:363677]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:490398:property_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/childhood_onset_autosomal_recessive_myopathy_with_external_ophthalmoplegia\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:502702:name: obsolete rare disease with malignant hyperthermia\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:510412:name: maternally-inherited progressive external ophthalmoplegia\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:510419:synonym: \"maternally-inherited chronic progressive external ophthalmoplegia\" EXACT [Orphanet:663]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:510428:property_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/mitochondrial_dna_related_progressive_external_ophthalmoplegia\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:511382:comment: Note that the ordo class is specifically for rare diseases, but we broaden to be inclusive of HH1\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:514228:def: \"Androgen insensitivity syndrome (AIS) is a disorder of sex development (DSD) characterized by the presence of female external genitalia, ambiguous genitalia or variable defects in virilization in a 46,XY individual with absent or partial responsiveness to age-appropriate levels of androgens. It comprises two clinical subgroups: complete AIS (CAIS) and partial AIS (PAIS).\" [Orphanet:754]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:514286:def: \"A condition in males that affects sexual development. It is characterized by underdevelopment of the Leydig cells, which are cells in the testes that secrete male sex hormones (androgens) and are important for male sexual development. Individuals with LCH have a typical male genetic make-up (46, XY), but due to lowered levels of androgens, may have a range of genital (reproductive organ) differences. Individuals with LCH may have a small penis (micropenis),the opening of the urethra may be located on the underside of the penis (hypospadias), or the scrotum may be divided into two halves (bifid scrotum). Given these differences in development, the external genitalia may not appear clearly male or female (ambiguous genitalia). Some individuals with LCH can have female external genitalia and small testes that have not descended and are located in the pelvis, abdomen, or groin. This may be referred to as type 1, whereas less severe cases might be called type 2. LCH is inherited in an autosomal recessive manner and is caused by mutations in the LHCGR gene.Although there is no specific treatment or cure for LCH, there may be ways to manage the symptoms. A team of doctors or specialists is often needed to figure out the treatment options for each person.\" [GARD:0003244]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:515059:def: \"The association of auricular abnormalities and cleft lip with or without cleft palate has been described in two siblings. One sibling had postauricular pits, profound myopia, nystagmus and retinal pigment abnormalities. The second sibling was a fetus (gestational age: 23 weeks) with severe cleft lip, cleft palate and external ear abnormalities.\" [Orphanet:77300]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:515634:def: \"A rare genetic neuromuscular disease characterized by early onset of proximal or generalized muscle weakness, external ophthalmoplegia with or without ptosis, and joint contractures. Hypotonia, neonatal respiratory distress necessitating ventilation, and severe dysphagia have also been reported. The disease is of variable severity and non- or slowly progressive. Patients typically remain ambulatory. Muscle biopsy may show predominance of type 1 fibers, marked variability in fiber size, increased internal nuclei, and proliferation of perimysial and endomysial connective tissue.\" [Orphanet:79091]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:516024:def: \"Bickerstaff's brainstem encephalitis (BBE) is a rare post-infectious neurological disease characterized by the association of external ophthalmoplegia, ataxia, lower limb arreflexia, extensor plantar response and disturbance of consciousness (drowsiness, stupor or coma).\" [Orphanet:79138]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:520876:name: macrostomia-preauricular tags-external ophthalmoplegia syndrome\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:520877:def: \"Macrostomia-preauricular tags-external ophthalmoplegia syndrome combines macrostomia or abnormal mouth contour, preauricular tags, uni- or bilateral ptosis and external ophthalmoplegia. It was described in nine members of a Brazilian family. It is a new phenotype belonging to the so-called oculoauriculovertebral spectrum, resulting from a branchial arch anomaly. Transmission is autosomal dominant.\" [Orphanet:83619]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:520889:property_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/macrostomia_preauricular_tags_external_ophthalmoplegia_syndrome\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:520907:synonym: \"perineal hemangioma-external genitalia malformations-lipomyelomeningocele-vesicorenal abnormalities-imperforate anus syndrome\" EXACT []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:526931:def: \"OBSOLETE. 46,XY disorder of sex development due to isolated 17,20-lyase deficiency is a rare disorder of sex development due to reduced 17,20-lyase activity that affects individuals with 46,XY karyotype and is characterized by ambiguous external genitalia, including micropenis, perineal hypospadias, bifid scrotum, cryptorchidism, and a blind vaginal pouch. Blood pressure and electrolytes are normal whilst hormonal investigations show normal basal and stimulated levels of cortisol, and low basal and stimulated androgen levels.\" [Orphanet:90796]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:526952:def: \"OBSOLETE. Primary lipodystrophies represent a heterogeneous group of very rare diseases characterized by a generalized or localized loss of body fat (lipoatrophy).\" [Orphanet:90970]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:531097:def: \"A congenital malformation of the external ear and the most extreme form of microtia characterized by the complete absence of the external ear and auditory canal, conductive hearing loss, attention deficit disorders and delayed language development.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432, Orphanet:93976]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:536165:def: \"Robinow syndrome (RS) is a rare genetic syndrome characterized by limb shortening and abnormalities of the head, face and external genitalia.\" [Orphanet:97360]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:536852:name: obsolete rare disease with odontological manifestation\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:537093:synonym: \"rare disease of cellular proliferation\" EXACT []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:539661:name: obsolete malposition of external canthus\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:540426:name: obsolete rare disease with glaucoma as a major feature\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:550476:def: \"Hearing loss caused by impaired transmission of signals from the external auditory canal or middle ear to the cochlea.\" [NCIT:C27645]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:553413:def: \"The result of pathological changes in the hard tissue of a tooth caused by carious lesions, mechanical factors, or trauma, which render the pulp susceptible to bacterial invasion from the external environment.\" [MESH:D003789]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:553794:name: progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal recessive 5\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:553799:synonym: \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal recessive 5\" EXACT [OMIM:618098]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:553800:synonym: \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia, autosomal recessive 5\" EXACT [OMIM:618098]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:553806:is_a: MONDO:0000090 {source=\"OMIM:618098\"} ! progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:553808:property_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/progressive_external_ophthalmoplegia_with_mitochondrial_dna_deletions_autosomal_recessive_5\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:554591:def: \"Hemochromatosis type 1 (classic) is the most common form of hereditary hemochromatosis (HH), a group of diseases characterized by excessive tissue iron deposition. Due to its incidence (1/200-1/1000), it is not considered as a rare disease, unlike the other subforms of the disease\" [EFO:0006513, https://github.com/EBISPOT/efo/issues/58]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:555142:def: \"Complete androgen insensitivity syndrome (CAIS) is a form of androgen insensitivity syndrome (AIS), a disorder of sex development (DSD), characterized by the presence of female external genitalia in a 46,XY individual with normal testis development but undescended testes and unresponsiveness to age-appropriate levels of androgens.\" [Orphanet:99429]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:558033:comment: This term was created for characterizing a disease via axiom. We do not maintain axioms to indicate that a disease is rare/not-rare. Please use the Mondo rare disease subset to identify rare diseases. (https://mondo.readthedocs.io/en/latest/editors-guide/rare-disease-subset/)\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:558042:comment: This term was created for characterizing a disease via axiom. We do not maintain axioms to indicate that a disease is rare/not-rare. Please use the Mondo rare disease subset to identify rare diseases. (https://mondo.readthedocs.io/en/latest/editors-guide/rare-disease-subset/)\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:558050:comment: This term was created for characterizing a disease via axiom. We do not maintain axioms to indicate that a disease is rare/not-rare. Please use the Mondo rare disease subset to identify rare diseases. (https://mondo.readthedocs.io/en/latest/editors-guide/rare-disease-subset/)\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:558803:def: \"Damage inflicted on the body as the direct or indirect result of an external force, with or without disruption of structural continuity.\" [NCIT:C3671]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:559223:name: obsolete rare disease\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:559225:synonym: \"rare disease\" EXACT [MONDO:patterns/rare]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:559226:synonym: \"rare disease or disorder\" EXACT [MONDO:patterns/rare]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:559227:synonym: \"rare diseases\" EXACT []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:560044:name: external ear neoplasm\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:560045:def: \"A neoplasm (disease) that involves the external ear.\" [MONDO:patterns/location]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:560046:synonym: \"external ear neoplasm (disease)\" EXACT [MONDO:patterns/location]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:560047:synonym: \"external Ear tumor\" EXACT [NCIT:C4652]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:560048:synonym: \"external ear tumor\" EXACT [MONDO:patterns/neoplasm, NCIT:C4652]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:560049:synonym: \"external Ear tumour\" EXACT OMO:0003005 []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:560050:synonym: \"external ear tumour\" EXACT OMO:0003005 []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:560051:synonym: \"neoplasm of external Ear\" EXACT [NCIT:C4652]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:560052:synonym: \"neoplasm of external ear\" EXACT [MONDO:patterns/neoplasm, NCIT:C4652]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:560053:synonym: \"neoplasm of the external Ear\" EXACT [NCIT:C4652]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:560054:synonym: \"tumor of external Ear\" EXACT [NCIT:C4652]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:560055:synonym: \"tumor of external ear\" EXACT [MONDO:patterns/neoplasm, NCIT:C4652]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:560056:synonym: \"tumor of the external Ear\" EXACT [NCIT:C4652]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:560057:synonym: \"tumour of external Ear\" EXACT OMO:0003005 []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:560058:synonym: \"tumour of external ear\" EXACT OMO:0003005 []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:560059:synonym: \"tumour of the external Ear\" EXACT OMO:0003005 []\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:560064:is_a: MONDO:0002776 {source=\"NCIT:C4652\"} ! external ear disorder\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:563376:name: polyp of external auditory canal\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:563377:def: \"A polyp that involves the external acoustic meatus.\" [MONDO:patterns/location]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:563378:synonym: \"external acoustic meatus polyp\" EXACT [MONDO:patterns/location]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:563379:synonym: \"external auditory canal polyp\" EXACT [NCIT:C4366]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:563380:synonym: \"external Ear polyp\" EXACT [NCIT:C4366]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:563381:synonym: \"polyp of the external auditory canal\" EXACT [NCIT:C4366]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:563387:is_a: MONDO:0021235 {source=\"MONDO:Redundant\", source=\"NCIT:C4366/inferred\"} ! external ear neoplasm\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:568242:def: \"A viral or bacterial infection that affects the external, middle, or inner ear. It may follow an upper respiratory infection. Signs and symptoms include pain, ear discharge, ear fullness, hearing loss, vertigo, nausea, and vomiting.\" [NCIT:C27193]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:571844:comment: This term was found in the globalgenes.org rare disease list, but no information could be found about it.\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:571927:comment: This term was found in the globalgenes.org rare disease list, but no information could be found about it.\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:576161:comment: This term was found in the globalgenes.org rare disease list, but no information could be found about it.\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:580160:name: external hirudiniasis\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:580161:def: \"The attachment of leeches to the skin. After the leeches drop off, bleeding may continue as a result of the action of hirudin. Bites may become infected or ulcerate.\" [https://medical-dictionary.thefreedictionary.com/external+hirudiniasis]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:581249:def: \"A circadian sleep disorder in which the individual's internal body clock is delayed with respect to the external day/night cycle.\" [https://www.circadiansleepdisorders.org/defs.php#defDSPS]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:581323:def: \"A circadian sleep disorder that occurs when work schedules force people to be awake when their circadian rhythms dictate that they should be sleeping. It is classified as a Circadian Rhythm Disorder (CRD) and is extrinsic, i.e. caused by external behavioral factors.\" [https://www.circadiansleepdisorders.org/defs.php#defSWD]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:583283:name: progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant 1\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:583284:def: \"Any autosomal dominant progressive external ophthalmoplegia in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the POLG gene.\" [MONDO:patterns/disease_series_by_gene]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:583288:synonym: \"autosomal dominant progressive external ophthalmoplegia caused by mutation in POLG\" EXACT [MONDO:design_pattern]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:583290:synonym: \"POLG autosomal dominant progressive external ophthalmoplegia\" EXACT [MONDO:design_pattern, MONDO:patterns/disease_series_by_gene]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:583291:synonym: \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant 1\" EXACT [OMIM:157640]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:583292:synonym: \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia, autosomal dominant 1\" EXACT [OMIM:157640]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:583298:is_a: MONDO:0008003 {source=\"MONDO:Redundant\"} ! autosomal dominant progressive external ophthalmoplegia\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:583299:intersection_of: MONDO:0008003 ! autosomal dominant progressive external ophthalmoplegia\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:592260:name: obsolete rare disease with Cushing syndrome as a major feature\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:599286:name: ophthalmoplegia, external, with rib and vertebral anomalies\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:599294:property_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/ophthalmoplegia_external_with_rib_and_vertebral_anomalies\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:614042:def: \"Choanal atresia-athelia-hypothyroidism-delayed puberty-short stature syndrome is an autosomal dominant disorder characterized by choanal atresia, athelia or hypoplastic nipples, branchial sinus abnormalities, neck pits, lacrimal duct anomalies, hearing loss, external ear malformations, and thyroid abnormalities.\" [OMIM:620186]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:622850:def: \"Penetrating and non-penetrating injuries to the spinal cord resulting from traumatic external forces (e.g., WOUNDS, GUNSHOT; WHIPLASH INJURIES; etc.).\" [MESH:D013119]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:623111:def: \"Harm or hurt to the ankle or ankle joint usually inflicted by an external source.\" [MESH:D016512]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:627406:name: X-linked external auditory canal atresia-dilated internal auditory canal-facial dysmorphism syndrome\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:640792:def: \"46,XX testicular disorder of sex development (46,XX testicular DSD) is characterized by male external genitalia, ranging from normal to ambiguous with associated testosterone deficiency.\" [Orphanet:393]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:648490:def: \"An anterior midline defect with variable expression involving the infraumbilical abdominal wall including the pelvis, urinary tract, and external genitalia.\" [OMIM:600057]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:648652:def: \"An abscess contained between the internal and external anal sphincters.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2658-1136, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2825-0621]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:651147:def: \"A central nervous system dysperception disorder characterized by the perception of a sound not justified by any internal or external vibration, lasting at least 5 minutes and occurring more than once a week, arising from maladaptive neuroplasticity secondary to an organic cochlear peripheral lesion, and classifiable as positive auditory hallucinosis in the absence of delusional attitudes or behaviors.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4142-7153, https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2955-4640, PMID:35645199]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:652216:def: \"A rare disease due to a severely impaired central autonomic control of breathing and dysfunction of the autonomous nervous system. The incidence is estimated to be at 1 of 200 000 livebirths. A heterozygous mutation of PHOX-2B gene is found in 90% of the patients. Association with a Hirschsprung's disease is observed in 16% of the cases. Despite a high mortality rate and a lifelong dependence to mechanical ventilation, the long-term outcome of CCHS should be ultimately improved by multidisciplinary and coordinated follow-up of the patients.\" [Orphanet:661]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:653348:def: \"A botryomycosis that involves internal organs such as lungs, liver, or brain. It is a rare disease and has been described mainly in patients with underlying diseases such as diabetes mellitus, cystic fibrosis, or HIV infection. It is most commonly affecting the lungs, although involvement of other organs including liver, spleen, kidney, and brain has also been described.\" [https://www.uptodate.com/contents/botryomycosis, PMID:9524833]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:659219:def: \"A myopathy that is characterized by muscle breakdown (rhabdomyolysis), heat and exertion-related muscle pain (myalgia) and cramping symptoms, severe muscle pain, sudden elevation and subsequent fall of serum creatine phosphokinase levels and products of muscle breakdown in the urine (myoglobinuria). Associated with RYR1 variations. Rhabdomyolysis is associated with a range of external triggers, including strenuous exercise beyond the limit of fatigue, heat stress, illicit drug or alcohol abuse, use of supplements or certain medications, recent viral illness or muscle trauma.\" [DOID:0080992]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:668387:name: progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial dna deletions, autosomal recessive 6\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:668394:is_a: MONDO:0000090 {source=\"OMIM:620647\"} ! progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.obo:668396:property_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/progressive_external_ophthalmoplegia_with_mitochondrial_dna_deletions_autosomal_recessive_6\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:20619:      \"lbl\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:20625:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mtDNA deletions\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:20879:          \"val\" : \"Auriculo-condylar syndrome (ACS) presents with bilateral external ear malformations ('question mark' ears), mandibular condyle hypoplasia, microstomia, micrognathia, microglossia and facial asymmetry. Additional manifestations include hypotonia, ptosis, cleft palate, puffy cheeks, developmental delay, impaired hearing and respiratory distress.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:25207:          \"val\" : \"Fungus infection of the external ear, usually by aspergillus species\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:25212:          \"val\" : \"external ear fungal infectious disease\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:54589:      \"lbl\" : \"external ear lipoma\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:54593:          \"val\" : \"A benign adipose tissue neoplasm of the external ear.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:54598:          \"val\" : \"external Ear lipoma\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:54602:          \"val\" : \"external ear lipoma\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:54606:          \"val\" : \"lipoma of external Ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:54610:          \"val\" : \"lipoma of external ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:54614:          \"val\" : \"lipoma of the external Ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:54618:          \"val\" : \"lipoma of the external auditory meatus\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:54621:          \"val\" : \"lipoma of the external ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:54639:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/external_ear_lipoma\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:55456:          \"val\" : \"A contagious viral infection caused by the mumps virus. Symptoms include swollen and tender parotid glands, fever, muscle aches and fatigue. Due to vaccination programs, mumps has become a rare disease.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:58649:          \"val\" : \"An otitis externa which involves infection of the external ear that has spread to involve the skull bone containing part of the ear canal, the middle ear, and the inner ear. It is caused by the bacteria Pseudomonas. This is common in people with weakened immune systems and in older people with diabetes.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:93197:          \"val\" : \"Resorption of calcified dental tissue, involving demineralization due to reversal of the cation exchange and lacunar resorption by osteoclasts. There are two types: external (as a result of tooth pathology) and internal (apparently initiated by a peculiar inflammatory hyperplasia of the pulp). (From Jablonski, Dictionary of Dentistry, 1992, p676)\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:103784:          \"val\" : \"A male infertility disorder caused by conditions external to the testis, such as hormonal imbalances, reproductive tract obstructions, or systemic illness.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:108339:          \"val\" : \"A type of defective gonadal development in patients with a wide spectrum of chromosomal mosaic variants. Their karyotypes are of partial sex chromosome monosomy resulting from an absence or an abnormal second sex chromosome (X or Y). Karyotypes include 45,X/46,xx; 45,X/46,xx/47,xxx; 46,xxp-; 45,X/46,xy; 45,X/47,xyy; 46,xypi; etc. The spectrum of phenotypes may range from phenotypic female to phenotypic male including variations in gonads and internal and external genitalia, depending on the ratio in each gonad of 45,X primordial germ cells to those with normal 46,xx or 46,xy constitution.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:109206:      \"lbl\" : \"external pathological resorption\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:109222:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/external_pathological_resorption\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:115934:          \"val\" : \"A category of psychiatric disorders which are characterized by physical or psychological symptoms that are intentionally produced in order to assume the sick role; there is no external incentive for the behavior, such as economic gain or avoiding legal responsibility, and the person is unaware of any self-motivating factors.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:122895:          \"val\" : \"Papilloma's are benign epithelial neoplasms that produce visible warty projections from epithelial surfaces. Papilloma's of the urethra typically occur just within or on the external meatus. - 2003\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:128408:          \"val\" : \"An illusion of movement, either of the external world revolving around the individual or of the individual revolving in space. Vertigo may be associated with disorders of the inner ear (ear, inner); vestibular nerve; brainstem; or cerebral cortex. Lesions in the temporal lobe and parietal lobe may be associated with focal seizures that may feature vertigo as an ictal manifestation. (From Adams et al., Principles of Neurology, 6th ed, pp300-1)\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:155804:          \"val\" : \"A rare condition characterized by the unequivocal presence of both testicular and ovarian tissues in an individual. It is usually manifested with ambiguous external genitalia.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:156108:      \"lbl\" : \"external ear disorder\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:156112:          \"val\" : \"A disease involving the external ear.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:156118:          \"val\" : \"disease of external ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:156122:          \"val\" : \"disease or disorder of external ear\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:156125:          \"val\" : \"disorder of external ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:156129:          \"val\" : \"external ear disease\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:156133:          \"val\" : \"external ear disease or disorder\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:156137:          \"val\" : \"external ear disorder\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:156183:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/external_ear_disease\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:157741:          \"val\" : \"A benign epithelial neoplasm arising from the apocrine sweat glands. Representative examples include tubular apocrine adenoma and external auditory canal ceruminous adenoma.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:165804:      \"lbl\" : \"external ear basal cell carcinoma\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:165808:          \"val\" : \"A basal cell carcinoma that arises from the skin of the external ear.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:165814:          \"val\" : \"basal cell carcinoma of external Ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:165818:          \"val\" : \"basal cell carcinoma of the external Ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:165822:          \"val\" : \"basal cell carcinoma of the external ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:165826:          \"val\" : \"basal cell external ear carcinoma\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:165830:          \"val\" : \"external Ear basal cell carcinoma\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:165834:          \"val\" : \"external ear skin basal cell carcinoma\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:165838:          \"val\" : \"skin basal cell carcinoma of external ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:165854:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/external_ear_basal_cell_carcinoma\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:165871:      \"lbl\" : \"external ear carcinoma\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:165875:          \"val\" : \"A carcinoma that arises from epithelial cells of the external ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:165880:          \"val\" : \"carcinoma of external Ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:165884:          \"val\" : \"carcinoma of external ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:165888:          \"val\" : \"carcinoma of the external Ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:165892:          \"val\" : \"carcinoma of the external ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:165896:          \"val\" : \"external Ear carcinoma\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:165900:          \"val\" : \"external ear carcinoma\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:165914:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/external_ear_carcinoma\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:184489:          \"val\" : \"A malignant neoplasm that affects the ear. Representative examples include ceruminous adenocarcinoma and squamous cell carcinoma of the external ear and adenocarcinoma of the middle ear.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:196668:      \"lbl\" : \"external ear squamous cell carcinoma\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:196672:          \"val\" : \"A squamous cell carcinoma that arises from the skin of the external ear.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:196678:          \"val\" : \"epidermoid carcinoma of external Ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:196682:          \"val\" : \"epidermoid carcinoma of the external Ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:196686:          \"val\" : \"epidermoid carcinoma of the external ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:196690:          \"val\" : \"external Ear epidermoid carcinoma\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:196694:          \"val\" : \"external Ear squamous cell carcinoma\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:196698:          \"val\" : \"external ear squamous cell carcinoma\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:196702:          \"val\" : \"squamous cell carcinoma of external Ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:196706:          \"val\" : \"squamous cell carcinoma of the external Ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:196722:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/external_ear_squamous_cell_carcinoma\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:200603:      \"lbl\" : \"external ear cancer\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:200607:          \"val\" : \"A malignant neoplasm involving the external ear.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:200612:          \"val\" : \"cancer of external ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:200616:          \"val\" : \"external ear cancer\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:200620:          \"val\" : \"malignant external Ear neoplasm\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:200624:          \"val\" : \"malignant external Ear tumor\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:200629:          \"val\" : \"malignant external Ear tumour\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:200632:          \"val\" : \"malignant external ear neoplasm\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:200636:          \"val\" : \"malignant neoplasm of external Ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:200640:          \"val\" : \"malignant neoplasm of external ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:200644:          \"val\" : \"malignant neoplasm of the external Ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:200648:          \"val\" : \"malignant neoplasm of the external ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:200652:          \"val\" : \"malignant tumor of external Ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:200656:          \"val\" : \"malignant tumor of the external Ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:200661:          \"val\" : \"malignant tumour of external Ear\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:200665:          \"val\" : \"malignant tumour of the external Ear\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:218749:          \"val\" : \"An infiltrating adenocarcinoma derived from ceruminous glands in the external auditory canal.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:239830:          \"val\" : \"A benign epithelial neoplasm derived from ceruminous glands in the external auditory canal. It presents as a gray mass covered by skin. It is characterized by a proliferation of glands composed of cells with abundant eosinophilic and granular cytoplasm.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:239846:          \"val\" : \"ceruminous adenoma of external auditory canal\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:239850:          \"val\" : \"ceruminous adenoma of the external auditory canal\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:239854:          \"val\" : \"external auditory canal ceruminous adenoma\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:240052:          \"val\" : \"Diseases of the ninth cranial (glossopharyngeal) nerve or its nuclei in the medulla. The nerve may be injured by diseases affecting the lower brain stem, floor of the posterior fossa, jugular foramen, or the nerve's extracranial course. Clinical manifestations include loss of sensation from the pharynx, decreased salivation, and syncope. Glossopharyngeal neuralgia refers to a condition that features recurrent unilateral sharp pain in the tongue, angle of the jaw, external auditory meatus and throat that may be associated with syncope. Episodes may be triggered by cough, sneeze, swallowing, or pressure on the tragus of the ear. (Adams et al., Principles of Neurology, 6th ed, p1390)\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:260486:          \"val\" : \"Death of tissue due to external pressure.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:270123:          \"val\" : \"external Ear infection\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:273888:          \"val\" : \"Thrombosed external haemorrhoids\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:273891:          \"val\" : \"external thrombosed hemorrhoids\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:295442:      \"lbl\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:295452:          \"val\" : \"chronic progressive external ophthalmoplegia [ambiguous]\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:295455:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:295459:          \"val\" : \"chronic progressive external ophthalmoplegia\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:295490:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/chronic_progressive_external_ophthalmoplegia\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:322758:          \"val\" : \"A sexually transmitted papillary growth caused by the human papillomavirus. It usually arises in the skin and mucous membranes of the perianal region and external genitalia.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:331588:          \"val\" : \"An acute, localized swelling of the eyelid that may be external or internal and usually is a pyogenic (typically staphylococcal) infection or abscess.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:374361:      \"lbl\" : \"cholesteatoma of external ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:374365:          \"val\" : \"A cholesteatoma (disease) that involves the external ear.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:374371:          \"val\" : \"cholesteatoma (disease) of external ear\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:374374:          \"val\" : \"external ear cholesteatoma (disease)\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:374394:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/cholesteatoma_of_external_ear\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:386647:          \"val\" : \"A rare cutaneous tumor of eccrine sweat gland origin. It is most commonly found on the extremities and is usually benign. There is no indication that heredity or external agents cause these tumors.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:398983:          \"val\" : \"Narrowing or occlusion of the renal artery or arteries. It is due usually to atherosclerosis; fibromuscular dysplasia; thrombosis; embolism, or external pressure. The reduced renal perfusion can lead to renovascular hypertension (hypertension, renovascular).\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:400142:          \"val\" : \"Overproduction of parathyroid hormone in response to influence external to the parathyroid glands.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:400281:          \"val\" : \"A condition with a clinical picture similar to that of Parkinson disease, but which is caused by external factors, including medication.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:403627:          \"val\" : \"An acute neurological disorder characterized by the triad of ophthalmoplegia, ataxia, and disturbances of mental activity or consciousness. Eye movement abnormalities include nystagmus, external rectus palsies, and reduced conjugate gaze. thiamine deficiency and chronic alcoholism are associated conditions. Pathologic features include periventricular petechial hemorrhages and neuropil breakdown in the diencephalon and brainstem. Chronic thiamine deficiency may lead to korsakoff syndrome. (Adams et al., Principles of Neurology, 6th ed, pp1139-42; Davis & Robertson, Textbook of Neuropathology, 2nd ed, pp452-3)\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:413518:          \"val\" : \"Distal arthrogryposis type 5 is an inherited developmental defect syndrome characterized by multiple congenital contractures of limbs, without primary neurologic and/or muscle disease that affects limb function, and ocular anomalies (ptosis, external ophtalmoplegia and/or strabismus). Intelligence is normal.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:414410:      \"lbl\" : \"atresia of external auditory canal and conductive deafness\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:414416:          \"val\" : \"atresia of external auditory canal and conductive deafness\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:414430:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/atresia_of_external_auditory_canal_and_conductive_deafness\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:415151:          \"val\" : \"Spinocerebellar ataxia type 3 (SCA3), also known as Machado-Joseph disease, is the most common subtype of type 1 autosomal dominant cerebellar ataxia (ADCA type 1), a neurodegenerative disorder, and is characterized by ataxia, external progressive ophthalmoplegia, and other neurological manifestations.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:425804:          \"val\" : \"Autosomal dominant popliteal pterygium syndrome (AD-PPS) is a rare genetic malformative disorder characterized by cleft lip, with or without cleft palate, contractures of the lower extremities, abnormal external genitalia, syndactyly of fingers and/or toes, and a pyramidal skin fold over the hallux nail.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:431637:          \"val\" : \"Gorham-Stout disease (GSD) is a rare disease of massive osteolysis associated with proliferation and dilation of lymphatic vessels. GSD may affect any bone in the body and can be monostotic or polyostotic. Symptoms at presentation are dependent upon the location(s) of the disease; the most common symptom is localized pain. The disease may be discovered after a pathological fracture.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:432184:          \"val\" : \"Deafness-ear malformation-facial palsy syndrome is characterized by profound conductive deafness due to stapedial abnormalities associated with variable malformations of the external ears and facial paralysis. It has been described in three sibs and their mother. Inheritance is autosomal dominant.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:437188:          \"val\" : \"exostoses of external auditory canal\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:437292:          \"val\" : \"A congenital disorder characterized by malformations of the external ear, which is caused by the first and second branchial arch dysplasia or the first branchial groove insufficiency in the embryonic stage.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:443371:      \"lbl\" : \"external auditory canal atresia-vertical talus-hypertelorism syndrome\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:443388:          \"val\" : \"external auditory canal, bilateral atresia of, with congenital vertical talus\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:443391:          \"val\" : \"inherited congenital bilateral atresia of the external auditory canal, congenital bilateral vertical talus and increased interocular distance\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:443407:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/external_auditory_canal_atresia_vertical_talus_hypertelorism_syndrome\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:443410:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/external_auditory_canal_bilateral_atresia_of_with_congenital_vertical_talus\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:451593:          \"val\" : \"Oculoauriculovertebral spectrum (OAVS) with radial defects is a rare branchial arches and limb primordia development disorder characterized by variable degrees of uni- or bilateral craniofacial malformation and radial defects that result in extremely variable phenotypic manifestations. Characteristic features include low postnatal weight, short stature, vertebral defects, hearing loss, and facial dysmorphism (incl. facial asymmetry, external, middle, and inner ear malformations, orofacial clefts, and mandibular hypoplasia). These features are invariably associated with radial defects, such as preaxial polydactyly, thumb and/or radius hypoplasia/agenesis, or triphalangeal thumb. Cardiac, pulmonary, renal, and central nervous system involvement has also been reported.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:459795:          \"val\" : \"radial ray defects, hearing impairment, external ophthalmoplegia, and thrombocytopenia\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:459811:          \"val\" : \"radial Ray defects, hearing impairment, external ophthalmoplegia, and thrombocytopenia\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:459868:          \"val\" : \"Johnson neuroectodermal syndrome is characterized by alopecia, anosmia or hyposmia, conductive deafness with malformed ears and microtia and/or atresia of the external auditory canal, and hypogonadotropic hypogonadism.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:467741:          \"val\" : \"Nager syndrome, also called Nager acrofacial dysostosis (NAFD) is a congenital malformation syndrome characterized by mandibulofacial dystosis (malar hypoplasia, micrognathia, external ear malformations) and variable preaxial limb defects.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:471764:      \"lbl\" : \"autosomal dominant progressive external ophthalmoplegia\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:471768:          \"val\" : \"Autosomal dominant form of progressive external ophthalmoplegia.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:471778:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant type 1\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:471782:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia, autosomal dominant\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:471791:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant 1\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:471807:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/progressive_external_ophthalmoplegia_with_mitochondrial_dna_deletions_autosomal_dominant_1\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:472787:          \"val\" : \"A condition that affects the skin, hair, mucosa (areas ofthe body that are lined with mucus), gums (gingiva), eyes, nose and lungs. Symptoms typically begin in infancy and may include development of cataracts (clouding of the eye lens); blindness; hair loss (alopecia); abnormal changes to the perineum (the area between the anus and external genitalia); and small, skin-colored bumps (keratosis pilaris). Terminal lung disease has also been reported. The cause of HMD is thought to be an abnormality in desmosomes and gap junctions, which are structures involved in cell-to-cell contact. HMD typically follows autosomal dominant inheritance, but has occurred sporadically (in an individual who has no family history of the condition). Treatment typically focuses on individual symptoms of the condition.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:480565:          \"val\" : \"external ophthalmoplegia, nonprogressive, congenital hereditary\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:496640:          \"val\" : \"Radio-renal syndrome is a rare developmental defect during embryogenesis characterized by variable upper limb reduction defects and renal anomalies. Patients typically present absence/hypoplasia of digits, radii and/or ulnae, short stature and mild external ear malformation, as well as kidney agenesis or ectopia. There have been no further descriptions in the literature since 1983.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:498452:          \"val\" : \"Autosomal dominant Robinow syndrome (DRS) is the more common type of Robinow syndrome (RS) characterized by mild to moderate limb shortening and abnormalities of the head, face and external genitalia.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:518662:          \"val\" : \"microcephaly, IUGR, hypertelorism, ptosis, iris coloboma, hooked nose, external ear dysplasia, psychomotor retardation\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:519384:          \"val\" : \"Ablepharon macrostomia syndrome is an extremely rare multiple congenital malformation syndrome characterized by the association of ablepharon, macrostomia, abnormal external ears, syndactyly of the hands and feet, skin findings (such as dry and coarse skin or redundant folds of skin), absent or sparse hair, genital malformations and developmental delay (in 2/3 of cases). Other reported manifestations include malar hypoplasia, absent or hypoplastic nipples, umbilical abnormalities and growth retardation. It is a mainly sporadic disorder, although a few familial cases having been reported, and it displays significant clinical overlap with Fraser syndrome.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:520921:          \"val\" : \"Acrocraniofacial dysostosis is a very rare form of acrofacial dyosotosis, reported in two sisters to date, characterized by short stature, acrocephaly, ocular hypertelorism, ptosis of eyelids, ocular proptosis, downslanting palpebral fissures, high nasal bridge, anteverted nostrils, short philtrum, cleft palate, micrognathia, abnormal external ears, preauricular pits, mixed hearing loss, bulbous digits, metatarsus varus, pectus excavatum and various radiological abnormalities. Features of this syndrome were reported to overlap with otopalatodigital syndrome types 1 and 2. There have been no further descriptions in the literature since 1988.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:522026:          \"val\" : \"A type of arthrogryposis characterized by congenital cleft palate, microcephaly, craniostenosis and arthrogryposis (limitation of extension of elbows, flexed adducted thumbs, camptodactyly and clubfeet). Additional features include facial dysmorphism (\\\"myopathic\\\" stiff face, antimongoloid slanting, external ophthalmoplegia, telecanthus, low-set large malrotated ears, open mouth, mierogenia and high arched palate). Velopharyngeal insufficiency with difficulties in swallowing, increased secretion of the nose and throat, prominent occiput, generalized muscular hypotonia with mild cyanosis and no spontaneous movements, seizures, torticollis, areflexia, intellectual disability, hypertrichosis of the lower extremities, and scleredema (in the first days of life) are also observed. The disease often leads to early death. Transmission is autosomal recessive. No new cases of adducted thumbs-arthrogryposis, Christian type have been described since 1983.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:537687:          \"val\" : \"Cereballar ataxia - ectodermal dysplasia is a very rare disease, characterized by hypodontia and sparse hair in combination with cerebellar ataxia and normal intelligence. Imaging demonstrates a cerebellar atrophy.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:541745:          \"val\" : \"Verloove Vanhorick-Brubakk syndrome is a multiple congenital anomalies/dysmorphic syndrome characterized by multiple skeletal malformations (short femora and humeri, bilateral absence of metatarsal and metacarpal bone in hands and feet, bilateral partial syndactyly of fingers and toes or oligopolysyndactyly, deformed lumbosacral spine), congenital heart disease (truncus arteriosus), lung and urogenital malformations (bilateral bilobar lungs, horseshoe kidney, cryptorchidism), and facial malformations (bilateral cleft lip and palate, micrognathia, small, low-set ears without external meatus). It is lethal in the neonatal period. There have been no further descriptions in the literature since 1981.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:548314:      \"lbl\" : \"conductive deafness-malformed external ear syndrome\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:548324:          \"val\" : \"conductive hearing loss-malformed external ear syndrome\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:548332:          \"val\" : \"conductive deafness - malformed external ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:548336:          \"val\" : \"conductive deafness with malformed external ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:548344:          \"val\" : \"deafness, conductive, with malformed external EAR\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:548365:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/deafness_conductive_with_malformed_external_ear\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:548389:          \"val\" : \"Conductive deafness-ptosis-skeletal anomalies syndrome is a rare, genetic ectodermal dysplasia syndrome characterized by conductive hearing loss due to atresia of the external auditory canal and the middle ear complicated by chronic infection, ptosis and skeletal anomalies (internal rotation of hips, dislocation of the radial heads and fifth finger clinodactyly). In addition, a thin, pinched nose, delayed hair growth and dysplastic teeth are associated. There have been no further descriptions in the literature since 1978.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:597454:      \"lbl\" : \"congenital multicore myopathy with external ophthalmoplegia\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:597470:          \"val\" : \"minicore myopathy with external ophthalmoplegia\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:597476:          \"val\" : \"multicore myopathy with external ophthalmoplegia\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:597480:          \"val\" : \"multiminicore disease with external ophthalmoplegia\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:597483:          \"val\" : \"multiminicore myopathy multicore myopathy with external ophthalmoplegia\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:597505:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/congenital_multicore_myopathy_with_external_ophthalmoplegia\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:603134:      \"lbl\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal recessive 1\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:603138:          \"val\" : \"Any autosomal recessive progressive external ophthalmoplegia in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the POLG gene.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:603144:          \"val\" : \"POLG autosomal recessive progressive external ophthalmoplegia\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:603148:          \"val\" : \"autosomal recessive progressive external ophthalmoplegia caused by mutation in POLG\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:603152:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal recessive 1\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:603156:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal recessive type 1\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:603169:          \"val\" : \"autosomal recessive progressive external ophthalmoplegia\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:603173:          \"val\" : \"cerebellar ataxia infantile with progressive external ophthalmoplegia\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:603177:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with cerebellar ataxia infantile\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:603181:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia, autosomal recessive 1\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:603196:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/progressive_external_ophthalmoplegia_with_mitochondrial_dna_deletions_autosomal_recessive_1\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:603199:          \"val\" : \"https://rarediseases.info.nih.gov/diseases/1191/progressive-external-ophthalmoplegia-autosomal-recessive-1\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:604388:          \"val\" : \"A rare, genetic intellectual disability syndrome characterized by macrocephaly, hypotonia, dysmorphic facial features (wide forehead, ptosis, downslanting palpebral fissures, enlarged and calcified external ears, large jaw), sparse body hair, tall stature, and intellectual disability. Hearing loss, insulin-resistant diabetes, and progressive distal muscle wasting (leading to joint contractures) have also been reported in adulthood. Rare manifestations include behavioral abnormalities (aggression and restlessness), hypothyroidism, cerebral calcification, ataxia, and peripheral neuropathy.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:617499:          \"val\" : \"Ulbright-Hodes syndrome is characterized by renal dysplasia, growth retardation, phocomelia or mesomelia, radiohumeral fusion, rib abnormalities, anomalies of the external genitalia and a potter-like facies. The syndrome has been described in three infants (one pair of sibs and an unrelated case), all of whom died shortly after birth from respiratory distress resulting from pulmonary hypoplasia and oligohydramnios caused by renal dysplasia. The mode of transmission appears to be autosomal recessive.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:619918:          \"val\" : \"Autosomal recessive Robinow syndrome (RRS) is the less common type of Robinow syndrome (RS) characterized by short-limb dwarfism, costovertebral segmentation defects and abnormalities of the head, face and external genitalia.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:625149:          \"val\" : \"Spondylocostal dysostosis-anal and genitourinary malformations syndrome is characterized by the association of spondylocostal dysostosis with anal and genitourinary malformations (anal atresia and agenesis of external and internal genitalia). To date, only four cases have been described in the literature. Autosomal recessive inheritance has been suggested.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:633528:          \"val\" : \"visceral myopathy-familial external ophthalmoplegia syndrome\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:633532:          \"val\" : \"familial visceral myopathy with external ophthalmoplegia\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:633536:          \"val\" : \"intestinal pseudoobstruction with external ophthalmoplegia\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:633542:          \"val\" : \"visceral myopathy - familial external ophthalmoplegia\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:633546:          \"val\" : \"visceral myopathy, familial, with external ophthalmoplegia\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:633568:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/visceral_myopathy_familial_with_external_ophthalmoplegia\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:674638:      \"lbl\" : \"ophthalmoplegia, external, and myopia\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:674648:          \"val\" : \"ophthalmoplegia, external, and myopia\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:674665:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/ophthalmoplegia_external_and_myopia\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:674930:          \"val\" : \"A rare neurodevelopmental disorder in the ciliopathy group that is lethal in males and characterized by variable anomalies including external malformations (craniofacial and digital), and possible involvement of the central nervous system (CNS) and of viscera (kidneys, pancreas and ovaries) in females.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:677243:          \"val\" : \"progressive basal ganglion dysfunction, mental and growth retardation, external ophthalmoplegia, postnatal microcephaly and deafness\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:679783:          \"val\" : \"46,XY complete gonadal dysgenesis (46,XY CGD) is a disorder of sex development (DSD) associated with anomalies in gonadal development that result in the presence of female external and internal genitalia despite the 46,XY karyotype.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:681077:          \"val\" : \"Kearns-Sayre syndrome (KSS) is a mitochondrial disease characterized by progressive external ophthalmoplegia (PEO), pigmentary retinitis and an onset before the age of 20 years. Common additional features include deafness, cerebellar ataxia and heart block.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:681114:          \"val\" : \"chronic progressive external ophthalmoplegia with myopathy\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:681130:          \"val\" : \"ophthalmoplegia, progressive external, with ragged red fibers\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:681135:          \"val\" : \"ophthalmoplegia, progressive external, with ragged red fibres\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:681138:          \"val\" : \"ophthalmoplegia, progressive external, with ragged-Red fibers\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:681142:          \"val\" : \"ophthalmoplegia, progressive external, with ragged-Red fibres\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:681644:          \"val\" : \"Lethal infantile mitochondrial myopathy is a rare mitochondrial oxidative phosphorylation disorder characterized by progressive generalized hypotonia, progressive external ophthalmoplegia and severe lactic acidosis, which results in early fatality (days to months after birth). Patients may present with lethargy and areflexia and may associate additional features, such as cardiomyopathy, renal dysfunction, liver involvement and seizures.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:683226:          \"val\" : \"Chondrodysplasia - disorder of sex development is an extremely rare disorder of sex development, reported in only two siblings (one terminated in pregnancy) to date, characterized by the clinical features of 46,XY complete gonadal dysgenesis (normal external female genitalia, lack of pubertal development, primary amenorrhea, and hypergonadotrophic hypogonadism) in association with severe dwarfism with generalized chondrodysplasia (bell-shaped thorax, micromelia, brachydactyly). Other reported features in the live sibling included eye anomalies (hypoplastic irides, myopia, coloboma of optic disks), dysmorphic features (deep-set eyes, upslanting palpebral fissures, puffy eyelids, large ears and mouth, mild prognathism), muscular hypoplasia, mild intellectual deficiency and severe microcephaly with cerebellar vermis hypoplasia. An autosomal recessive inheritance has been suggested.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:688586:          \"val\" : \"Waters-West syndrome is characterized by the association of lethal non-spherocytic, non-immune hemolytic anemia with abnormalities of the external genitalia (micropenis and hypospadias), flat occiput, dimpled earlobes, deep plantar creases, and increased space between the first and second toes. It has been described only once in two brothers who died a few hours after birth. The second-born infant had massive ascites and hepatosplenomegaly. The mother had two spontaneous abortions (at 6 and 12 weeks gestation) but gave birth to a normal girl, suggesting an autosomal or X-linked recessive mode of inheritance. Although the parents were not known to be consanguineous, they shared a French-Canadian and American Indian ethnic origin.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:689695:          \"val\" : \"Loose anagen syndrome is a rare benign hair disorder affecting predominantly blond females in childhood and characterized by the presence of hair that can be easily and painlessly pulled out. Most of the hair is in the anagen phase and lacks an external epithelial sheath. Hair grows back quickly and the condition improves spontaneously with aging. Loose anagen hair can be associated with other anomalies, such as coloboma.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:690632:          \"val\" : \"A congenital malformation of the external ear, seen more frequently in males, that occurs sporadically or is inherited, that is characterized by unilateral (79-93% of cases, 60% of which involve the right ear) or bilateral small and abnormally shaped auricles and that is often associated with atresia or stenosis of the ear canal, attention deficit disorders and delayed language development. The variation in auricle size ranges from grade I, where the auricle is simply smaller than normal, to grade IV, also known as anotia, where there is a complete absence of the external ear and of the auditory canal.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:701634:          \"val\" : \"A rare, congenital malformation syndrome characterized by the association of anterior ocular chamber cleavage disorder with developmental delay, short stature and congenital hypothyroidism. Additional manifestations include cerebellar hypoplasia, tracheal stenosis, narrow external auditory meatus, and hip dislocation. There have been no further description in the literature since 1995.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:718961:          \"val\" : \"Limb-mammary syndrome (LMS) is a rare disease belonging to the group of ectodermal dysplasias.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:750037:          \"val\" : \"Inflammation of the nasal mucous membranes caused by an IgE-mediated response to external allergens. The inflammation may also involve the mucous membranes of the sinuses, eyes, middle ear, and pharynx. Symptoms include sneezing, nasal congestion, rhinorrhea, and itching. It may lead to fatigue, drowsiness, and malaise thus causing impairment of the quality of life.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:751574:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia and scoliosis\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:751586:          \"val\" : \"ophthalmoplegia, progressive external, and scoliosis\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:760802:          \"val\" : \"anophthalmia clinical with micrognathia malformed ears digital anomalies and abnormal external genitalia\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:760806:          \"val\" : \"anophthalmia, clinical, with micrognathia, malformed ears, digital anomalies, and abnormal external genitalia\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:774002:      \"lbl\" : \"lateral semicircular canal malformation, familial, with external and middle ear abnormalities\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:774007:          \"val\" : \"lateral semicircular canal malformation, familial, with external and middle ear abnormalities\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:774021:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/lateral_semicircular_canal_malformation_familial_with_external_and_middle_ear_abnormalities\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:774024:          \"val\" : \"https://rarediseases.info.nih.gov/diseases/10067/lateral-semicircular-canal-malformation-familial-with-external-and-middle-ear-abnormalities\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:780913:      \"lbl\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant 2\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:780917:          \"val\" : \"Any progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the SLC25A4 gene.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:780923:          \"val\" : \"SLC25A4 progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:780927:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions caused by mutation in SLC25A4\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:780931:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant 2\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:780935:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant type 2\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:780944:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia, autosomal dominant 2\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:780961:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/progressive_external_ophthalmoplegia_with_mitochondrial_dna_deletions_autosomal_dominant_2\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:781132:      \"lbl\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant 3\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:781136:          \"val\" : \"Any progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the TWNK gene.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:781142:          \"val\" : \"TWNK progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:781146:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions caused by mutation in TWNK\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:781150:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant 3\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:781154:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant type 3\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:781163:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia, autosomal dominant 3\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:781180:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/progressive_external_ophthalmoplegia_with_mitochondrial_dna_deletions_autosomal_dominant_3\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:785495:          \"val\" : \"external ophthalmoplegia with synergistic divergence\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:785498:          \"val\" : \"external ophthalmoplegia, synergistic divergence, jaw winking, and oculocutaneous hypopigmentation\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:792391:      \"lbl\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant 4\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:792395:          \"val\" : \"Any progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the POLG2 gene.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:792401:          \"val\" : \"POLG2 progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:792405:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions caused by mutation in POLG2\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:792409:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant 4\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:792413:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant type 4\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:792422:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia, autosomal dominant 4\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:792439:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/progressive_external_ophthalmoplegia_with_mitochondrial_dna_deletions_autosomal_dominant_4\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:818601:          \"val\" : \"Oculoauricular syndrome, Schorderet type is a rare, genetic developmental defect during embryogenesis characterized by various ophthalmic anomalies (including congenital microphthalmia, microcornea, cataract, anterior segment dysgenesis, ocular coloboma and early onset rod-cone dystrophy), and abnormal external ears (low-set pinna with crumpled helix, narrow intertragic incisure, abnormal bridge connecting the crus of the helix and the anthelix, narrow external acoustic meatus, and lobule aplasia).\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:818619:          \"val\" : \"microphthalmia, microcornea, anterior segment dysgenesis, cataract, ocular coloboma, retinal pigment epithelium abnormalities, Rod-cone dystrophy, and anomalies of the external Ear\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:839867:      \"lbl\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant 5\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:839871:          \"val\" : \"Any progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the RRM2B gene.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:839877:          \"val\" : \"RRM2B progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:839881:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions caused by mutation in RRM2B\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:839885:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant 5\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:839889:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant type 5\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:839898:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia, autosomal dominant 5\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:839915:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/progressive_external_ophthalmoplegia_with_mitochondrial_dna_deletions_autosomal_dominant_5\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:859277:          \"val\" : \"A rare, genetic, developmental defect during embryogenesis disorder characterized by severe, early-onset, salt-wasting adrenal insufficiency and ambiguous/female external genitalia (irrespective of chromosomal sex) due to mutations in the <i>CYP11A1</i> gene. Milder cases may present delayed onset of adrenal gland dysfunction and genitalia phenotype may range from normal male to female in individuals with 46,XY karyotype. Imaging studies reveal hypoplastic/absent adrenal glands and biochemical findings include low serum cortisol, mineralocorticoids, androgens, and sodium, with elevated potassium levels.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:900715:          \"val\" : \"Progressive external ophthalmoplegia-myopathy-emaciation syndrome is a rare mitochondrial oxidative phosphorylation disorder due to nuclear DNA anomalies characterized by progressive external ophthalmoplegia without diplopia, cerebellar atrophy, proximal skeletal muscle weakness with generalized muscle wasting, profound emaciation, respiratory failure, spinal deformity and facial muscle weakness (manifesting with ptosis, dysphonia, dysphagia and nasal speech). Intellectual disability, gastrointestinal symptoms (e.g. nausea, abdominal fullness, and loss of appetite), dilated cardiomyopathy and renal colic have also been reported.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:900754:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia-myopathy-emaciation syndrome\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:902093:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant type 6\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:902102:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant 6\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:902106:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia, autosomal dominant 6\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:902123:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/progressive_external_ophthalmoplegia_with_mitochondrial_dna_deletions_autosomal_dominant_6_2\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:913010:          \"val\" : \"Syndromic microphthalmia-12 is a rare disease characterized by bilateral small eyeballs (microphthalmia), lungs that are too small (pulmonary hypoplasia), and a defect or hole in the diaphragm that allows the abdominal contents to move into the chest cavity (diaphragmatic hernia). Other symptoms may include: Severe global developmental delay with progressive motor impairment due to spasticity and/or uncontrolled repetitive muscular contractions (dystonia), with or without abnormal quick movements that resemble dancing (chorea), Defects of the cerebellum (Chiari type I malformation) Accumulation of cerebrospinal fluid inside the brain (hydrocephaly), Severe feeding difficulties, Mild facial dysmorphism with broad nasal root and tip, and a very small chin (micrognathia), Severe language delay, Wheelchair-bound. Syndromic microphthalmia-12 is caused by mutations in the RARB gene. There is no specific treatment for this syndrome.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:941230:      \"lbl\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal recessive 2\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:941234:          \"val\" : \"Any progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the RNASEH1 gene.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:941240:          \"val\" : \"RNASEH1 progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:941244:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions caused by mutation in RNASEH1\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:941248:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal recessive 2\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:941252:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal recessive type 2\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:941261:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia, autosomal recessive 2\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:941276:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/progressive_external_ophthalmoplegia_with_mitochondrial_dna_deletions_autosomal_recessive_2\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:945328:          \"val\" : \"Autosomal dominant optic atrophy plus syndrome (ADOA plus) is a variant of autosomal dominant optic atrophy (ADOA) associating the typical optic atrophy with other extra-ocular manifestations such as sensorineural deafness, myopathy, chronic progressive external ophthalmoplegia, ataxia and peripheral neuropathy. More rarely, other manifestations have been associated with this condition, such as spastic paraplegia, multiple-sclerosis like illness.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:956484:      \"lbl\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal recessive 3\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:956488:          \"val\" : \"Any autosomal recessive progressive external ophthalmoplegia in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the TK2 gene.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:956499:          \"val\" : \"TK2 autosomal recessive progressive external ophthalmoplegia\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:956503:          \"val\" : \"autosomal recessive progressive external ophthalmoplegia caused by mutation in TK2\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:956507:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal recessive 3\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:956511:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal recessive 3; PEOB3\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:956514:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal recessive type 3\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:956518:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia, autosomal recessive 3\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:956533:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/progressive_external_ophthalmoplegia_with_mitochondrial_dna_deletions_autosomal_recessive_3\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:956550:      \"lbl\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal recessive 4\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:956554:          \"val\" : \"An extremely rare multiple mitochondrial DNA deletion syndrome with markedly decreased deoxyguanosine kinase (DGUOK) activity in skeletal muscle characterized by a highly variable phenotype. Clinical manifestations include progressive external ophthalmoplegia, mitochondrial myopathy, recurrent rhabdomyolysis, lower motor neuron disease, mild cognitive impairment, sensory axonal neuropathy, optic atrophy, ataxia, hypogonadism and/or parkinsonism.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:956573:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal recessive 4\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:956577:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal recessive type 4\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:956581:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia, autosomal recessive 4\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:956600:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/progressive_external_ophthalmoplegia_with_mitochondrial_dna_deletions_autosomal_recessive_4\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:971374:      \"lbl\" : \"obsolete rare disease involving intestinal motility\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:973918:          \"val\" : \"Arachnodactyly-intellectual disability-dysmorphism syndrome is characterized by moderate intellectual deficit, brachycephaly, typical facies (thin lips and microstomia), ectomorphic habitus with extremely long, thin fingers and toes, and hypoplastic external genitalia. It has been described in three patients.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:974011:          \"val\" : \"Arrhinia is an extremely rare, major congenital malformation consisting of an absence of the nose ranging from hyporrhinia (absence of external nasal structures) to total arrhinia (absence of external nose, nasal airways, olfactory bulbs, or olfactory nerve) often causing respiratory distress and requiring surgical correction. Arrhinia can be bilateral or unilateral (hemiarrhinia). Associated anomalies include ocular features (hypertelorism, microphthalmia, eyelid coloboma), facial clefts, midline defects and microtia.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:977174:          \"val\" : \"Maternally inherited cardiomyopathy and hearing loss is a mitochondrial disease described in two unrelated families to date that has a heterogeneous clinical presentation characterized by the association of progressive sensorineural hearing loss with hypertrophic cardiomyopathy and, in the majority of cases, encephalomyopathy symptoms such as ataxia, slurred speech, progressive external opthalmoparesis (PEO), muscle weakness, myalgia, and exercise intolerance.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:978950:      \"lbl\" : \"obsolete rare disease with Pierre Robin syndrome\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:982167:      \"lbl\" : \"obsolete external auditory canal aplasia/hypoplasia\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:982173:          \"val\" : \"external auditory canal stenosis/atresia\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:982200:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/external_auditory_canal_aplasia_hypoplasia\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:982428:          \"val\" : \"Proboscis lateralis (PL) is a rare congenital facial abnormality characterized by failed development of the external nose on one side that is replaced by a tubular structure composed of skin and soft tissue usually attached at the inner canthus of the eye and therefore often associated with maldevelopment of the nasal cavity or paranasal sinuses of the affected side. PL is also associated with other craniofacial abnormalities such as orbital anomalies, cleft lip/palate, frontal encephalocele and holoprosencephaly.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:988511:      \"lbl\" : \"obsolete pinnae and external auditory canal anomaly\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:988520:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/pinnae_and_external_auditory_canal_anomaly\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:991839:          \"val\" : \"Isolated congenital auditory ossicle malformation is a rare, congential, middle ear anomaly characterized by, usually unilateral and sporadic, variations in the number, size and/or configuration of the ossicles, with no tympanic membrane and external ear abnormalities and no history of trauma or infection. Patients frequently present late, after schooling has started, with non- progressive, conductive hearing loss often associated with speech delay and poor school performance.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:991845:          \"val\" : \"congenital auditory ossicle malformation without external ear abnormality\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:996419:      \"lbl\" : \"obsolete rare disease with dentinogenesis imperfecta\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1004897:          \"val\" : \"Complete septate uterus is a rare, non-syndromic uterovaginal malformation characterized by a uterus that has a longitudinal septum which elongates from the uterine fundus to the internal or external cervical os. Most often women are asymptomatic, however dysmenorrhoea, unilateral obstruction, and endometriosis could be observed. Unlike urinary tract abnormalities, which are very rarely associated, poor reproductive outcome is frequent.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1006400:      \"lbl\" : \"obsolete rare disease with autism\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1009435:          \"val\" : \"Axial mesodermal dysplasia spectrum is a rare developmental defect during embryogenesis syndrome characterized by congenital manifestations of both oculo-auriculo-vertebral spectrum and caudal regression sequence. Phenotype is highly variable but patients typically present facial dysmorphism (incl. asymmetry, hypertelorism), auricular abnormalities (e.g. preauricular tags, microtia, absence of middle ear ossicles), skeletal malformations (hemivertebrae, hip dislocation, sacral agenesis/dysplasia, talipes equinovarus, flexion deformity of lower limbs), cardiac defects (dextrocardia, septal defects), renal and genitourinary anomalies (such as renal agensis/dysplasia, abnormal external genitalia, cryptorchidia), as well as anal anomalies such as anal atresia and rectovesical fistula.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1009500:          \"val\" : \"OBSOLETE. Polymalformative genetic syndrome with increased risk of developing cancer (PGSIRC) comprises a wide range of syndromes characterized by congenital malformations with a high risk of developing tumors including up to 50 different rare diseases.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1020075:          \"val\" : \"OPCA with macular Degeneration and external ophthalmoplegia\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1022087:          \"val\" : \"Pulmonary fibrosis - hepatic hyperplasia - bone marrow hypoplasia, also named Btrimorphic syndromeB (i.e. three (inherited) morbidities, pulmonary, hepatic and cytopenia), is a rare disease reported in 4 cases to date, manifesting with idiopathic pulmonary fibrosis, hepatic nodular regenerative hyperplasia leading to portal hypertension and thrombocytopenia due to bone marrow hypoplasia. The condition was associated with 100% mortality.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1026646:          \"val\" : \"A rare, genetically highly heterogeneous otorhinolaryngologic disease, resulting from inner and/or middle ear or hearing nerve anomalies, typically characterized by bilateral, severe to profound hearing loss (mean sensorineural hearing impairment of 60 dB or more for 500-, 1,000-, and 2,000-Hz frequency tones in the better ear) which occurs before the onset of speech development and is not associated with visible external ear abnormalities or any other medical problems. It is usually nonprogressive and impedes oral language acquisition.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1026691:          \"val\" : \"Postlingual non-syndromic genetic deafness is a rare, genetically highly heterogeneous otorhinolaryngologic disease, resulting from inner and/or middle ear or hearing nerve anomalies, typically characterized by progressive, bilateral, moderate to profound hearing loss (mean sensorineural hearing impairment equal to 40 dB or more for 500-, 1,000-, and 2,000-Hz frequency tones in the better ear) which occurs after the onset of speech development and is not associated with visible external ear abnormalities or any other medical problems. Language development is not initially significantly delayed.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1026733:          \"val\" : \"A central nervous system malformation syndrome characterized by holoprosencephaly with microcephaly, abnormal eye morphology (hypotelorism, cyclopia, exophthalmos), nasal anomalies (single nostril or absent nose), and cleft lip/palate, combined with signs of caudal regression (sacral agenesis, sirenomelia with absent external genitalia).\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1029517:          \"val\" : \"OBSOLETE. Rare hereditary hemochromatosis comprises the rare forms of hereditary hemochromatosis (HH), a group of diseases characterized by excessive tissue iron deposition. These rare forms are hemochromatosis type 2 (juvenile), type 3 (TFR2-related), and type 4 (ferroportin disease). Hemochromatosis type 1 (also called classic hemochromatosis) is not a rare disease.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1034561:          \"val\" : \"Isotretinoin embryopathy is an association of malformations caused by the teratogenic effect of isotretinoin, an oral synthetic vitamin A derivative, which is used to treat severe recalcitrant cystic acne. Exposure to isotretinoin during the first trimester of pregnancy has been associated with an increased risk of spontaneous abortions and severe birth defects including serious craniofacial (microcephaly, asymmetric crying facies, microphthalmia, developmental abnormalities of the external ear, ocular hypertelorism), cardio vascular (conotruncal heart defects, aortic arch abnormalities), and central nervous system (hydrocephalus, microcephaly, lissencephaly, Dandy-Walker malformation, cognitive deficit) anomalies and thymic aplasia. Isoretinoin is contraindicated during pregnancy.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1040467:          \"val\" : \"OBSOLETE. Mitochondrial oxidative phosphorylation disorder due to nuclear DNA anomalies is a group of clinically heterogeneous diseases, commonly defined by lack of cellular energy due to defects of oxidative phosphorylation (OXPHOS), resulting from pathogenic mutations in the nuclear DNA. Mitochondrial oxidative phosphorylation disorder due to nuclear DNA anomalies includes diseases classified according to defects in: genes encoding structural components of OXPHOS complexes (such as Leigh syndrome, coenzyme Q10 deficiency); genes encoding assembly factors of OXPHOS complexes (such as GRACILE syndrome); genes altering the stability of mitochondrial DNA (such as autosomal dominant progressive external ophthalmoplegia, mitochondrial DNA depletion syndrome); mitochondrial protein synthesis.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1052254:          \"val\" : \"Mitochondrial DNA depletion syndrome, encephalomyopathic form is a group of mitochondrial DNA maintenance syndrome diseases characterized by predominantly neuromuscular manifestations with typically infantile onset of hypotonia, lactic acidosis, psychomotor delay, progressive hyperkinetic-dystonic movement disorders, external ophtalmoplegia, sensosineural hearing loss, generalized seizures and variable renal tubular dysfunction. It may be associated with a broad range of other clinical features.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1052700:          \"val\" : \"A rare, mitochondrial DNA maintenance syndrome characterized by cerebellar ataxia, sensory peripheral neuropathy, myoclonus, epilepsy, progressive cognitive impairment, late-onset ptosis and external ophthalmoplegia. Liver failure may also occur, most often in association with the use of antiepileptic drug sodium valproate.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1052754:      \"lbl\" : \"autosomal recessive progressive external ophthalmoplegia\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1052758:          \"val\" : \"Autosomal recessive form of progressive external ophthalmoplegia.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1052768:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia, autosomal recessive\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1052784:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/autosomal_recessive_progressive_external_ophthalmoplegia\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1069857:          \"val\" : \"Machado-Joseph disease type 2 is a subtype of Machado-Joseph disease (SCA3/MJD) with intermediate severity characterized by an intermediate age of onset, cerebellar ataxia and external progressive ophthalmoplegia, with variable pyramidal and extrapyramidal signs.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1075661:          \"val\" : \"Infantile glycerol kinase deficiency (GKD) is a severe form of GKD characterized clinically by poor feeding, failure to thrive, salt-wasting dehydration, vomiting, Addisonian pigmentation, hypotonia, and disorders of consciousness. Some patients have complex GKD associated with adrenal hypoplasia congenita and/or Duchenne muscular dystrophy (DMD) with manifestations including intellectual deficit, dysmorphic facial features, abnormal external genitalia, strabismus, seizures, and progressive lethargy.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1076363:      \"lbl\" : \"obsolete rare disease with thoracic aortic aneurysm and aortic dissection\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1077723:          \"val\" : \"Inherited isolated adrenal insufficiency due to partial CYP11A1 deficiency is a rare, genetic, chronic, primary adrenal insufficiency disorder, due to partial loss-of-function CYP11A1 mutations, characterized by early-onset adrenal insufficiency without associated abnormal external male genitalia. Patients present with signs of adrenal crisis, including electrolite abnormalities, severe weakness, recurrent vomiting and seizures. Ultrasound reveals absent (or very small) adrenal glands.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1080600:          \"val\" : \"A rare disease caused by compression of the celiac axis by an abnormally shaped arcuate ligament (the part of the diaphragm in which both pillars join in the midline around the aorta). Patients have recurrent abdominal pain, anorexia and weight loss. The pain is epigastric, and diarrhea or constipation may be present as well. Onset of pain will usually, although not always, be after food intake, and may be associated with nausea and emesis. Other symptoms may include lassitude, exercise intolerance and vomiting. Occasionally, a patient may show an abdominal murmur upon auscultation.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1088036:          \"val\" : \"A syndrome characterized by the association of gastrointestinal dysmotility, peripheral neuropathy, chronic progressive external ophthalmoplegia and leukoencephalopathy.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1088146:          \"val\" : \"Conditions affecting individuals with 46,XX karyotype characterized by atypical development of one or more of the following: the gonads, the internal reproductive structures, the external reproductive/genital structures.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1091815:      \"lbl\" : \"obsolete rare disease with myoclonus as a major feature\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1098816:          \"val\" : \"A rare multiple congenital anomalies syndrome characterized by mild to severe intellectual disability, a distinctive facial gestalt (blepharophimosis, maxillary hypoplasia, telecanthus, microtia and atresia of the external auditory meatus) as well as skeletal and articular abnormalities (e.g. camptodactyly of the fingers, cutaneous syndactyly, talipes equinovarus, flexion contractures of the proximal interphalangeal joints, hip or elbow subluxation, joint laxity). Affected individuals also present neonatal hypotonia, variable respiratory manifestations, chronic feeding difficulties and gray matter heterotopia.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1099168:          \"val\" : \"rare disease with Cushing syndrome as a major feature\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1100085:          \"val\" : \"The salt wasting form of classic congenital adrenal hyperplasia due to 21-hydroxylase deficiency (classical 21 OHD CAH) is characterized by virilization of the external genitalia in females, hypocortisolism, precocious pseudopuberty and renal salt loss due to aldosterone deficiency.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1100120:          \"val\" : \"The simple virilizing form of classical congenital adrenal hyperplasia due to 21-hydroxylase deficiency (classical 21 OHD CAH) is characterized by genital ambiguity and virilization of the external genitalia in females, hypocortisolism and precocious pseudopuberty without salt-wasting.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1105967:      \"lbl\" : \"obsolete non-familial rare disease with dilated cardiomyopathy\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1108096:      \"lbl\" : \"adult-onset chronic progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial myopathy\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1108100:          \"val\" : \"Adult-onset chronic progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial myopathy is a rare mitochondrial disease characterized by adult onset of progressive external ophthalmoplegia, exercise intolerance, muscle weakness, manifestations of spinocerebellar ataxia (e.g. impaired gait, dysarthria) and mild motor peripheral neuropathy. Respiratory insufficiency has been reported in some cases.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1119411:      \"lbl\" : \"childhood-onset autosomal recessive myopathy with external ophthalmoplegia\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1119415:          \"val\" : \"A rare, genetic, non-dystrophic myopathy disease characterized by childhood-onset severe external ophthalmoplegia, typically without ptosis, associated with mild, very slowly progressive muscular weakness and atrophy, involving the facial, neck flexor and limb (upper > lower, proximal > distal) muscles. Muscle biopsy shows type 1 fiber uniformity, absent, or abnormally small, type 2A fibers, increased variability of fiber size, internalized nuclei and/or fatty infiltration.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1119433:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/childhood_onset_autosomal_recessive_myopathy_with_external_ophthalmoplegia\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1144110:      \"lbl\" : \"obsolete rare disease with malignant hyperthermia\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1160438:      \"lbl\" : \"maternally-inherited progressive external ophthalmoplegia\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1160448:          \"val\" : \"maternally-inherited chronic progressive external ophthalmoplegia\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1160461:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/mitochondrial_dna_related_progressive_external_ophthalmoplegia\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1162507:        \"comments\" : [ \"Note that the ordo class is specifically for rare diseases, but we broaden to be inclusive of HH1\" ],\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1168436:          \"val\" : \"Androgen insensitivity syndrome (AIS) is a disorder of sex development (DSD) characterized by the presence of female external genitalia, ambiguous genitalia or variable defects in virilization in a 46,XY individual with absent or partial responsiveness to age-appropriate levels of androgens. It comprises two clinical subgroups: complete AIS (CAIS) and partial AIS (PAIS).\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1168569:          \"val\" : \"A condition in males that affects sexual development. It is characterized by underdevelopment of the Leydig cells, which are cells in the testes that secrete male sex hormones (androgens) and are important for male sexual development. Individuals with LCH have a typical male genetic make-up (46, XY), but due to lowered levels of androgens, may have a range of genital (reproductive organ) differences. Individuals with LCH may have a small penis (micropenis),the opening of the urethra may be located on the underside of the penis (hypospadias), or the scrotum may be divided into two halves (bifid scrotum). Given these differences in development, the external genitalia may not appear clearly male or female (ambiguous genitalia). Some individuals with LCH can have female external genitalia and small testes that have not descended and are located in the pelvis, abdomen, or groin. This may be referred to as type 1, whereas less severe cases might be called type 2. LCH is inherited in an autosomal recessive manner and is caused by mutations in the LHCGR gene.Although there is no specific treatment or cure for LCH, there may be ways to manage the symptoms. A team of doctors or specialists is often needed to figure out the treatment options for each person.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1170253:          \"val\" : \"The association of auricular abnormalities and cleft lip with or without cleft palate has been described in two siblings. One sibling had postauricular pits, profound myopia, nystagmus and retinal pigment abnormalities. The second sibling was a fetus (gestational age: 23 weeks) with severe cleft lip, cleft palate and external ear abnormalities.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1171439:          \"val\" : \"A rare genetic neuromuscular disease characterized by early onset of proximal or generalized muscle weakness, external ophthalmoplegia with or without ptosis, and joint contractures. Hypotonia, neonatal respiratory distress necessitating ventilation, and severe dysphagia have also been reported. The disease is of variable severity and non- or slowly progressive. Patients typically remain ambulatory. Muscle biopsy may show predominance of type 1 fibers, marked variability in fiber size, increased internal nuclei, and proliferation of perimysial and endomysial connective tissue.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1172252:          \"val\" : \"Bickerstaff's brainstem encephalitis (BBE) is a rare post-infectious neurological disease characterized by the association of external ophthalmoplegia, ataxia, lower limb arreflexia, extensor plantar response and disturbance of consciousness (drowsiness, stupor or coma).\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1182244:      \"lbl\" : \"macrostomia-preauricular tags-external ophthalmoplegia syndrome\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1182248:          \"val\" : \"Macrostomia-preauricular tags-external ophthalmoplegia syndrome combines macrostomia or abnormal mouth contour, preauricular tags, uni- or bilateral ptosis and external ophthalmoplegia. It was described in nine members of a Brazilian family. It is a new phenotype belonging to the so-called oculoauriculovertebral spectrum, resulting from a branchial arch anomaly. Transmission is autosomal dominant.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1182263:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/macrostomia_preauricular_tags_external_ophthalmoplegia_syndrome\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1182299:          \"val\" : \"perineal hemangioma-external genitalia malformations-lipomyelomeningocele-vesicorenal abnormalities-imperforate anus syndrome\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1195049:          \"val\" : \"OBSOLETE. 46,XY disorder of sex development due to isolated 17,20-lyase deficiency is a rare disorder of sex development due to reduced 17,20-lyase activity that affects individuals with 46,XY karyotype and is characterized by ambiguous external genitalia, including micropenis, perineal hypospadias, bifid scrotum, cryptorchidism, and a blind vaginal pouch. Blood pressure and electrolytes are normal whilst hormonal investigations show normal basal and stimulated levels of cortisol, and low basal and stimulated androgen levels.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1195099:          \"val\" : \"OBSOLETE. Primary lipodystrophies represent a heterogeneous group of very rare diseases characterized by a generalized or localized loss of body fat (lipoatrophy).\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1203605:          \"val\" : \"A congenital malformation of the external ear and the most extreme form of microtia characterized by the complete absence of the external ear and auditory canal, conductive hearing loss, attention deficit disorders and delayed language development.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1213803:          \"val\" : \"Robinow syndrome (RS) is a rare genetic syndrome characterized by limb shortening and abnormalities of the head, face and external genitalia.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1215199:      \"lbl\" : \"obsolete rare disease with odontological manifestation\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1215724:          \"val\" : \"rare disease of cellular proliferation\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1221169:      \"lbl\" : \"obsolete malposition of external canthus\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1222927:      \"lbl\" : \"obsolete rare disease with glaucoma as a major feature\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1243789:          \"val\" : \"Hearing loss caused by impaired transmission of signals from the external auditory canal or middle ear to the cochlea.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1250328:          \"val\" : \"The result of pathological changes in the hard tissue of a tooth caused by carious lesions, mechanical factors, or trauma, which render the pulp susceptible to bacterial invasion from the external environment.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1251198:      \"lbl\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal recessive 5\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1251209:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal recessive 5\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1251213:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia, autosomal recessive 5\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1251229:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/progressive_external_ophthalmoplegia_with_mitochondrial_dna_deletions_autosomal_recessive_5\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1253127:          \"val\" : \"Hemochromatosis type 1 (classic) is the most common form of hereditary hemochromatosis (HH), a group of diseases characterized by excessive tissue iron deposition. Due to its incidence (1/200-1/1000), it is not considered as a rare disease, unlike the other subforms of the disease\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1254361:          \"val\" : \"Complete androgen insensitivity syndrome (CAIS) is a form of androgen insensitivity syndrome (AIS), a disorder of sex development (DSD), characterized by the presence of female external genitalia in a 46,XY individual with normal testis development but undescended testes and unresponsiveness to age-appropriate levels of androgens.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1261409:        \"comments\" : [ \"This term was created for characterizing a disease via axiom. We do not maintain axioms to indicate that a disease is rare/not-rare. Please use the Mondo rare disease subset to identify rare diseases. (https://mondo.readthedocs.io/en/latest/editors-guide/rare-disease-subset/)\" ],\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1261427:        \"comments\" : [ \"This term was created for characterizing a disease via axiom. We do not maintain axioms to indicate that a disease is rare/not-rare. Please use the Mondo rare disease subset to identify rare diseases. (https://mondo.readthedocs.io/en/latest/editors-guide/rare-disease-subset/)\" ],\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1261442:        \"comments\" : [ \"This term was created for characterizing a disease via axiom. We do not maintain axioms to indicate that a disease is rare/not-rare. Please use the Mondo rare disease subset to identify rare diseases. (https://mondo.readthedocs.io/en/latest/editors-guide/rare-disease-subset/)\" ],\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1263115:          \"val\" : \"Damage inflicted on the body as the direct or indirect result of an external force, with or without disruption of structural continuity.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1264180:      \"lbl\" : \"obsolete rare disease\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1264189:          \"val\" : \"rare disease\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1264193:          \"val\" : \"rare disease or disorder\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1264197:          \"val\" : \"rare diseases\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1266499:      \"lbl\" : \"external ear neoplasm\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1266503:          \"val\" : \"A neoplasm (disease) that involves the external ear.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1266508:          \"val\" : \"external Ear tumor\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1266513:          \"val\" : \"external Ear tumour\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1266516:          \"val\" : \"external ear neoplasm (disease)\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1266520:          \"val\" : \"external ear tumor\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1266525:          \"val\" : \"external ear tumour\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1266528:          \"val\" : \"neoplasm of external Ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1266532:          \"val\" : \"neoplasm of external ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1266536:          \"val\" : \"neoplasm of the external Ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1266540:          \"val\" : \"tumor of external Ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1266544:          \"val\" : \"tumor of external ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1266548:          \"val\" : \"tumor of the external Ear\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1266553:          \"val\" : \"tumour of external Ear\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1266557:          \"val\" : \"tumour of external ear\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1266561:          \"val\" : \"tumour of the external Ear\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1275215:      \"lbl\" : \"polyp of external auditory canal\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1275219:          \"val\" : \"A polyp that involves the external acoustic meatus.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1275224:          \"val\" : \"external Ear polyp\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1275228:          \"val\" : \"external acoustic meatus polyp\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1275232:          \"val\" : \"external auditory canal polyp\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1275236:          \"val\" : \"polyp of the external auditory canal\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1287695:          \"val\" : \"A viral or bacterial infection that affects the external, middle, or inner ear. It may follow an upper respiratory infection. Signs and symptoms include pain, ear discharge, ear fullness, hearing loss, vertigo, nausea, and vomiting.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1296205:        \"comments\" : [ \"This term was found in the globalgenes.org rare disease list, but no information could be found about it.\" ],\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1296363:        \"comments\" : [ \"This term was found in the globalgenes.org rare disease list, but no information could be found about it.\" ],\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1305125:        \"comments\" : [ \"This term was found in the globalgenes.org rare disease list, but no information could be found about it.\" ],\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1314132:      \"lbl\" : \"external hirudiniasis\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1314137:          \"xrefs\" : [ \"https://medical-dictionary.thefreedictionary.com/external+hirudiniasis\" ]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1316532:          \"val\" : \"A circadian sleep disorder in which the individual's internal body clock is delayed with respect to the external day/night cycle.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1316727:          \"val\" : \"A circadian sleep disorder that occurs when work schedules force people to be awake when their circadian rhythms dictate that they should be sleeping. It is classified as a Circadian Rhythm Disorder (CRD) and is extrinsic, i.e. caused by external behavioral factors.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1321332:      \"lbl\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant 1\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1321336:          \"val\" : \"Any autosomal dominant progressive external ophthalmoplegia in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the POLG gene.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1321347:          \"val\" : \"POLG autosomal dominant progressive external ophthalmoplegia\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1321351:          \"val\" : \"autosomal dominant progressive external ophthalmoplegia caused by mutation in POLG\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1321355:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal dominant 1\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1321359:          \"val\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia, autosomal dominant 1\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1341370:      \"lbl\" : \"obsolete rare disease with Cushing syndrome as a major feature\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1356448:      \"lbl\" : \"ophthalmoplegia, external, with rib and vertebral anomalies\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1356468:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/ophthalmoplegia_external_with_rib_and_vertebral_anomalies\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1386795:          \"val\" : \"Choanal atresia-athelia-hypothyroidism-delayed puberty-short stature syndrome is an autosomal dominant disorder characterized by choanal atresia, athelia or hypoplastic nipples, branchial sinus abnormalities, neck pits, lacrimal duct anomalies, hearing loss, external ear malformations, and thyroid abnormalities.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1407145:          \"val\" : \"Penetrating and non-penetrating injuries to the spinal cord resulting from traumatic external forces (e.g., WOUNDS, GUNSHOT; WHIPLASH INJURIES; etc.).\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1407829:          \"val\" : \"Harm or hurt to the ankle or ankle joint usually inflicted by an external source.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1417264:      \"lbl\" : \"X-linked external auditory canal atresia-dilated internal auditory canal-facial dysmorphism syndrome\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1445716:          \"val\" : \"46,XX testicular disorder of sex development (46,XX testicular DSD) is characterized by male external genitalia, ranging from normal to ambiguous with associated testosterone deficiency.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1461796:          \"val\" : \"An anterior midline defect with variable expression involving the infraumbilical abdominal wall including the pelvis, urinary tract, and external genitalia.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1462124:          \"val\" : \"An abscess contained between the internal and external anal sphincters.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1466908:          \"val\" : \"A central nervous system dysperception disorder characterized by the perception of a sound not justified by any internal or external vibration, lasting at least 5 minutes and occurring more than once a week, arising from maladaptive neuroplasticity secondary to an organic cochlear peripheral lesion, and classifiable as positive auditory hallucinosis in the absence of delusional attitudes or behaviors.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1468831:          \"val\" : \"A rare disease due to a severely impaired central autonomic control of breathing and dysfunction of the autonomous nervous system. The incidence is estimated to be at 1 of 200 000 livebirths. A heterozygous mutation of PHOX-2B gene is found in 90% of the patients. Association with a Hirschsprung's disease is observed in 16% of the cases. Despite a high mortality rate and a lifelong dependence to mechanical ventilation, the long-term outcome of CCHS should be ultimately improved by multidisciplinary and coordinated follow-up of the patients.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1471331:          \"val\" : \"A botryomycosis that involves internal organs such as lungs, liver, or brain. It is a rare disease and has been described mainly in patients with underlying diseases such as diabetes mellitus, cystic fibrosis, or HIV infection. It is most commonly affecting the lungs, although involvement of other organs including liver, spleen, kidney, and brain has also been described.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1482910:          \"val\" : \"A myopathy that is characterized by muscle breakdown (rhabdomyolysis), heat and exertion-related muscle pain (myalgia) and cramping symptoms, severe muscle pain, sudden elevation and subsequent fall of serum creatine phosphokinase levels and products of muscle breakdown in the urine (myoglobinuria). Associated with RYR1 variations. Rhabdomyolysis is associated with a range of external triggers, including strenuous exercise beyond the limit of fatigue, heat stress, illicit drug or alcohol abuse, use of supplements or certain medications, recent viral illness or muscle trauma.\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1500760:      \"lbl\" : \"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial dna deletions, autosomal recessive 6\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1500775:          \"val\" : \"https://www.malacards.org/card/progressive_external_ophthalmoplegia_with_mitochondrial_dna_deletions_autosomal_recessive_6\"\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1528626:      \"lbl\" : \"Synonym to be removed from public release but maintained in edit version as record of external usage\",\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1528683:        \"comments\" : [ \"DOID rare disease subset\" ]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1528701:        \"comments\" : [ \"GARD rare disease subset\" ]\nsrc/ontology/subsets/mondo-clingen.json:1528743:        \"comments\" : [ \"inferred rare disease subset\" ]\n","exit_code":2,"status":"failed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' docs/editors-guide/update-external-sources.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' docs/editors-guide/update-external-sources.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Update external sources\n\n**Note:** this documentation is outdated and will be updated soon.\n\n## Update OMIM\n\n1. run ingest: https://ci.monarchinitiative.org/job/build-omim/ note: right now only a few people can actually run this and it is likely to be replaced by the new ingest being developed by Dazhi soon. For the moment, ping Nico to run this ingest. Before continuing to step 2, make sure that the run has completed by checking that the last run in the [build history](https://ci.monarchinitiative.org/job/build-omim/) is green. \n2. In terminal: `cd src/ontology`\n3. In terminal: `sh run.sh make omim_slurp -B`\n4. If successful this command will create two files: mondo/src/ontology/tmp/ps_slurp_omim.obo and mondo/src/ontology/tmp/rest_slurp_omim.obo\n5. Add all the classes from the slurped files to mondo-edit.obo. (Use a text editor, rathe than Protege). \n6. If ps_slurp_omim.obo is not empty, go back to step 3 and run the slurp again until the ps_slurp_omim.obo is empty\n\n## Update ORDO\n\n1. In Finder/atom, go to src/ontology/sources/orphanet/Makefile\n1. Change V=`3.2` to whatever version is the latest. To find the latest version, go to http://www.orphadata.org/, scroll down, search for Ontologies and click on section about ORDO.\n1. In terminal: `cd src/ontology`\n1. In terminal: `sh run.sh make ordo_slurp -B`\n1. If successful this command will create two files: mondo/src/ontology/tmp/ps_slurp_ordo.obo and mondo/src/ontology/tmp/rest_slurp_ordo.obo. Note: ps_slurp_ordo.obo should always be empty\n1. Add all the classes from the slurped files to mondo-edit.obo \n\n## Notes about adding new classes to mondo\n1. Add the new classes via the mondo-edit.obo text file (ie Open mondo-edit.obo in Atom and copy and paste the text into the end of the mondo-edit.obo text file.)\n1. Before copying and pasting the new terms into the text file, the terms should be reviewed and edited as described below.\n\n### Review new OMIM terms \n1. Check Mondo to ensure the term does not already exist (ie the term was already added from another source).\n1. If the term already exists in Mondo, add the OMIM ID as a dbxref, and add MONDO:equivalentTo.\n1. Add any synonyms from OMIM (if they don't already exist), or add OMIM as a dbxref to any existing synonyms, as applicable.\n1. Terms in the OMIM slurp include RELATED synonyms in the format TERM IN ALL CAPS; ABBREVIATION, for example: `synonym: \"MEGACYSTIS-MICROCOLON-INTESTINAL HYPOPERISTALSIS SYNDROME 2; MMIHS2\" RELATED  [OMIM:619351]`. \n1. For these cases, we do not want to duplicate the label in the synonym, so delete the duplicate label.\n1. In almost all cases, the synonym should be EXACT.\n1. Mark the abbreviation with ABBREVIATION \nFor example: `synonym: \"MMIHS2\" RELATED ABBREVIATION [OMIM:619351]`\n\n### Review new Orphanet terms \n1. Check Mondo to ensure the term does not already exist (ie the term was already added from another source like OMIM or NCIT).\n1. If the term already exists in Mondo, add the Orphanet ID as a dbxref, and add MONDO:equivalentTo.\n1. Add any synonyms from Orphanet (if they don't already exist), or add Orphanet as a dbxref to any existing synonyms, as applicable.\n1. Check the capitalization of the synonyms and revise accordingly. All synonyms should lowercase unless they are proper names or abbreviations.\n1. Add abbreviation tags to synonyms where applicable.\n1. Fix annotations to 'narrow to broad term' or 'broad to narrow term'. The format should be changed as shown in the example below:\n- **Original:**\nxref: `ICD10:D21.9 {source=\"Orphanet:595133\"} {source=\"NTBT (ORPHA code's Narrower Term maps to a Broader Term)\"}` \n- **Fixed:**\nxref: `ICD10:D21.9 {source=\"Orphanet:595133\", source=\"Orphanet:595133/ntbt\"}`\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
